+<header><div><div class="brand"><b>F</b> FRONTIER <span style="color:#566572"> / </span> GEOMETRY LAB</div><div class="sub">Spatial detail, not whole-object swaps</div></div><span class="tag">INTERACTIVE · ORIGINAL EDUCATIONAL DEMO</span></header>
+<main><section class="stage"><canvas id="scene" aria-label="Interactive adaptive sphere mesh; drag to orbit, scroll to change camera distance"></canvas><div class="stagehead"><div><div class="eyebrow">01 / CLUSTER-LOCAL DETAIL</div><h1>A different LOD on every patch.</h1><p>Move closer. Watch local detail respond to projected error—not just the object's distance.</p></div></div><div class="badge" id="policy">72 patches · shared boundaries stitched</div><div class="hud"><strong id="triangles">—</strong><small>SELECTED TRIANGLES · ENTIRE SHELL</small><strong id="reduction">—</strong><small>FEWER THAN FIXED MAX DETAIL</small><strong id="visible">—</strong><small>DRAWN TRIANGLES · THIS VIEW</small></div><div class="legend"><div class="eyebrow">PATCH RESOLUTION</div><div><i class="dot" style="background:#9b8ad8"></i>1 × 1 · coarse</div><div><i class="dot" style="background:#739bc8"></i>2 × 2</div><div><i class="dot" style="background:#5fcab1"></i>4 × 4</div><div><i class="dot" style="background:#efd489"></i>8 × 8 · fine</div></div><div class="modebar" role="group" aria-label="Display mode"><button class="active" data-mode="clusters">Clusters</button><button data-mode="shaded">Surface</button><button data-mode="wire">Wireframe</button></div><div class="hint">DRAG TO ORBIT &nbsp;·&nbsp; SCROLL TO DOLLY &nbsp;·&nbsp; <span id="build">—</span> <span id="seamstatus"></span></div></section>
+<aside><h2>Detail controller</h2><div class="row"><button class="active" id="adaptive">Adaptive</button><button id="fixed">Fixed maximum</button></div><label class="range" for="distance">LOD camera distance <output id="distanceValue"></output></label><input id="distance" type="range" min="2.2" max="16" step=".1" value="4.5"><label class="range" for="error">Screen error target <output id="errorValue"></output></label><input id="error" type="range" min=".3" max="8" step=".1" value="1.8"><p class="small">Lower error asks for more triangles. This demo uses a parametric error heuristic, not an offline QEM hierarchy.</p><label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="observer">Observer view · see the LOD camera</label><div class="divider"></div><h2>Surface-aware detail</h2><label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="normals" checked>Normal-variation LOD weighting</label><label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="normalmap">Normal-map-style shading detail</label><p class="small">Shading normals alone do not create triangles or change the silhouette.</p><label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="uv" checked>Show locked UV island boundaries</label><label class="range" for="height">Procedural height displacement <output id="heightValue"></output></label><input id="height" type="range" min="0" max=".18" step=".01" value=".03"><div class="divider"></div><div class="row"><button class="active" id="opaque">Opaque</button><button id="glass">Glass shell</button></div><label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="safe" checked>Lock full shell for transmission</label><div class="note" id="explain">Opaque backfaces can be culled from this view. They must remain available to reflection and shadow rays.</div><button id="reset" style="margin-top:18px;width:100%">Reset experiment</button></aside></main>
+<div class="foot"><article><h3><span>01</span>Local selection</h3><p>72 parametric patches independently choose a subdivision level. Real triangle counts come from the generated mesh, not a drawn overlay.</p></article><article><h3><span>02</span>Boundary agreement</h3><p>Neighboring patches share edge samples and stitch different levels. UV island boundaries remain fixed; this is not a general UV-aware simplifier.</p></article><article><h3><span>03</span>Transmission policy</h3><p>Glass-safe mode keeps the entire closed shell at maximum detail. Transparency here is illustrative—not a physically traced refraction test.</p></article></div>
