+# FrontierEngine — Engine Test Level (Lobby/Garage + Proving Grounds)
+
+Cleaned-up copy of the vehicle HMI demo for engine testing. This folder is the
+**Lobby + Proving Grounds only** test level — no other levels.
+
+| Area | What it is | Where |
+|---|---|---|
+| **Lobby (Garage / Hangar)** | The Garage/Hangar workshop area: hangar walls + roof, tool cabinets, tyre stacks, lamp strips, forecourt apron. The in-world "lobby" — spawn, Garage tablet, vehicle workshop. | `Source/LevelStructure.js` — `HangarPanel` / `HangarAccent` / `HangarRoof`, `ArenaZones` entry `Garage` at `[34.0, 20.0]` |
+| **Proving Grounds** | The driving course: main straight + start grid, skidpad ring, jump ramp, smash alley (breakables), tunnel, east training grounds, slalom. | `Source/LevelStructure.js` — `ResolveLevelPlacements`, `ResolveConePlacements`, `ResolveBreakables`, `EmitLevelGroundFacets`, `TrainingDrills` |
+
+## Provenance & cleanup
+
+- **Requested source:** `https://github.com/egoistm1inbox/Frontier/tree/arena/d96da802-frontier`
+  (fetched as `refs/remotes/egoist/arena/d96da802-frontier`, tip `8916354`).
+  That branch's `Experimental/VehicleProvingGrounds` (221 files) ships **four**
+  levels via `LevelCatalog`: `dday` (D-Day Assault), `inversion` (Inversion
+  Arena), `city` (City Pursuit & AI Lab), `proving` (Proving Grounds). It was
+  born with all four — there is no simpler pre-levels history on that branch.
+- **Simpler version used instead (per owner choice):** the proving-only tree
+  already on this repo's HEAD at
+  `Experimental/SlateReference/A/Exhibits/VehicleProvingGrounds` (157 files,
+  no `LevelCatalog`, no D-Day/City/Inversion/RoadStudio files). That tree was
+  copied verbatim into this folder (`Experimental/FrontierEngine/`) and
+  renamed to the generic engine name. No level-stripping edits were needed —
+  the copy is already Lobby (Garage/Hangar) + Proving Grounds only.
+- **Removed vs. the egoist branch (not copied):** `DDayStructure.js`,
+  `DDayBattleSequence.js`, `CityPursuitStructure.js`, `PolicePursuitSequence.js`,
+  `InversionArenaStructure.js`, `RoadStudio/` + `RoadStudioAdapter.js`,
+  `RoadEditorSequence.js`, `RoadStudio.html`, `CollapseSequence.js`,
+  `BollardSequence.js`, `DrivingHudSequence.js`, `HudAudio.js`,
+  `RampSurfaceProjection.js`, `ServiceStationSequence.js`, `TramSequence.js`,
+  `TrafficLightSequence.js`, `SignageBuilder.js`, `ServiceAudio.js`,
+  `CameraMotionBlur.js`, plus their Tools tests/hooks. The `PlumeVorticity.wgsl`
+  file is kept — the "city" substring match is `vorti**city**`, not a level.
+- **Kept verbatim:** `index.html`, `Source/` (69 JS modules), `Shader/` (57 WGSL),
+  `Style/` (FrontierEditor.css + DM Sans), `Archive/` (3 `.facet` + codec),
+  `Tools/` (proving-only tests + Dawn harness), `PLAN.md`, `SLATE_PORT.md`.
+  Only the package name, page title/comment, and this README header were
+  changed for the rename.
+
+## Run
+
+```sh
+cd Experimental/FrontierEngine
+npm ci            # installs pinned jolt-physics 1.1.0
+python3 Tools/Serve.py   # http://localhost:8080/  (WebGPU needs Chrome/Edge)
+npm test          # node --test Tools/*.test.mjs
+```
+
+---
+
+# Vehicle Proving Grounds — JavaScript/WebGPU + Jolt WebAssembly (original upstream README, kept for reference)
+
+Landed in Slate as `Exhibits/VehicleProvingGrounds` from
+`streamlinkinbox/Frontier`, branch `arena/85b411ac-frontier` (`dfc92a0`).
+That tree was reconstructed from `Experimental/01a141bc-a4a3-72ce-8295-398724231feb.patch`
+on `SultanAladin/Frontier-`, supplied branch `arena/9440f4d0-frontier`.
+The source patch is not retained. Vehicle `.facet` binaries were regenerated with
+`Archive/FacetArchiveCodec.py` from the four authored geometry archives on
+`arena/4f07c82a-frontier`; omitted DM Sans fonts come from `@fontsource/dm-sans@5.3.0`
+under the included OFL license. The separate reference configurator is preserved
+in `../interactive-vehicle-hmi-configurator`.
+
+## Local renderer work (Slate branch `arena/b55d93c0-slate`)
+
+Three renderer fixes landed on top of the import, all default-off or behaviour-preserving:
+
+- **Real cluster binning.** The analytic lights (batwing street lamps, low/high/fog beams,
+  roof flood) are binned per frame into a 16×16×4 world-space grid; each shaded point
+  evaluates only its cell. The curves are hand-tuned beam profiles, not measured IES data,
+  and nothing here calls them that anymore.
+- **Triangle-traced reflections** (inspector → Exposure & image, or `?triangles=1`). The
+  reflection ray walks a two-level triangle hierarchy (TLAS + binned-SAH BLAS) instead of
+  the SDF. Off, the SDF path runs exactly as before.
+- **Screen traces** (inspector → Global illumination · ReSTIR, or `?screentraces=1`). A
+  nearest-depth pyramid walk settles gather and reflection rays on screen before the SDF
+  takes over; the recombination writes the diffuse exitance the next frame reads back.
+  Off, the pyramid dispatch and the exitance store are both skipped, and every touched
+  path runs exactly as before. While on, the derez glow rests (its attribute channel
+  carries the occupant identity the exitance rule needs).
+
+The Frame timing card has a **Copy timing log** button: one text block with quality,
+extents, every cost-relevant toggle and every pass duration including the zeroes, for
+pasting into a stays/goes review. The console always gets the log too.
+
+## Added Garage functionality
+
+The cockpit/dashboard, steering wheel, integrated hexagonal cluster and centre tablet
+now follow **Slate `3c987f3`**, not the old binnacle design. HUD scale/position controls
+resize only the on-screen diagnostic HUD; the physical interior and seated camera do
+not move. See [SLATE_PORT.md](SLATE_PORT.md) for provenance and integration scope.
+
+Open the tablet's **Garage**. Paint, gloss/matte and rim controls update the shared
+GPU materials on the **actual driven car**, mirrors and live preview. Click to apply,
+or drag a paint swatch onto the preview's body / rim material onto a rim. Drops are
+ray-tested against the car's actual facets: background and wrong-material drops are
+rejected. Drag elsewhere in the preview to orbit. Cycle **Solid → Ghost → Wireframe
+→ Scan**; Scan sweeps an animated plane across the mesh. Inspection modes affect only
+the studio preview, not world-car opacity or physics. These are native WebGPU
+implementations of the requested interactions, not a Three.js embed or an exact
+copy of the configurator's animated ripple transition.
+
+Tyre smoke uses the actual Slate plume transport, source projection and march shaders.
+Loose rigid bodies now run **Jolt Physics 1.1.0 in browser JavaScript/WebAssembly**;
+custom suspension/tyre/drivetrain physics are deliberately retained and connected via
+a collision-impulse chassis bridge. No native C++ build is required.
+
+See [PLAN.md](PLAN.md) for earlier physics/VFX changes.
+
+## Rim, spark and HMI usability corrections
+
+- Shredding removes only rubber. The rim preserves Project Drive's two authored face slots: 1,296 dark faces and
+  272 blue emissive accent faces. The dark finish has its own RimBase identity so
+  shredding cannot remove it. Both parts remain visible in shadows/mirrors/Garage.
+  Garage rim-finish changes affect the accent slot only, not the black base.
+- Spark width is bounded to 0.65–1.35 render pixels with a tighter core, preserving
+  motion streaks without large close-up particle billboards.
+- Press **M** to toggle **HMI** focus / cockpit, or choose **HMI** in the camera selector
+  (also available via C). The HMI camera faces and frames the tablet for touch at any
+  viewport aspect ratio. Scroll to zoom in HMI, cockpit or passenger view.
+- **Cabin · HMI → Tablet / HMI size (not cluster)** scales just the tablet (0.75–2.5×),
+  including housing, screen and touch region. Cluster, wheel, dashboard and seated
+  eyes are unchanged. The HMI focus camera reframes the enlarged tablet automatically.
+  **Reset HMI size / zoom** restores tablet scale, focus distance and cockpit FOV.
+  Diagnostic **HUD scale** remains a separate control.
+
+## Display colour and material dragging
+
+Open **Garage** on the tablet to drag paint, gloss/matte finishes or rim finishes
+onto the live car preview. A material chip follows your pointer/finger, including
+over the GPU-rendered preview. The turntable pauses during dragging. Release on the
+matching body/rim surface to apply to the actual car; background/wrong-surface drops
+cancel. **Blue accents** restores the original blue metallic/emissive accent slot.
+
+The screen is now display-referred/antiglare rather than HDR sky-reflective glass,
+so scene exposure no longer bleaches its authored colours. Both brightness controls
+reach zero correctly; set the in-tablet and inspector brightness to 100% / 1 for
+normal viewing. Scene emission strength does not boost the UI.
+
+## Materials garden: mirror, metals and glass
+
+North of the start straight sit four reference pieces: a standing mirror panel, an
+aluminium sphere, a gold sphere and a glass sphere. The metals are full-metal
+records in measured linear-space F0 colours with a roughness ladder from
+mirror-smooth (0.02) to softly brushed (0.12), so the GGX lobe spread reads at a
+glance. The glass sphere splits each reflection ray Schlick-against-Snell: a
+reflected leg plus one refracted leg resumed past the far side, with grazing
+angles going fully reflective. One index drives both halves — the authored F0 is
+converted from the IOR, and the shader inverts that exact mapping — so the Fresnel
+strength and the bend can never disagree. **Exposure & image → Garden glass IOR**
+(1.0–2.5) re-authors the record live, from air to dense glass.
+
+This is a single-refraction approximation, not a full dielectric: the exit bend
+is skipped, there is no absorption tint, and the diffuse gather still treats the
+sphere as opaque, so what you see through it is the traced leg only. The car's
+own glass keeps its long-standing opaque look.
+
+## Checks
+
+```sh
+# From Exhibits/VehicleProvingGrounds:
+npm ci
+npm --prefix Tools ci
+npm test
+npm --prefix Tools run test:stability
+npm --prefix Tools run validate
+npm --prefix Tools run validate:effects
+npm --prefix Tools run validate:slate
+npm --prefix Tools run validate:garden
+```
+
+Dawn's null backend checks shader/pipeline/command validity, not rendered pixels.
+Use a WebGPU-capable browser to assess appearance, interaction and hardware performance.
+
+---
+
+# IlluminationHost — distance-field GI · surface cards · ReSTIR GI (WebGPU)
+
+A self-contained WebGPU exhibit inside the **Frontier Editor** UI: one scene distance field (four camera-centred
+toroidal cascades), a surface cache of oriented cards with multi-bounce radiosity, a ReSTIR GI final gather traced
+through that field, SVGF reconstruction, glossy reflections — and the Project-Drive ControlVehicle (a port of its
+struts, MF6.1 tyres and GT-R powertrain) on the **Frontier proving grounds** and its **training arena** (timed
+drills, 136 knockable cones), with GPU drift smoke and tyre fire, burnouts that lay sharp-edged rubber, breakable
+props whose debris are convex rigid bodies in the distance field, and a derez / rez effect for every respawn.
+
+**Provenance.** Imported verbatim from `SultanAladin/Slate`, branch `arena/c6cba543-slate`, commit
+`e7c4ea47` ("Add WebGPU distance-field GI exhibit: one scene distance field, surface cards, ReSTIR GI,
+ControlVehicle"). The later screen-trace commit `194ce3aa` is deliberately not included. Everything after the
+import in this folder was developed here. The editor look comes from `Experimental/FrontierEditor` (tokens in
