@@ -0,0 +1,138 @@
+# Slate cockpit/smoke and browser Jolt integration
+
+## Reference and provenance
+
+Requested source: https://github.com/unassignedinbox/Slate/commit/3c987f33c71c2477bd73ca29c69d5bd0ee484d1a,
+`Experimental/IlluminationHost`.
+
+- `CabinLayout.js` → `Source/SlateCabinLayout.js`: reference placements, dimensions,
+  camera eyes and dashboard/seat geometry; imported by the host's cabin adapter.
+- `CabinProjection.js` → `Source/SlateCabinFittings.js`: grip/spokes, hexagonal
+  cluster shell and tablet shell geometry, remapped to host material families.
+- `Source/PlumeSpace.js`, `Source/PlumeSourceProjection.js` and
+  `Shader/Plume{Records,Advection,Pressure,Vorticity,March}.wgsl`: copied from the
+  reference. The five shaders remain byte-identical. Host-side telemetry/preset
+  adaptation lives in `SmokeSequence.js`; composition is integrated into the
+  existing display pipeline before TAA.
+- The host's tablet applications, real-car material updates, glass and mirrors are
+  retained. The hexagonal screen is mounted on and rotates with the wheel.
+- New WebGPU scan and CPU-ray-tested material dragging implement the requested HMI
+  functionality natively. This is not an embedded Three.js configurator or its exact
+  scan/ripple transition. Paint drops target body-coat facets; rim drops target hub
+  facets. Click controls remain available. Material drops only target the Garage
+  preview, then update the shared driven-car materials—not arbitrary scene objects.
+
+## Jolt is the browser backend—not native C++
+
+Pinned dependency: `jolt-physics@1.1.0`, upstream https://github.com/jrouwe/JoltPhysics.js.
+Its npm package includes Jolt's MIT licence. Install with `npm ci` in this directory;
+`node_modules` is intentionally not committed. The local `wasm-compat` JavaScript
+entry point embeds its WASM payload, so there is no CDN, C++ compiler, native server,
+SharedArrayBuffer or cross-origin-isolation requirement. Serve the whole prototype
+folder, including installed `node_modules`.
+
+`JoltWorld.js` owns a single-threaded Jolt world, fixed 120 Hz physics (maximum twelve
+steps per frame), convex hull bodies, mass/inertia, friction/restitution, sleeping,
+CCD, static ground/kerbs/ramp/collider boxes, obstacle rebuilds, resets and cleanup.
+It synchronizes real Jolt poses back to the existing lighting/fracture/cone systems.
+The contact metric reports Jolt added/persisted manifold callbacks during the frame,
+not invented zeroes or a unique-point count.
+
+**Scope:** custom vehicle drivetrain, suspension, MF tyres, thermals and terrain
+contact solving remain. A dynamic Jolt chassis proxy exchanges collision-induced
+linear/angular velocity with that solver for loose-body collisions. It does not
+apply Jolt gravity/ground contacts or copy Jolt chassis position back, avoiding
+second chassis integration. `RigidBodyWorld` is inherited for body metadata,
+convex planes, tyre-support queries and support-load bookkeeping; its JavaScript
+contact integrator is not used for the Jolt runtime. This is a hybrid vehicle
+integration, not a claim that the entire vehicle is Jolt's VehicleConstraint.
+
+## HUD sizing correction
+
+Cabin/HMI geometry and seated eyes stay at their authored physical scale. The old
+cockpit scale/offset UI/query is removed. Cabin · HMI instead controls the diagnostic
+HUD's CSS scale and x/y offset, anchored top-left. The touch plane remains aligned
+with the fixed reference tablet.
+
+## Verification
+
+Run the commands in README.md after installing both prototype and Tools packages.
+Tests cover reference wheel/tablet poses, cluster attachment, touch picking, fixed
+physical cabin under HUD edits, ray/material drops, four inspection modes, tyre
+emission direction/release, plume retirement, actual WASM body settling/sleep/reset,
+fast wall collision and chassis collision feedback, plus the earlier VFX tests.
+
+Dawn null-backend runs cover idle startup, active effects and active plume
+source/transport/march/composition with the new cockpit camera. They validate WGSL,
+GPU layouts and submitted commands, **not pixels or physical GPU performance**.
+A real WebGPU-browser review of appearance, driving feel and pointer interaction
+is still required; no browser screenshot/rendered visual review is claimed.
+
+Recorded results for this integration: **20/20 tests pass**, all **23 stability
+scenarios pass**, and Dawn startup **12 frames**, effects **36 frames** and active
+plume/cockpit **48 frames** each complete with **0 errors / 0 warnings**.
+
+## Follow-up: rim classification and usable HMI focus
+
+The metal rim archive contains 1,296 incorrectly rubber-labelled facets and 272
+hub-labelled facets. `ProjectWheelFacets` now remaps the rim archive's rubber labels
+to Hub, without changing the separate 3,968 rubber tyre facets. Both mirrored sides
+retain their complete metal rims after shredding. Default Hub shading is neutral alloy.
+
+Tablet-only scaling uses a dedicated housing material and a shared GPU placement
+function for deferred/forward/shadow and screen-overlay paths. The same centre and
+scale drive CPU touch picking. Cluster, wheel and cockpit geometry do not scale.
+HMI focus uses the scaled screen's plane, aspect and up axis to frame it with padding;
+M toggles focus/cockpit, and scrolling adjusts focus distance or cockpit FOV. Pointer
+cancellation and touch-action handling protect touchscreen interaction.
+
+The existing baked distance field/surface-card geometry remains authored-size (as
+with the animated wheel); the tablet sizing control changes raster/screen/touch
+placement, not the underlying GI bake. Large scales may overlap nearby cabin fittings.
+
+New regression tests cover both actual rim archives, tablet-scale touch alignment,
+record encoding, portrait/landscape framing and the bounded spark footprint.
+**24/24 tests pass**; the 48-frame active integration also exercises scaled HMI and
+cockpit cameras. This remains command/shader validation, not rendered visual review.
+
+## Follow-up: display colour, material dragging and blue rims
+
+Restored the authored blue metallic/emissive rim finish as the default, keeping the
+corrected complete-rim geometry. Garage now offers a blue-glow rim chip as well as
+alloy/dark rims. Paint, gloss/matte and rim finishes can all be dragged; the chip
+follows the finger/pointer over the GPU preview, the turntable pauses during the
+drag, and material-matched facet picking still gates application to the driven car.
+
+The washed-out display came from treating the canvas UI as HDR emissive glass:
+sky reflection could remain even at brightness zero, and the final scene exposure
+and filmic curve changed authored colours. The antiglare screen now reconstructs
+radiance from desired linear display colour using the inverse of the final ACES
+fit and the exposure buffer. Window glass/mirror reflections are unchanged. The
+panel and inspector brightness controls multiply once (0 means black); canvas
+brightness is no longer baked into the cabin texture. Standalone canvas use keeps
+its own brightness overlay. Screens no longer use the scene's emission multiplier.
+
+27 tests pass, including brightness-zero, exposure/colour round trips and dragging
+blue emissive rims/matte finishes. Effects (36 frames) and scaled-HMI/plume (48
+frames) Dawn checks pass with no errors/warnings. Real-browser visual review is
+still required.
+
+## Correction: preserve the original two-material rim
+
+Rechecked Project Drive on `SultanAladin/Frontier-`, branch
+`arena/4f07c82a-frontier`: `EngineContent/GeometryArchives/ControlWheelStructure.inl`
+explicitly records **MatTyre: 1296, MatHub: 272**. `DriveSceneAuthor.cpp` gives the
+first slot its authored dark finish (linear 0.03741, roughness 0.76087) and calls
+MatHub “Material.024 — rim mag accent”, a blue tinted metal with 0.12 emissive lift.
+
+The earlier interpretation of those 1,296 labels as an authoring mistake was wrong;
+they are intentional dark faces, not additional blue faces. The runtime now maps
+ONLY those metal-archive MatTyre faces to a dedicated `RimBase` material carrying
+that same dark finish. The 272 marked blue faces stay Hub, triangle-for-triangle.
+Actual tyre rubber remains Tyre. Thus both rim slots survive shredding without
+turning the entire rim blue. Garage finish changes only affect the accent slot;
+drops are accepted on either rim slot. Both mirrored wheels are regression-tested
+against each original triangle's material assignment.
+
+Validation: 31 tests pass; populated effects/shredded-wheel Dawn validation completes
+36 frames with no errors/warnings. No new rendered browser review is claimed.
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/AtmosphereScattering.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/AtmosphereScattering.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..09adfcd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/AtmosphereScattering.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,122 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                        ATMOSPHERESCATTERING.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 Single-scattering quadrature of a Rayleigh, Mie and ozone atmosphere into the sky-view radiance texture.
+
+// 📝 Constants are Bruneton/Hillaire's Earth: R_g 6360 km, R_t 6460 km, Rayleigh scale height 8 km, Mie 1.2 km with
+//    g = 0.8, an ozone tent at 25 km. The observer stands at ObserverAltitude. The texture is recomputed only when
+//    the light moves; every escaped ray in the exhibit reads it through SampleSkyRadiance.
+
+//! include "SkyProjection.wgsl"
+
+struct AtmosphereRecord
+{
+    SunDirection     : vec3f,   // [-]  unit, toward the sun
+    SolarIlluminance : f32,     // [-]  top-of-atmosphere illuminance scale
+    ObserverAltitude : f32,     // [m]
+    Pad0             : f32,
+    Pad1             : f32,
+    Pad2             : f32,
+}
+
+@group(0) @binding(0) var<uniform> Atmosphere : AtmosphereRecord;
+@group(0) @binding(1) var SkyViewTarget       : texture_storage_2d<rgba16float, write>;
+
+const GroundRadius      : f32   = 6360000.0;                                  // [m]
+const AtmosphereRadius  : f32   = 6460000.0;                                  // [m]
+const RayleighScatter   : vec3f = vec3f(5.802e-6, 13.558e-6, 33.1e-6);       // [1/m]
+const RayleighHeight    : f32   = 8000.0;                                     // [m]
+const MieScatter        : f32   = 3.996e-6;                                   // [1/m]
+const MieExtinction     : f32   = 4.40e-6;                                    // [1/m]
+const MieHeight         : f32   = 1200.0;                                     // [m]
+const MieAsymmetry      : f32   = 0.8;                                        // [-]
+const OzoneAbsorption   : vec3f = vec3f(0.650e-6, 1.881e-6, 0.085e-6);       // [1/m]
+const ViewSamples       : u32   = 40u;
+const LightSamples      : u32   = 12u;
+
+// 📐 Ray–sphere intersection about the planet centre; returns (near, far), far < 0 when the sphere is missed.
+fn IntersectSphere(Origin: vec3f, Direction: vec3f, Radius: f32) -> vec2f
+{
+    let b = dot(Origin, Direction);
+    let c = dot(Origin, Origin) - Radius * Radius;
+    let Discriminant = b * b - c;
+    if (Discriminant < 0.0)
+    {
+        return vec2f(-1.0, -1.0);
+    }
+    let Root = sqrt(Discriminant);
+    return vec2f(-b - Root, -b + Root);
+}
+
+fn ResolveDensities(Altitude: f32) -> vec3f
+{
+    let Ozone = max(0.0, 1.0 - abs(Altitude - 25000.0) / 15000.0);
+    return vec3f(exp(-Altitude / RayleighHeight), exp(-Altitude / MieHeight), Ozone);
+}
+
+fn ResolveExtinction(Densities: vec3f) -> vec3f
+{
+    return RayleighScatter * Densities.x + vec3f(MieExtinction * Densities.y) + OzoneAbsorption * Densities.z;
+}
+
+fn ResolveSunTransmittance(Position: vec3f) -> vec3f
+{
+    if (IntersectSphere(Position, Atmosphere.SunDirection, GroundRadius).x > 0.0)
+    {
+        return vec3f(0.0);
+    }
+    let Exit = IntersectSphere(Position, Atmosphere.SunDirection, AtmosphereRadius).y;
+    let Step = Exit / f32(LightSamples);
+    var Depth = vec3f(0.0);
+    for (var Sample = 0u; Sample < LightSamples; Sample++)
+    {
+        let Point = Position + Atmosphere.SunDirection * ((f32(Sample) + 0.5) * Step);
+        Depth += ResolveExtinction(ResolveDensities(length(Point) - GroundRadius)) * Step;
+    }
+    return exp(-Depth);
+}
+
+@compute @workgroup_size(8, 8)
+fn IntegrateSkyView(@builtin(global_invocation_id) Invocation: vec3u)
+{
+    let Extent = textureDimensions(SkyViewTarget);
+    if (any(Invocation.xy >= Extent))
+    {
+        return;
+    }
+    let Coordinates = (vec2f(Invocation.xy) + 0.5) / vec2f(Extent);
+    var Direction = ReconstructSkyDirection(Coordinates);
+    // 📝 Below the horizon the view is lifted onto it: the scene's own ground answers those rays first.
+    Direction.z = max(Direction.z, 0.0);
+    Direction = normalize(Direction + vec3f(0.0, 0.0, 1.0e-4));
+    let Origin = vec3f(0.0, 0.0, GroundRadius + Atmosphere.ObserverAltitude);
+
+    let Ground = IntersectSphere(Origin, Direction, GroundRadius);
+    var Travel = IntersectSphere(Origin, Direction, AtmosphereRadius).y;
+    if (Ground.x > 0.0)
+    {
+        Travel = Ground.x;
+    }
+    let Step = Travel / f32(ViewSamples);
+    let Cosine = dot(Direction, Atmosphere.SunDirection);
+    let RayleighPhase = 3.0 / (16.0 * 3.14159265358979) * (1.0 + Cosine * Cosine);
+    let g2 = MieAsymmetry * MieAsymmetry;
+    let MiePhase = 3.0 / (8.0 * 3.14159265358979) * ((1.0 - g2) * (1.0 + Cosine * Cosine))
+                 / ((2.0 + g2) * pow(1.0 + g2 - 2.0 * MieAsymmetry * Cosine, 1.5));
+
+    var Transmittance = vec3f(1.0);
+    var Radiance = vec3f(0.0);
+    for (var Sample = 0u; Sample < ViewSamples; Sample++)
+    {
+        let Point = Origin + Direction * ((f32(Sample) + 0.5) * Step);
+        let Densities = ResolveDensities(length(Point) - GroundRadius);
+        let Extinction = ResolveExtinction(Densities);
+        let Scattering = RayleighScatter * Densities.x * RayleighPhase + vec3f(MieScatter * Densities.y * MiePhase);
+        let SegmentTransmittance = exp(-Extinction * Step);
+        // 📐 Energy-conserving segment integral: ∫ T(s)·S ds = S·(1 − T_seg)/σ_t, times the transmittance so far.
+        let Integral = (vec3f(1.0) - SegmentTransmittance) / max(Extinction, vec3f(1.0e-12));
+        Radiance += Transmittance * Scattering * ResolveSunTransmittance(Point) * Integral;
+        Transmittance *= SegmentTransmittance;
+    }
+    textureStore(SkyViewTarget, vec2i(Invocation.xy), vec4f(Radiance * Atmosphere.SolarIlluminance, 1.0));
+}
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/CabinOverlay.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/CabinOverlay.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8b9ec34
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/CabinOverlay.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,214 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                            CABINOVERLAY.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 What the deferred raster cannot carry: see-through glazing, the HMI's two screens and the mirrors' pictures, drawn over it.
+
+// 📝 Drawn into the recombined radiance before the temporal antialiasing, depth-tested (read only) against the opaque
+//    surface, premultiplied over what is there:
+//
+//    | Kind    | Geometry                                  | What it adds                                             |
+//    |---------|-------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------|
+//    | glass   | the body's glazing facets                 | the sky's Fresnel reflection and a sun glint; lets 70 %   |
+//    |         |                                           | of the cabin (or the world, from inside) through          |
+//    | tablet  | the centre-stack screen, 1.5 mm proud      | the TabletPanel launcher (its canvas), with the Garage's  |
+//    |         |                                           | live car composited into its preview well                |
+//    | cluster | the binnacle's hexagon                     | the TabletPanel cluster (its canvas, alpha to the outline)|
+//    | mirror  | each mirror's glass                        | the reflected view ForwardRaster rendered for it          |
+//
+//    The screens are self-lit (Luminance, in the scene's radiance units where sunlit white is about 5 — DriveCabin-
+//    Layout's 3 and 3.5), so they read the same in a dark cabin and at noon; their cover glass still reflects the sky.
+//    The derez mask applies here too: glass, screens and mirrors come apart with the car.
+
+//! include "FrameDescriptor.wgsl"
+//! include "SkyProjection.wgsl"
+//! include "EffectRecords.wgsl"
+//! include "VehicleVisual.wgsl"
+
+struct OverlayRecord
+{
+    Tablet   : vec4f,   // x luminance, y brightness [0, 1], z garage preview shown (1), w unused
+    Preview  : vec4f,   // xy top-left, zw bottom-right of the preview well in tablet UV
+    Corner   : vec4f,   // xy the well's corner radius in UV, z cluster luminance, w unused
+    Glass    : vec4f,   // x transmission at normal incidence, y mirror reflectance, z mirrors live (1), w unused
+}
+
+@group(0) @binding(1) var<storage, read> Occupants    : array<OccupantRecord>;
+@group(0) @binding(2) var<uniform> Overlay            : OverlayRecord;
+@group(0) @binding(3) var<uniform> Effect             : EffectRecord;
+@group(0) @binding(4) var<storage, read> VehicleState : VehicleRecord;
+@group(0) @binding(5) var TabletTexture               : texture_2d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(6) var ClusterTexture              : texture_2d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(7) var PreviewTexture              : texture_2d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(8) var MirrorTexture               : texture_2d_array<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(9) var LinearSampler               : sampler;
+@group(0) @binding(10) var SkyView                    : texture_2d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(11) var SkySampler                 : sampler;
+
+@group(0) @binding(12) var<storage, read> DisplayAdaptation : array<f32>;
+
+const KindGlass   : u32 = 0u;
+const KindTablet  : u32 = 1u;
+const KindCluster : u32 = 2u;
+const KindMirror  : u32 = 3u;
+
+struct OverlayVarying
+{
+    @builtin(position) Position             : vec4f,
+    @location(0) Normal                     : vec3f,
+    @location(1) Coordinates                : vec2f,
+    @location(2) WorldPosition              : vec3f,
+    @location(3) BodyLocal                  : vec3f,
+    @location(4) @interpolate(flat) Kind    : u32,
+    @location(5) @interpolate(flat) Layer   : u32,
+}
+
+@vertex
+fn OverlayVertex(@location(0) Position: vec3f, @location(1) Kind: u32, @location(2) Normal: vec3f, @location(3) Layer: f32,
+                 @location(4) Coordinates: vec2f) -> OverlayVarying
+{
+    let Body = Occupants[0];
+    // 📝 The two screens are cockpit fixtures: they scale and shift with it (the glazing and the mirrors stay with the
+    //    shell). Screens and mirrors sit 1.5 mm proud of their cover facets so they win the depth test against them.
+    var Placed = Position;
+    if (Kind == KindTablet) { Placed = PlaceTablet(Position); }
+    var TurnedNormal = Normal;
+    if (Kind == KindCluster) {
+        let Turned = TurnSteeringWheel(Position, Normal);
+        Placed = Turned.Position;
+        TurnedNormal = Turned.Normal;
+    }
+    let Lifted = Placed + TurnedNormal * select(0.0015, 0.0, Kind == KindGlass);
+    let World = Body.LocalToWorld * vec4f(Lifted, 1.0);
+    var Varying: OverlayVarying;
+    Varying.Position = Frame.ViewProjection * World;
+    Varying.Normal = (Body.LocalToWorld * vec4f(TurnedNormal, 0.0)).xyz;
+    Varying.Coordinates = Coordinates;
+    Varying.WorldPosition = World.xyz;
+    Varying.BodyLocal = Lifted;
+    Varying.Kind = Kind;
+    Varying.Layer = u32(Layer + 0.5);
+    return Varying;
+}
+
+fn ClassifyMasked(BodyLocal: vec3f) -> bool
+{
+    if (Effect.MaskMode == 0u)
+    {
+        return false;
+    }
+    if (Effect.MaskMode == 3u)
+    {
+        return true;
+    }
+    let Unit = (BodyLocal - Effect.BodyMinimum.xyz) / max(Effect.BodyMaximum.xyz - Effect.BodyMinimum.xyz, vec3f(1.0e-3));
+    let Elapsed = Effect.Clock - Effect.MaskStart;
+    let Seed = u32(Effect.Emitters[0].Centre.w);
+    if (Effect.MaskMode == 1u)
+    {
+        return Elapsed >= ResolveDerezRelease(Unit, Seed, Effect.Style, 1.0);
+    }
+    return Elapsed < ResolveRezArrival(Unit, Seed, Effect.Style, 1.0);
+}
+
+fn SampleSky(Direction: vec3f) -> vec3f
+{
+    return textureSampleLevel(SkyView, SkySampler, ProjectSkyCoordinates(Direction), 0.0).rgb * Frame.SkyScale + Frame.NightSkyRadiance;
+}
+
+// 📐 Rounded-rectangle coverage of the preview well in tablet UV (aspect-correct corner radii).
+fn ResolveWellCoverage(Coordinates: vec2f) -> f32
+{
+    let Low = Overlay.Preview.xy;
+    let High = Overlay.Preview.zw;
+    if (any(Coordinates < Low) || any(Coordinates > High))
+    {
+        return 0.0;
+    }
+    let Radius = Overlay.Corner.xy;
+    let Inner = clamp(Coordinates, Low + Radius, High - Radius);
+    let Offset = (Coordinates - Inner) / max(Radius, vec2f(1.0e-5));
+    return select(1.0, 0.0, dot(Offset, Offset) > 1.0);
+}
+
+@fragment
+fn OverlayFragment(Varying: OverlayVarying) -> @location(0) vec4f
+{
+    if (ClassifyMasked(Varying.BodyLocal))
+    {
+        discard;
+    }
+    let View = normalize(Frame.CameraPosition - Varying.WorldPosition);
+    var Normal = normalize(Varying.Normal);
+    if (dot(Normal, View) < 0.0)
+    {
+        Normal = -Normal;
+    }
+    let NdotV = clamp(dot(Normal, View), 0.0, 1.0);
+    let Fresnel = 0.04 + 0.96 * pow(1.0 - NdotV, 5.0);
+    let Reflected = reflect(-View, Normal);
+    var Reflection = SampleSky(Reflected) * Fresnel;
+    // 📝 A sun glint on the glass: a narrow lobe of the sun's illuminance.
+    let Glint = pow(max(dot(Reflected, Frame.SunDirection), 0.0), 900.0) * 60.0;
+    Reflection += Frame.SunIlluminance * (Glint * Fresnel);
+
+    if (Varying.Kind == KindGlass)
+    {
+        if (VehicleState.Cabin.y < 0.5)
+        {
+            discard;
+        }
+        let Transmission = Overlay.Glass.x * (1.0 - Fresnel);
+        return vec4f(Reflection, 1.0 - Transmission);
+    }
+    if (Varying.Kind == KindTablet)
+    {
+        var Picture = textureSampleLevel(TabletTexture, LinearSampler, Varying.Coordinates, 0.0).rgb;
+        if (Overlay.Tablet.z > 0.5)
+        {
+            var Well = ResolveWellCoverage(Varying.Coordinates);
+            if (Overlay.Tablet.w > 0.5) {
+                let P = abs((Varying.Coordinates - vec2f(Overlay.Corner.w, Overlay.Glass.w)) * vec2f(1200.0, 750.0));
+                let Q = P - vec2f(54.0, 13.0);
+                let Distance = length(max(Q, vec2f(0.0))) + min(max(Q.x,Q.y),0.0) - 12.0;
+                Well *= smoothstep(-1.0, 1.0, Distance);
+            }
+            if (Well > 0.0)
+            {
+                let Inside = (Varying.Coordinates - Overlay.Preview.xy) / max(Overlay.Preview.zw - Overlay.Preview.xy, vec2f(1.0e-5));
+                Picture = mix(Picture, textureSampleLevel(PreviewTexture, LinearSampler, Inside, 0.0).rgb, Well);
+            }
+        }
+        // An antiglare display is display-referred, not HDR sky-lit glass. Decode
+        // sRGB once at texture sampling; undo the final filmic/exposure transform
+        // so auto exposure cannot bleach the authored UI. Zero brightness is black.
+        return vec4f(ScreenRadiance(Picture * Overlay.Tablet.y), 1.0);
+    }
+    if (Varying.Kind == KindCluster)
+    {
+        let Texel = textureSampleLevel(ClusterTexture, LinearSampler, Varying.Coordinates, 0.0);
+        return vec4f(ScreenRadiance(Texel.rgb * Texel.a * Overlay.Tablet.y), 1.0);
+    }
+    // 📝 Mirror: in BVH ray-traced reflection mode when the raster mirror cameras are off, let the G-buffer's
+    //    multi-bounce ray-traced MirrorGlass reflection shine through instead of painting flat sky over it.
+    if (Overlay.Glass.z < 0.5 && FeatureEnabled(Frame, FeatureRayTracing) && FeatureEnabled(Frame, FeatureReflection)
+        && FeatureEnabled(Frame, FeatureRayTracedReflections))
+    {
+        discard;
+    }
+    var Mirrored = SampleSky(Reflected);
+    if (Overlay.Glass.z > 0.5)
+    {
+        Mirrored = textureSampleLevel(MirrorTexture, LinearSampler, Varying.Coordinates, Varying.Layer, 0.0).rgb;
+    }
+    return vec4f(Mirrored * Overlay.Glass.y, 1.0);
+}
+
+// Invert the same Narkowicz ACES fit used by DisplayPresent.wgsl.
+fn ScreenRadiance(LinearDisplay: vec3f) -> vec3f {
+    let Y = clamp(LinearDisplay, vec3f(0.0), vec3f(0.99));
+    let A = 2.51 - 2.43 * Y;
+    let B = 0.03 - 0.59 * Y;
+    let X = (-B + sqrt(B*B + 0.56*A*Y)) / (2.0*A);
+    let Exposure = select(1.0, DisplayAdaptation[0], DisplayAdaptation[0] > 0.0);
+    return X / Exposure;
+}
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/CabinVolume.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/CabinVolume.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..97b1a20
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/CabinVolume.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                             CABINVOLUME.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 How far a car-body-frame point lies inside the ControlVehicle's cabin: 1 deep inside, 0 outside, soft over 4 cm.
+
+// 📝 The car's shell is one facet thick — thinner than any distance-field voxel — and the cabin lies inside the body's
+//    own distance volume, so the traced indirect light there is the sunlit exterior's cards seen from within, and the
+//    cabin glowed brighter than the street. Lumen asks for thick walls and open interiors;
+//    here the cabin is known, so the light that cannot be traced is attenuated instead: two boxes, the greenhouse up
+//    to the headliner within the glass line and the lower tub forward to the footwells and back to the rear bench.
+//    The sun through the glazing is direct light (the shadow raster lets it in) and is never touched.
+
+fn ResolveBoxShare(Point: vec3f, Minimum: vec3f, Maximum: vec3f, Soft: f32) -> f32
+{
+    let Inside = min(Point - Minimum, Maximum - Point);
+    return clamp(min(min(Inside.x, Inside.y), Inside.z) / Soft, 0.0, 1.0);
+}
+
+fn ResolveCabinShare(BodyLocal: vec3f) -> f32
+{
+    let Greenhouse = ResolveBoxShare(BodyLocal, vec3f(-0.95, -1.04, -0.12), vec3f(1.33, 1.04, 1.19), 0.04);
+    let Tub = ResolveBoxShare(BodyLocal, vec3f(-1.85, -1.02, -0.12), vec3f(1.38, 1.02, 0.60), 0.04);
+    return max(Greenhouse, Tub);
+}
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/CardCapture.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/CardCapture.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..86aef1e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/CardCapture.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,63 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                             CARDCAPTURE.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 Orthographic capture of an occupant's facets into one card tile: diffuse albedo, local normal, emission, card depth.
+
+// 📝 Capture runs once per card at bring-up, in the occupant's own frame, so a moving occupant never recaptures —
+//    only its lighting is refreshed. The card index arrives as the instance index of the draw.
+
+//! include "CardProjection.wgsl"
+
+@group(0) @binding(0) var<storage, read> Cards     : array<CardRecord>;
+@group(0) @binding(1) var<storage, read> Occupants : array<OccupantRecord>;
+@group(0) @binding(2) var<storage, read> Materials : array<MaterialRecord>;
+
+struct CaptureVarying
+{
+    @builtin(position) Position             : vec4f,
+    @location(0) Normal                     : vec3f,
+    @location(1) @interpolate(flat) Family  : u32,
+    @location(2) @interpolate(flat) Card    : u32,
+}
+
+struct CaptureTargets
+{
+    @location(0) Albedo   : vec4f,
+    @location(1) Normal   : vec4f,
+    @location(2) Emission : vec4f,
+    @location(3) Depth    : vec4f,
+}
+
+@vertex
+fn CaptureVertex(@location(0) Position: vec3f, @location(1) Family: u32, @location(2) Normal: vec3f,
+                 @builtin(instance_index) CardIndex: u32) -> CaptureVarying
+{
+    let Card     = Cards[CardIndex];
+    let Occupant = Occupants[Card.Occupant];
+    let Coordinates = ProjectCardCoordinates(Card, Position);
+    var Varying: CaptureVarying;
+    Varying.Position = vec4f(Coordinates.x * 2.0 - 1.0, 1.0 - Coordinates.y * 2.0, Coordinates.z, 1.0);
+    Varying.Normal   = Normal;
+    Varying.Family   = select(Family, Occupant.MaterialOverride, Occupant.MaterialOverride != NoMaterialOverride);
+    Varying.Card     = CardIndex;
+    return Varying;
+}
+
+@fragment
+fn CaptureFragment(Varying: CaptureVarying) -> CaptureTargets
+{
+    let Card     = Cards[Varying.Card];
+    let Material = Materials[Varying.Family];
+    var Normal   = normalize(Varying.Normal);
+    // 📝 An open surface seen from behind still faces the card that saw it; the captured normal is turned toward it.
+    if (dot(Normal, ResolveCardAxis(Card.Axis)) < 0.0)
+    {
+        Normal = -Normal;
+    }
+    var Targets: CaptureTargets;
+    Targets.Albedo   = vec4f(Material.Albedo * (1.0 - Material.Metalness), 1.0);
+    Targets.Normal   = vec4f(Normal * 0.5 + 0.5, 1.0);
+    Targets.Emission = vec4f(Material.Emission, 1.0);
+    Targets.Depth    = vec4f(Varying.Position.z, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0);
+    return Targets;
+}
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/CardDirect.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/CardDirect.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2512d06
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/CardDirect.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,89 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                             CARDDIRECT.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 Direct sun and light-grid irradiance on every scheduled card texel, feeding the surface cache and indirect GI radiosity.
+
+//! include "FrameDescriptor.wgsl"
+//! include "DistanceTraversal.wgsl"
+//! include "CardProjection.wgsl"
+//! include "CardIrradiance.wgsl"
+//! include "FireIllumination.wgsl"
+//! include "LightClusterSpace.wgsl"
+
+@group(0) @binding(1) var<storage, read> Cards        : array<CardRecord>;
+@group(0) @binding(2) var<storage, read> Occupants    : array<OccupantRecord>;
+@group(0) @binding(3) var<storage, read> Tiles        : array<vec2u>;
+@group(0) @binding(4) var<uniform> Work               : CardWorkRecord;
+@group(0) @binding(5) var CardNormal                  : texture_2d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(6) var CardDepth                   : texture_2d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(7) var CardDirectTarget            : texture_storage_2d<rgba16float, write>;
+@group(0) @binding(8) var<storage, read> SceneLights   : LightClusterRecords;
+
+@compute @workgroup_size(8, 8)
+fn IntegrateCardDirect(@builtin(workgroup_id) Group: vec3u, @builtin(local_invocation_id) Local: vec3u)
+{
+    let WorkIndex = ResolveWorkIndex(Group);
+    if (WorkIndex >= Work.TileCount)
+    {
+        return;
+    }
+    let Assignment = Tiles[WorkIndex];
+    let Card = Cards[Assignment.x];
+    let TileTexel = ResolveTileTexel(Assignment, Local.xy);
+    if (any(TileTexel >= Card.TexelExtent))
+    {
+        return;
+    }
+    let Texel = Card.TexelOrigin + TileTexel;
+    let Depth = textureLoad(CardDepth, vec2i(Texel), 0).x;
+    if (Depth > 1.5)
+    {
+        textureStore(CardDirectTarget, Texel, vec4f(0.0));
+        return;
+    }
+
+    let Occupant    = Occupants[Card.Occupant];
+    let Coordinates = vec3f((vec2f(TileTexel) + 0.5) / vec2f(Card.TexelExtent), Depth);
+    let Position    = (Occupant.LocalToWorld * vec4f(ReconstructCardLocal(Card, Coordinates), 1.0)).xyz;
+    let LocalNormal = textureLoad(CardNormal, vec2i(Texel), 0).xyz * 2.0 - 1.0;
+    let Normal      = normalize((Occupant.LocalToWorld * vec4f(LocalNormal, 0.0)).xyz);
+
+    let Cosine = dot(Normal, Frame.SunDirection);
+    var Irradiance = vec3f(0.0);
+    if (Cosine > 0.0)
+    {
+        let Bias = ResolveSurfaceBias(Position);
+        var Visibility = 1.0;
+        if (FeatureEnabled(Frame, FeatureDirectShadow))
+        {
+            Visibility = TraverseSceneShadow(Position + Normal * Bias, Frame.SunDirection, 0.5 * Bias, 400.0, 6.0);
+        }
+        Irradiance = Frame.SunIlluminance * Cosine * Visibility;
+    }
+    let Fire = ResolveFireArrival(Position, Normal);
+    Irradiance += Fire.Illuminance * max(dot(Normal, Fire.Direction), 0.0);
+
+    // 📝 Light irradiance feeding the surface cards, which bounce into ReSTIR GI and multi-bounce radiosity. Only the lights
+    //    whose reach touches this point's cell are evaluated, and each is shadowed by the distance field like the sun.
+    var Candidates = ResolveLightCandidates(Position);
+    while (Candidates != 0u)
+    {
+        let Index = firstTrailingBit(Candidates);
+        Candidates &= Candidates - 1u;
+        let Light = SceneLights.Lights[Index];
+        let Illuminance = EvaluateLightArrival(Light, Position, Normal);
+        if (any(Illuminance > vec3f(0.0)))
+        {
+            let Toward = Light.PositionType.xyz - Position;
+            var Shade = 1.0;
+            if (FeatureEnabled(Frame, FeatureDirectShadow))
+            {
+                let Bias = ResolveSurfaceBias(Position);
+                Shade = TraverseSceneShadow(Position + Normal * Bias, normalize(Toward), 0.5 * Bias, max(length(Toward) - 0.5, 0.0), 4.0);
+            }
+            Irradiance += Illuminance * Shade;
+        }
+    }
+
+    textureStore(CardDirectTarget, Texel, vec4f(Irradiance, 1.0));
+}
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/CardFinal.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/CardFinal.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..26c5762
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/CardFinal.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,82 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                              CARDFINAL.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 Final card radiance: diffuse albedo over π times direct plus interpolated radiosity irradiance, plus authored emission.
+
+//! include "FrameDescriptor.wgsl"
+//! include "CardIrradiance.wgsl"
+
+@group(0) @binding(1) var<storage, read> Cards : array<CardRecord>;
+@group(0) @binding(2) var<storage, read> Tiles : array<vec2u>;
+@group(0) @binding(3) var<uniform> Work        : CardWorkRecord;
+@group(0) @binding(4) var CardAlbedo           : texture_2d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(5) var CardEmission         : texture_2d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(6) var CardDirect           : texture_2d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(7) var CardDepth            : texture_2d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(8) var<storage, read> Sites : array<vec4f>;
+@group(0) @binding(9) var CardFinalTarget      : texture_storage_2d<rgba16float, write>;
+
+// 📐 Radiosity sites are spatially filtered as they are interpolated: a Gaussian (σ = 0.9 site) over the 4×4 sites
+//    around the texel, restricted to the texel's own card and to sites that have gathered at all. Indirect irradiance
+//    is low-frequency, and 16 rays per site per gather is otherwise visible as a 4×4-texel speckle.
+fn InterpolateSiteIrradiance(Card: CardRecord, Texel: vec2u) -> vec3f
+{
+    let Continuous = (vec2f(Texel) + 0.5) / 4.0 - 0.5;
+    let Corner     = vec2i(floor(Continuous)) - vec2i(1);
+    let Lowest     = vec2i(Card.TexelOrigin / 4u);
+    let Highest    = vec2i((Card.TexelOrigin + Card.TexelExtent) / 4u) - vec2i(1);
+    var Sum = vec4f(0.0);
+    for (var Y = 0; Y < 4; Y++)
+    {
+        for (var X = 0; X < 4; X++)
+        {
+            let Site = Corner + vec2i(X, Y);
+            if (any(Site < Lowest) || any(Site > Highest))
+            {
+                continue;
+            }
+            let Record = Sites[u32(Site.y) * Work.SiteStride + u32(Site.x)];
+            if (Record.w <= 0.0)
+            {
+                continue;
+            }
+            let Offset = vec2f(Site) - Continuous;
+            let Weight = exp(-dot(Offset, Offset) / (2.0 * 0.9 * 0.9));
+            Sum += vec4f(Record.rgb * Weight, Weight);
+        }
+    }
+    return select(vec3f(0.0), Sum.rgb / Sum.w, Sum.w > 1.0e-4);
+}
+
+@compute @workgroup_size(8, 8)
+fn IntegrateCardFinal(@builtin(workgroup_id) Group: vec3u, @builtin(local_invocation_id) Local: vec3u)
+{
+    let WorkIndex = ResolveWorkIndex(Group);
+    if (WorkIndex >= Work.TileCount)
+    {
+        return;
+    }
+    let Assignment = Tiles[WorkIndex];
+    let Card = Cards[Assignment.x];
+    let TileTexel = ResolveTileTexel(Assignment, Local.xy);
+    if (any(TileTexel >= Card.TexelExtent))
+    {
+        return;
+    }
+    let Texel = Card.TexelOrigin + TileTexel;
+    if (textureLoad(CardDepth, vec2i(Texel), 0).x > 1.5)
+    {
+        textureStore(CardFinalTarget, vec2i(Texel), vec4f(0.0));
+        return;
+    }
+    let Albedo   = textureLoad(CardAlbedo, vec2i(Texel), 0).rgb;
+    let Emission = textureLoad(CardEmission, vec2i(Texel), 0).rgb * Frame.EmissionScale;
+    let Direct   = textureLoad(CardDirect, vec2i(Texel), 0).rgb;
+    var Indirect = vec3f(0.0);
+    if (FeatureEnabled(Frame, FeatureCardRadiosity))
+    {
+        Indirect = InterpolateSiteIrradiance(Card, Texel);
+    }
+    let Radiance = Albedo * InversePi * (Direct + Indirect) + Emission;
+    textureStore(CardFinalTarget, vec2i(Texel), vec4f(Radiance, 1.0));
+}
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/CardIrradiance.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/CardIrradiance.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1b1d931
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/CardIrradiance.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                           CARDIRRADIANCE.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 The scheduled-tile record shared by the three card lighting passes (direct, radiosity, final).
+
+// 📝 Three passes walk the same scheduled 8×8 card tiles, in this order each frame:
+//    ① CardDirect.wgsl    — E_direct = E_sun · max(n·l, 0) · V, V traced through the scene distance field;
+//    ② CardRadiosity.wgsl — one site per 4×4 texels gathers 16 cosine rays whose hits read LAST frame's card
+//       radiance, so every frame adds a bounce and the depot converges toward multiple bounces;
+//    ③ CardFinal.wgsl     — L_card = (albedo/π)·(E_direct + E_indirect) + emission, the radiance tracers read.
+
+struct CardWorkRecord
+{
+    TileCount    : u32,   // [-]    scheduled tiles this frame
+    SiteStride   : u32,   // [site] sites per row of the card texel space
+    StaticWeight  : f32,   // [-]    minimum radiosity weight for static cards
+    DynamicWeight : f32,   // [-]    minimum radiosity weight for moving cards
+}
+
+fn ResolveTileTexel(Assignment: vec2u, Local: vec2u) -> vec2u
+{
+    return vec2u(Assignment.y & 0xFFFFu, Assignment.y >> 16u) * 8u + Local;
+}
+
+fn ResolveWorkIndex(Group: vec3u) -> u32
+{
+    return Group.x + Group.y * 65535u;
+}
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/CardProjection.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/CardProjection.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1dc5b09
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/CardProjection.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                           CARDPROJECTION.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 The one mapping between an occupant's local frame and a card's (u, v, depth) — shared by capture and every lookup.
+
+//! include "SceneRecords.wgsl"
+
+//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+//                                                   CARD PROJECTION
+//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+fn ResolveCardAxis(Axis: u32) -> vec3f
+{
+    var Outward = vec3f(0.0);
+    Outward[Axis >> 1u] = select(1.0, -1.0, (Axis & 1u) == 1u);
+    return Outward;
+}
+
+// 📐 Card coordinates of a local point: u, v across the face, depth along the inward view direction, all in [0, 1].
+//    Depth axis k = Axis/2, u axis (k+1) mod 3, v axis (k+2) mod 3 — capture and lookup share this one mapping.
+fn ProjectCardCoordinates(Card: CardRecord, Local: vec3f) -> vec3f
+{
+    let DepthAxis = Card.Axis >> 1u;
+    let AcrossU   = (DepthAxis + 1u) % 3u;
+    let AcrossV   = (DepthAxis + 2u) % 3u;
+    let Extent    = max(Card.LocalMaximum - Card.LocalMinimum, vec3f(1.0e-5));
+    let U = (Local[AcrossU] - Card.LocalMinimum[AcrossU]) / Extent[AcrossU];
+    let V = (Local[AcrossV] - Card.LocalMinimum[AcrossV]) / Extent[AcrossV];
+    let FromMaximum = (Card.LocalMaximum[DepthAxis] - Local[DepthAxis]) / Extent[DepthAxis];
+    let FromMinimum = (Local[DepthAxis] - Card.LocalMinimum[DepthAxis]) / Extent[DepthAxis];
+    return vec3f(U, V, select(FromMinimum, FromMaximum, (Card.Axis & 1u) == 0u));
+}
+
+fn ReconstructCardLocal(Card: CardRecord, Coordinates: vec3f) -> vec3f
+{
+    let DepthAxis = Card.Axis >> 1u;
+    let AcrossU   = (DepthAxis + 1u) % 3u;
+    let AcrossV   = (DepthAxis + 2u) % 3u;
+    let Extent    = Card.LocalMaximum - Card.LocalMinimum;
+    var Local = vec3f(0.0);
+    Local[AcrossU] = Card.LocalMinimum[AcrossU] + Coordinates.x * Extent[AcrossU];
+    Local[AcrossV] = Card.LocalMinimum[AcrossV] + Coordinates.y * Extent[AcrossV];
+    Local[DepthAxis] = select(Card.LocalMinimum[DepthAxis] + Coordinates.z * Extent[DepthAxis],
+                              Card.LocalMaximum[DepthAxis] - Coordinates.z * Extent[DepthAxis], (Card.Axis & 1u) == 0u);
+    return Local;
+}
+
+fn ResolveCardDepthExtent(Card: CardRecord) -> f32
+{
+    let Extent = Card.LocalMaximum - Card.LocalMinimum;
+    return max(Extent[Card.Axis >> 1u], 1.0e-4);
+}
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/CardRadiosity.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/CardRadiosity.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5cbc520
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/CardRadiosity.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,104 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                            CARDRADIOSITY.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 Hemispherical gather for card radiosity sites: 16 stratified cosine rays per site, hits read last frame's card radiance.
+
+// 📝 A site stands for a 4×4 block of card texels. Its 16 lanes first elect the occupied texel nearest the block centre,
+//    then each traces one stratum of a 4×4 cosine-weighted hemisphere from it. E = π·mean(L) is folded into the site's
+//    running estimate with an exponential weight that never falls below a floor, so the depot keeps responding to
+//    moving light and moving occupants instead of freezing once converged.
+
+//! include "CardSampling.wgsl"
+//! include "CardIrradiance.wgsl"
+//! include "DiscrepancySequence.wgsl"
+
+@group(0) @binding(1) var<storage, read> Tiles      : array<vec2u>;
+@group(0) @binding(2) var<uniform> Work             : CardWorkRecord;
+@group(0) @binding(3) var CardNormal                : texture_2d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(4) var<storage, read_write> Sites : array<vec4f>;
+
+var<workgroup> SiteKeys     : array<atomic<u32>, 4>;
+var<workgroup> LaneRadiance : array<vec3f, 64>;
+
+@compute @workgroup_size(64)
+fn IntegrateCardRadiosity(@builtin(workgroup_id) Group: vec3u, @builtin(local_invocation_index) Lane: u32)
+{
+    let WorkIndex = ResolveWorkIndex(Group);
+    if (WorkIndex >= Work.TileCount)
+    {
+        return;
+    }
+    let Site = Lane >> 4u;
+    let Ray  = Lane & 15u;
+    if (Lane < 4u)
+    {
+        atomicStore(&SiteKeys[Lane], 0xFFFFFFFFu);
+    }
+    workgroupBarrier();
+
+    let Assignment = Tiles[WorkIndex];
+    let Card = Cards[Assignment.x];
+    let SiteOrigin = ResolveTileTexel(Assignment, vec2u(Site & 1u, Site >> 1u) * 4u);
+    let CandidateTile = SiteOrigin + vec2u(Ray & 3u, Ray >> 2u);
+
+    // ① elect the occupied texel nearest the block centre
+    if (all(CandidateTile < Card.TexelExtent))
+    {
+        let Depth = textureLoad(CardDepth, vec2i(Card.TexelOrigin + CandidateTile), 0).x;
+        if (Depth <= 1.5)
+        {
+            let Offset = vec2f(f32(Ray & 3u), f32(Ray >> 2u)) - vec2f(1.5);
+            let Key = (u32(dot(Offset, Offset) * 4.0) << 4u) | Ray;
+            atomicMin(&SiteKeys[Site], Key);
+        }
+    }
+    workgroupBarrier();
+    let Elected = atomicLoad(&SiteKeys[Site]);
+
+    var Radiance = vec3f(0.0);
+    if (Elected != 0xFFFFFFFFu)
+    {
+        let ElectedRay  = Elected & 15u;
+        let TileTexel   = SiteOrigin + vec2u(ElectedRay & 3u, ElectedRay >> 2u);
+        let Texel       = vec2i(Card.TexelOrigin + TileTexel);
+        let Depth       = textureLoad(CardDepth, Texel, 0).x;
+        let Occupant    = Occupants[Card.Occupant];
+        let Coordinates = vec3f((vec2f(TileTexel) + 0.5) / vec2f(Card.TexelExtent), Depth);
+        let Position    = (Occupant.LocalToWorld * vec4f(ReconstructCardLocal(Card, Coordinates), 1.0)).xyz;
+        let LocalNormal = textureLoad(CardNormal, Texel, 0).xyz * 2.0 - 1.0;
+        let Normal      = normalize((Occupant.LocalToWorld * vec4f(LocalNormal, 0.0)).xyz);
+
+        // ② one stratum of a jittered 4×4 cosine hemisphere per lane
+        var Seed = ConstructPixelSeed(vec2u(Texel), Frame.FrameIndex, Ray);
+        let Pair = (vec2f(f32(Ray & 3u), f32(Ray >> 2u)) + vec2f(AdvanceUniform(&Seed), AdvanceUniform(&Seed))) * 0.25;
+        let Direction = ConstructTangentFrame(Normal) * ProjectCosineHemisphere(Pair);
+        let Bias = ResolveSurfaceBias(Position);
+        let Hit = TraverseSceneDistance(Position + Normal * Bias, Direction, 0.5 * Bias, 120.0, 0.02);
+        Radiance = ResolveTraversalRadiance(Hit, Direction);
+    }
+    LaneRadiance[Lane] = Radiance;
+    workgroupBarrier();
+
+    // ③ fold E = π·mean(L) into the site estimate
+    if (Ray == 0u)
+    {
+        let SiteTexel = Card.TexelOrigin + SiteOrigin;
+        let SiteIndex = (SiteTexel.y / 4u) * Work.SiteStride + SiteTexel.x / 4u;
+        if (Elected == 0xFFFFFFFFu)
+        {
+            Sites[SiteIndex] = vec4f(0.0);
+            return;
+        }
+        var Sum = vec3f(0.0);
+        for (var Index = 0u; Index < 16u; Index++)
+        {
+            Sum += LaneRadiance[Site * 16u + Index];
+        }
+        let Estimate = Pi * Sum / 16.0;
+        let Prior    = Sites[SiteIndex];
+        let Dynamic  = (Occupants[Card.Occupant].Roles & RoleDynamic) != 0u;
+        let Floor    = select(Work.StaticWeight, Work.DynamicWeight, Dynamic);
+        let Fraction = max(1.0 / (Prior.w + 1.0), Floor);
+        Sites[SiteIndex] = vec4f(mix(Prior.rgb, Estimate, Fraction), min(Prior.w + 1.0, 64.0));
+    }
+}
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/CardSampling.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/CardSampling.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..234497b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/CardSampling.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,202 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                            CARDSAMPLING.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 Surface-card lookup — the radiance a distance-field hit point carries, read from its occupant's cards (the surface cache).
+
+//! include "FrameDescriptor.wgsl"
+//! include "DistanceTraversal.wgsl"
+//! include "SkyProjection.wgsl"
+//! include "CardProjection.wgsl"
+
+// 📝 Group 2 is the card depot as the tracers see it: occupants, cards, card depth (2.0+ marks a vacant texel) and the
+//    card final radiance, plus the sky-view radiance a ray that escapes reads instead.
+@group(2) @binding(0) var<storage, read> Occupants : array<OccupantRecord>;
+@group(2) @binding(1) var<storage, read> Cards     : array<CardRecord>;
+@group(2) @binding(2) var CardDepth                : texture_2d<f32>;
+@group(2) @binding(3) var CardFinal                : texture_2d<f32>;
+@group(2) @binding(4) var SkyView                  : texture_2d<f32>;
+@group(2) @binding(5) var SkySampler               : sampler;
+
+//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+//                                                     GROUND CARDS
+//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+// 📝 Ground tiles own one +Z card each, allocated consecutively, so a ground hit resolves its card from x, y alone.
+fn ResolveGroundCard(Planar: vec2f) -> u32
+{
+    let PadMinimum = vec2f(GroundPadMinimumX, GroundPadMinimumY);
+    let TileCount  = vec2u(GroundTileCountX, GroundTileCountY);
+    let PadMaximum = PadMinimum + GroundTileExtent * vec2f(TileCount);
+    if (all(Planar >= PadMinimum) && all(Planar < PadMaximum))
+    {
+        let Tile = min(vec2u((Planar - PadMinimum) / GroundTileExtent), TileCount - vec2u(1u));
+        return GroundFirstCard + Tile.x * TileCount.y + Tile.y;
+    }
+    if (Planar.x < PadMinimum.x)
+    {
+        return GroundStripCard;
+    }
+    if (Planar.x >= PadMaximum.x)
+    {
+        return GroundStripCard + 1u;
+    }
+    if (Planar.y < PadMinimum.y)
+    {
+        return GroundStripCard + 2u;
+    }
+    return GroundStripCard + 3u;
+}
+
+//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+//                                                    CARD RADIANCE
+//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+// 📝 Four bilinear taps, each validated on its own captured depth. Returns (Σw·L, Σw) for depth-validated taps in the
+//    first vector and the same for every occupied tap in the second, which is the fallback when validation rejects all.
+struct CardTaps
+{
+    Validated : vec4f,
+    Occupied  : vec4f,
+}
+
+fn SampleCardTaps(Card: CardRecord, Coordinates: vec3f, Tolerance: f32) -> CardTaps
+{
+    var Taps: CardTaps;
+    Taps.Validated = vec4f(0.0);
+    Taps.Occupied  = vec4f(0.0);
+    let Lowest   = vec2i(Card.TexelOrigin);
+    let Highest  = vec2i(Card.TexelOrigin + Card.TexelExtent) - vec2i(1);
+    let Position = vec2f(Card.TexelOrigin) + clamp(Coordinates.xy, vec2f(0.0), vec2f(1.0)) * vec2f(Card.TexelExtent) - 0.5;
+    let Corner   = floor(Position);
+    let Fraction = Position - Corner;
+    for (var Tap = 0u; Tap < 4u; Tap++)
+    {
+        let Offset   = vec2u(Tap & 1u, Tap >> 1u);
+        let Texel    = clamp(vec2i(Corner) + vec2i(Offset), Lowest, Highest);
+        let Bilinear = select(1.0 - Fraction.x, Fraction.x, Offset.x == 1u) * select(1.0 - Fraction.y, Fraction.y, Offset.y == 1u);
+        let Depth    = textureLoad(CardDepth, Texel, 0).x;
+        if (Depth > 1.5)
+        {
+            continue;
+        }
+        let Radiance = textureLoad(CardFinal, Texel, 0).rgb;
+        let Weight   = max(Bilinear, 1.0e-3);
+        Taps.Occupied += vec4f(Radiance * Weight, Weight);
+        if (abs(Depth - Coordinates.z) <= Tolerance)
+        {
+            Taps.Validated += vec4f(Radiance * Weight, Weight);
+        }
+    }
+    return Taps;
+}
+
+// 📝 Radiance leaving a scene point toward the tracer, from the cards of the occupant the distance field names there.
+//    Each card is weighted by how squarely it faces the hit normal; a card that cannot see the point fails its depth
+//    test and drops out, which is how a concave occupant's six cards stay correct. Tolerance [m] scales with the
+//    cascade that produced the hit, since the hit point is only as precise as that cascade's voxel.
+//    Returns (radiance, coverage); coverage 0 means no card covers the point at all.
+fn SampleCardRadiance(Position: vec3f, Normal: vec3f, Identity: u32, Tolerance: f32) -> vec4f
+{
+    if (Identity == GroundIdentity)
+    {
+        let Card = Cards[ResolveGroundCard(Position.xy)];
+        let Coordinates = ProjectCardCoordinates(Card, vec3f(Position.xy, Distance.GroundHeight));
+        let Taps = SampleCardTaps(Card, Coordinates, 2.0);
+        if (Taps.Occupied.w > 0.0)
+        {
+            return vec4f(Taps.Occupied.rgb / Taps.Occupied.w, 1.0);
+        }
+        return vec4f(0.0);
+    }
+    if (Identity >= arrayLength(&Occupants))
+    {
+        return vec4f(0.0);
+    }
+    let Occupant    = Occupants[Identity];
+    if ((Occupant.Roles & RoleFallback) != 0u)
+    {
+        return vec4f(ResolveFallbackRadiance(Occupant, Position, Normal), 1.0);
+    }
+    let Local       = (Occupant.WorldToLocal * vec4f(Position, 1.0)).xyz;
+    let LocalNormal = normalize((Occupant.WorldToLocal * vec4f(Normal, 0.0)).xyz);
+    var Validated = vec4f(0.0);
+    var Occupied  = vec4f(0.0);
+    for (var Index = 0u; Index < Occupant.CardCount; Index++)
+    {
+        let Card   = Cards[Occupant.FirstCard + Index];
+        let Facing = dot(LocalNormal, ResolveCardAxis(Card.Axis));
+        if (Facing <= 0.0)
+        {
+            continue;
+        }
+        let Coordinates = ProjectCardCoordinates(Card, Local);
+        if (any(Coordinates.xy < vec2f(-0.02)) || any(Coordinates.xy > vec2f(1.02)))
+        {
+            continue;
+        }
+        let Taps = SampleCardTaps(Card, Coordinates, Tolerance / ResolveCardDepthExtent(Card));
+        let AxisWeight = Facing * Facing;
+        Validated += vec4f(Taps.Validated.rgb, Taps.Validated.w) * AxisWeight;
+        Occupied  += vec4f(Taps.Occupied.rgb, Taps.Occupied.w) * AxisWeight;
+    }
+    if (Validated.w > 1.0e-4)
+    {
+        return vec4f(Validated.rgb / Validated.w, 1.0);
+    }
+    if (Occupied.w > 1.0e-4)
+    {
+        return vec4f(Occupied.rgb / Occupied.w, 0.5);
+    }
+    return vec4f(0.0);
+}
+
+// 📝 A card-less occupant (a fragment: born mid-frame, gone into the field the same frame, never captured) shades its
+//    hit from its packed albedo, under the sun with a short traced shadow and the sky's hemisphere toward the normal:
+//    L = ρ/π · (E_sun · cosθ · V + π · L_sky(n') · (½ + ½ n_z)). Rough, and enough for a second bounce.
+fn ResolveFallbackRadiance(Occupant: OccupantRecord, Position: vec3f, Normal: vec3f) -> vec3f
+{
+    let Albedo = unpack4x8unorm(Occupant.FirstCard).rgb;
+    var Irradiance = vec3f(0.0);
+    let Cosine = dot(Normal, Frame.SunDirection);
+    if (Cosine > 0.0)
+    {
+        let Bias = ResolveSurfaceBias(Position);
+        Irradiance += Frame.SunIlluminance * Cosine * TraverseSceneShadow(Position + Normal * Bias, Frame.SunDirection, 0.5 * Bias, 60.0, 6.0);
+    }
+    let Upward = normalize(Normal + vec3f(0.0, 0.0, 1.0));
+    Irradiance += 3.14159265 * SampleSkyRadiance(Upward) * (0.5 + 0.5 * Normal.z);
+    return Albedo * InversePi * Irradiance;
+}
+
+// 📝 Tolerance for a hit answered by cascade Level: one and a half of its voxels, never below 6 cm.
+fn ResolveCardTolerance(Level: u32) -> f32
+{
+    let Clamped = min(Level, Distance.ClipCount - 1u);
+    return max(1.5 * Distance.Clips[Clamped].VoxelExtent, 0.06);
+}
+
+//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+//                                                     SKY RADIANCE
+//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+fn SampleSkyRadiance(Direction: vec3f) -> vec3f
+{
+    let Coordinates = ProjectSkyCoordinates(normalize(Direction));
+    return textureSampleLevel(SkyView, SkySampler, Coordinates, 0.0).rgb * Frame.SkyScale + Frame.NightSkyRadiance;
+}
+
+// 📝 What a traced ray brings back: card radiance at a surface, sky radiance on an escape. A surface no card covers
+//    returns nothing — an uncovered point is treated as an absorber rather than guessed, which can only darken.
+fn ResolveTraversalRadiance(Hit: TraversalHit, Direction: vec3f) -> vec3f
+{
+    if (!Hit.Hit)
+    {
+        return SampleSkyRadiance(Direction);
+    }
+    let Card = SampleCardRadiance(Hit.Position, Hit.Normal, Hit.Identity, ResolveCardTolerance(Hit.Level));
+    if (Card.w > 0.0)
+    {
+        return Card.rgb;
+    }
+    return vec3f(0.0);
+}
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/DirectRadiance.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/DirectRadiance.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ac3e074
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/DirectRadiance.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,199 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                           DIRECTRADIANCE.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 Direct sun radiance, tyre-fire and light-grid arrivals at every primary surface, cascaded shadow depth, and sky background.
+
+//! include "FrameDescriptor.wgsl"
+//! include "SurfaceReflectance.wgsl"
+//! include "PackingCodec.wgsl"
+//! include "SkyProjection.wgsl"
+//! include "FireIllumination.wgsl"
+//! include "DistanceTraversal.wgsl"
+//! include "LightClusterSpace.wgsl"
+//! include "RayTraversal.wgsl"
+
+struct CascadeReceiver
+{
+    LightViewProjection : array<mat4x4f, 3>,
+    Splits              : vec4f,   // [m]   xyz far distance of each cascade, w cascade count
+    TexelWorld          : vec4f,   // [m]   world size of one shadow texel per cascade
+}
+
+@group(0) @binding(1) var<storage, read> Materials     : array<MaterialRecord>;
+@group(0) @binding(2) var SurfaceAttributes            : texture_2d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(3) var SurfaceDepth                 : texture_depth_2d;
+@group(0) @binding(4) var ShadowDepth                  : texture_depth_2d_array;
+@group(0) @binding(5) var ShadowSampler                : sampler_comparison;
+@group(0) @binding(6) var<uniform> Receiver            : CascadeReceiver;
+@group(0) @binding(7) var DirectSkyView                : texture_2d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(8) var DirectSkySampler             : sampler;
+@group(0) @binding(9) var DirectTarget                 : texture_storage_2d<rgba16float, write>;   // rgb radiance, w sun visibility
+// 📝 SceneLights (group 3, binding 3) is declared once, by RayTraversal.wgsl: the same light records and cell masks serve this pass,
+//    the ray-traced next-event estimation and the card relighting.
+@group(0) @binding(10) var DirectIrradianceTarget      : texture_storage_2d<rgba16float, write>;   // rgb diffuse irradiance of fire and lights
+
+// 📐 3×3 percentage-closer taps, each a hardware bilinear comparison, after a normal offset of 1.5 texels.
+fn ResolveCascadeVisibility(Position: vec3f, Normal: vec3f) -> f32
+{
+    let ViewDistance = ResolveViewDepth(Position);
+    let Count = u32(Receiver.Splits.w);
+    var Cascade = 0u;
+    while (Cascade + 1u < Count && ViewDistance > Receiver.Splits[Cascade])
+    {
+        Cascade++;
+    }
+    if (ViewDistance > Receiver.Splits[Count - 1u])
+    {
+        return 1.0;
+    }
+    let Offset = Position + Normal * (1.5 * Receiver.TexelWorld[Cascade]);
+    let Clip = Receiver.LightViewProjection[Cascade] * vec4f(Offset, 1.0);
+    let Ndc = Clip.xyz / Clip.w;
+    let Coordinates = vec2f(Ndc.x * 0.5 + 0.5, 0.5 - Ndc.y * 0.5);
+    if (any(Coordinates < vec2f(0.0)) || any(Coordinates > vec2f(1.0)) || Ndc.z > 1.0)
+    {
+        return 1.0;
+    }
+    let Texel = 1.0 / vec2f(textureDimensions(ShadowDepth).xy);
+    var Lit = 0.0;
+    for (var Y = -1; Y <= 1; Y++)
+    {
+        for (var X = -1; X <= 1; X++)
+        {
+            Lit += textureSampleCompareLevel(ShadowDepth, ShadowSampler, Coordinates + vec2f(f32(X), f32(Y)) * Texel, Cascade, Ndc.z);
+        }
+    }
+    return Lit / 9.0;
+}
+
+fn ResolveBackgroundRadiance(Direction: vec3f) -> vec3f
+{
+    var Radiance = textureSampleLevel(DirectSkyView, DirectSkySampler, ProjectSkyCoordinates(Direction), 0.0).rgb * Frame.SkyScale
+                 + Frame.NightSkyRadiance;
+    // 📝 The solar disc (0.27° radius) is added only here, never to escaped rays, so it is not counted twice.
+    let Cosine = dot(Direction, Frame.SunDirection);
+    if (Cosine > 0.99998)
+    {
+        Radiance += Frame.SunIlluminance * 2500.0;
+    }
+    return Radiance;
+}
+
+@compute @workgroup_size(8, 8)
+fn IntegrateDirectRadiance(@builtin(global_invocation_id) Invocation: vec3u)
+{
+    let Pixel = Invocation.xy;
+    if (any(vec2f(Pixel) >= Frame.ScreenExtent))
+    {
+        return;
+    }
+    let Depth = textureLoad(SurfaceDepth, vec2i(Pixel), 0);
+    let Centre = vec2f(Pixel) + 0.5;
+    if (Depth <= 0.0)
+    {
+        let Far = ReconstructWorldPosition(Centre, 1.0e-6);
+        textureStore(DirectTarget, vec2i(Pixel), vec4f(ResolveBackgroundRadiance(normalize(Far - Frame.CameraPosition)), 0.0));
+        textureStore(DirectIrradianceTarget, vec2i(Pixel), vec4f(0.0));
+        return;
+    }
+    let Position     = ReconstructWorldPosition(Centre, Depth);
+    let Attributes   = textureLoad(SurfaceAttributes, vec2i(Pixel), 0);
+    let Normal       = DecodeOctahedral(Attributes.xy);
+    let Surface      = ProjectSurfaceSample(Materials[u32(Attributes.z + 0.5)]);
+    let View         = normalize(Frame.CameraPosition - Position);
+    let UseRtShadows = FeatureEnabled(Frame, FeatureRayTracing) && FeatureEnabled(Frame, FeatureRayTracedShadows);
+    let RayOrigin    = Position + Normal * RayEpsilon;
+
+    var Visibility = 1.0;
+    var SunDir     = Frame.SunDirection;
+    if (FeatureEnabled(Frame, FeatureDirectShadow))
+    {
+        if (UseRtShadows)
+        {
+            SunDir     = SampleSunConeDirection(Frame.SunDirection, ProjectTemporalPair(Pixel, Frame.FrameIndex, 17u));
+            Visibility = TraceSceneVisibility(RayOrigin, SunDir, RayEpsilon, 400.0);
+        }
+        else
+        {
+            Visibility = ResolveCascadeVisibility(Position, Normal);
+        }
+    }
+    var Radiance = Frame.SunIlluminance * Visibility * ResolveDirectReflectance(Surface, Normal, View, SunDir);
+
+    // 📝 Irradiance here is diffuse (cosine-weighted, unscaled by the albedo): the display's screen exitance and the cards
+    //    both need it, and the radiance above carries only the specular-inclusive response for direct shading.
+    var Irradiance = vec3f(0.0);
+    let Fire = ResolveFireArrival(Position, Normal);
+    if (any(Fire.Illuminance > vec3f(0.0)))
+    {
+        let FireCosine = max(dot(Normal, Fire.Direction), 0.0);
+        Radiance += Fire.Illuminance * ResolveDirectReflectance(Surface, Normal, View, Fire.Direction);
+        Irradiance += Fire.Illuminance * FireCosine;
+    }
+
+    // 📝 Only the lights whose reach touches this point's grid cell are evaluated (LightClusterSpace.wgsl). Their shadow is the exact
+    //    BVH visibility when the BVH renderer is active and the distance-field soft shadow otherwise.
+    var Candidates = ResolveLightCandidates(Position);
+    while (Candidates != 0u)
+    {
+        let Index = firstTrailingBit(Candidates);
+        Candidates &= Candidates - 1u;
+        let Light = SceneLights.Lights[Index];
+        let Illuminance = EvaluateLightArrival(Light, Position, Normal);
+        if (any(Illuminance > vec3f(0.0)))
+        {
+            let Offset      = Light.PositionType.xyz - Position;
+            let LightDist   = length(Offset);
+            let TowardLight = Offset / max(LightDist, 1.0e-4);
+            var Shade       = 1.0;
+            if (UseRtShadows)
+            {
+                Shade = TraceSceneVisibility(RayOrigin, TowardLight, RayEpsilon, max(LightDist - 0.08, RayEpsilon));
+            }
+            else if (FeatureEnabled(Frame, FeatureDirectShadow))
+            {
+                let Bias = ResolveSurfaceBias(Position);
+                Shade = TraverseSceneShadow(Position + Normal * Bias, TowardLight, 0.5 * Bias, max(LightDist - 0.5, 0.0), 4.0);
+            }
+            let Lit = Illuminance * Shade;
+            Irradiance += Lit;
+            Radiance += Lit * ResolveDirectReflectance(Surface, Normal, View, TowardLight);
+        }
+    }
+
+    // 📝 The light technique of the emissive partition at this primary vertex (BVH mode only; see EmissiveLightSpace.js and RayTraversal.wgsl). The ReSTIR candidates that start here are
+    //    cosine sampled and see diffuse transport only, so this adds the emitters' DIFFUSE share: albedo/π × irradiance, with the BSDF technique's w_b taken off (the candidate's
+    //    first hit carries it). Specular reflections of emitters stay with the reflection pass, which counts them in full.
+    let EmissiveWords = ResolveEmissiveCell(Position);
+    if (EmissiveUsable(EmissiveWords))
+    {
+        var EmissiveIrradiance = vec3f(0.0);
+        for (var Sample = 0u; Sample < EmissiveSamplesPerVertex; Sample += 1u)
+        {
+            let Draw    = vec4f(ProjectTemporalPair(Pixel, Frame.FrameIndex, 21u + 4u * Sample), ProjectTemporalPair(Pixel, Frame.FrameIndex, 23u + 4u * Sample));
+            let Emitter = SampleEmissiveLight(Position, EmissiveWords, Draw);
+            if (!Emitter.Valid)
+            {
+                continue;
+            }
+            let Toward     = Emitter.Position - Position;
+            let Dist       = length(Toward);
+            let LDir       = Toward / max(Dist, 1.0e-4);
+            let CosSurface = dot(Normal, LDir);
+            if (CosSurface <= 1.0e-4)
+            {
+                continue;
+            }
+            let CosEmitter = abs(dot(Emitter.Normal, LDir));
+            let BsdfWeight = EvaluateEmissiveBsdfWeight(CosSurface * InversePi, Dist, CosEmitter);
+            let Visible    = TraceSceneVisibility(RayOrigin, LDir, RayEpsilon, max(Dist - 0.08, RayEpsilon));
+            EmissiveIrradiance += Emitter.Radiance * (CosEmitter * CosSurface * (1.0 - BsdfWeight) * Visible
+                                                      / (max(Dist * Dist, 1.0e-4) * max(Emitter.Pdf, 1.0e-8) * f32(EmissiveSamplesPerVertex)));
+        }
+        Irradiance += EmissiveIrradiance;
+        Radiance   += ResolveDiffuseAlbedo(Surface) * InversePi * EmissiveIrradiance;
+    }
+
+    textureStore(DirectTarget, vec2i(Pixel), vec4f(Radiance, Visibility));
+    textureStore(DirectIrradianceTarget, vec2i(Pixel), vec4f(Irradiance, 1.0));
+}
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/DiscrepancySequence.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/DiscrepancySequence.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..652a058
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/DiscrepancySequence.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                         DISCREPANCYSEQUENCE.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 Per-pixel sample streams — a PCG hash for decorrelation and the R2 additive recurrence for temporal stratification.
+
+// 📐 PCG-RXS-M-XS 32-bit permutation (O'Neill 2014), used as an integer hash.
+fn PermuteUnsigned(Input: u32) -> u32
+{
+    let Advanced = Input * 747796405u + 2891336453u;
+    let Word = ((Advanced >> ((Advanced >> 28u) + 4u)) ^ Advanced) * 277803737u;
+    return (Word >> 22u) ^ Word;
+}
+
+fn ConstructPixelSeed(Pixel: vec2u, FrameIndex: u32, Stream: u32) -> u32
+{
+    return PermuteUnsigned(Pixel.x + PermuteUnsigned(Pixel.y + PermuteUnsigned(FrameIndex + PermuteUnsigned(Stream))));
+}
+
+fn AdvanceUniform(Seed: ptr<function, u32>) -> f32
+{
+    *Seed = PermuteUnsigned(*Seed);
+    return f32(*Seed >> 8u) * (1.0 / 16777216.0);
+}
+
+// 📐 R2 sequence (Roberts 2018): x_n = frac(s + n·(1/φ₂, 1/φ₂²)), φ₂ the plastic constant. A per-pixel hashed start
+//    turns it into a Cranley–Patterson rotated stream, so each pixel walks a stratified sequence over frames.
+fn ProjectTemporalPair(Pixel: vec2u, FrameIndex: u32, Stream: u32) -> vec2f
+{
+    let Start = vec2f(f32(PermuteUnsigned((Pixel.x * 73856093u) ^ (Pixel.y * 19349663u) ^ (Stream * 83492791u)) >> 8u),
+                      f32(PermuteUnsigned((Pixel.y * 73856093u) ^ (Pixel.x * 19349663u) ^ (Stream * 2654435761u)) >> 8u))
+                * (1.0 / 16777216.0);
+    let Step = vec2f(0.7548776662466927, 0.5698402909980532);
+    return fract(Start + f32(FrameIndex % 65536u) * Step);
+}
+
+// 📐 Cosine-weighted hemisphere direction about +Z (Malley's method), pdf = cosθ / π.
+fn ProjectCosineHemisphere(Pair: vec2f) -> vec3f
+{
+    let Radius = sqrt(Pair.x);
+    let φ = 2.0 * 3.14159265358979 * Pair.y;
+    return vec3f(Radius * cos(φ), Radius * sin(φ), sqrt(max(0.0, 1.0 - Pair.x)));
+}
+
+// 📐 Uniform disk sample (concentric would be lower distortion; uniform suffices for reuse offsets).
+fn ProjectUniformDisk(Pair: vec2f) -> vec2f
+{
+    let Radius = sqrt(Pair.x);
+    let φ = 2.0 * 3.14159265358979 * Pair.y;
+    return vec2f(cos(φ), sin(φ)) * Radius;
+}
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/DisplayAntialias.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/DisplayAntialias.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ffac598
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/DisplayAntialias.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,87 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                          DISPLAYANTIALIAS.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 Temporal antialiasing: motion-reprojected prior colour, clamped to the surrounding 3×3 YCoCg extent.
+
+//! include "FrameDescriptor.wgsl"
+
+@group(0) @binding(1) var RecombinedRadiance : texture_2d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(2) var PriorRadiance     : texture_2d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(3) var SurfaceMotion     : texture_2d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(4) var LinearClamp       : sampler;
+@group(0) @binding(5) var AntialiasTarget   : texture_storage_2d<rgba16float, write>;
+
+fn ProjectCoCg(Colour: vec3f) -> vec3f
+{
+    return vec3f(0.25 * Colour.r + 0.5 * Colour.g + 0.25 * Colour.b, 0.5 * Colour.r - 0.5 * Colour.b,
+                 -0.25 * Colour.r + 0.5 * Colour.g - 0.25 * Colour.b);
+}
+
+fn ReconstructRgb(CoCg: vec3f) -> vec3f
+{
+    return vec3f(CoCg.x + CoCg.y - CoCg.z, CoCg.x + CoCg.z, CoCg.x - CoCg.y - CoCg.z);
+}
+
+// 📝 Range compression keeps a single bright texel from dominating the clamp box (Karis 2014).
+fn CompressRange(Colour: vec3f) -> vec3f
+{
+    return Colour / (1.0 + ResolveLuminance(Colour));
+}
+
+fn ExpandRange(Colour: vec3f) -> vec3f
+{
+    return Colour / max(1.0 - ResolveLuminance(Colour), 1.0e-4);
+}
+
+@compute @workgroup_size(8, 8)
+fn IntegrateAntialias(@builtin(global_invocation_id) Invocation: vec3u)
+{
+    let Pixel = vec2i(Invocation.xy);
+    if (any(vec2f(Pixel) >= Frame.ScreenExtent))
+    {
+        return;
+    }
+    let Current = CompressRange(textureLoad(RecombinedRadiance, Pixel, 0).rgb);
+    if (!FeatureEnabled(Frame, FeatureTemporalAntialias) || Frame.InspectionMode == 6u || Frame.InspectionMode == 7u)
+    {
+        textureStore(AntialiasTarget, Pixel, vec4f(ExpandRange(Current), 1.0));
+        return;
+    }
+    var Minimum = vec3f(1.0e9);
+    var Maximum = vec3f(-1.0e9);
+    var Mean = vec3f(0.0);
+    var Square = vec3f(0.0);
+    let Limit = vec2i(Frame.ScreenExtent) - vec2i(1);
+    for (var Y = -1; Y <= 1; Y++)
+    {
+        for (var X = -1; X <= 1; X++)
+        {
+            let Tap = ProjectCoCg(CompressRange(textureLoad(RecombinedRadiance, clamp(Pixel + vec2i(X, Y), vec2i(0), Limit), 0).rgb));
+            Minimum = min(Minimum, Tap);
+            Maximum = max(Maximum, Tap);
+            Mean += Tap;
+            Square += Tap * Tap;
+        }
+    }
+    Mean /= 9.0;
+    let Deviation = sqrt(max(Square / 9.0 - Mean * Mean, vec3f(0.0)));
+    Minimum = max(Minimum, Mean - 1.25 * Deviation);
+    Maximum = min(Maximum, Mean + 1.25 * Deviation);
+
+    let Motion = textureLoad(SurfaceMotion, Pixel, 0).xy;
+    let PriorCoordinates = (vec2f(Pixel) + 0.5 - Motion) * Frame.InverseScreenExtent;
+    var Fraction = 0.1;
+    var Prior = Current;
+    if (any(PriorCoordinates < vec2f(0.0)) || any(PriorCoordinates > vec2f(1.0)) || Frame.FrameIndex < 2u
+        || FeatureEnabled(Frame, FeatureTemporalRestart))
+    {
+        Fraction = 1.0;
+    }
+    else
+    {
+        Prior = CompressRange(textureSampleLevel(PriorRadiance, LinearClamp, PriorCoordinates, 0.0).rgb);
+        Prior = ReconstructRgb(clamp(ProjectCoCg(Prior), Minimum, Maximum));
+    }
+    let Resolved = mix(Prior, Current, Fraction);
+    textureStore(AntialiasTarget, Pixel, vec4f(ExpandRange(Resolved), 1.0));
+}
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/DisplayExposure.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/DisplayExposure.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c77bbbd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/DisplayExposure.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,84 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                           DISPLAYEXPOSURE.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 Eye adaptation: log-average luminance of a 64×64 lattice of the frame, approached exponentially by the exposure.
+//    When ExtendedCockpitExposure is active (camera inside the car cabin), metering weights the windshield sightline and
+//    exterior sky/road samples so dark dashboard & pillar trim cannot trick auto-exposure into blowing out the view.
+
+//! include "FrameDescriptor.wgsl"
+
+@group(0) @binding(1) var ResolvedRadiance                 : texture_2d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(2) var<storage, read_write> Adaptation  : array<f32, 4>;
+
+var<workgroup> LaneSums    : array<f32, 256>;
+var<workgroup> LaneWeights : array<f32, 256>;
+
+@compute @workgroup_size(256)
+fn IntegrateExposure(@builtin(local_invocation_index) Lane: u32)
+{
+    let Cockpit = ExtendedEnabled(Frame, ExtendedCockpitExposure);
+    var Sum = 0.0;
+    var WeightSum = 0.0;
+    for (var Sample = 0u; Sample < 16u; Sample++)
+    {
+        let Index = Lane * 16u + Sample;
+        let Lattice = vec2f(f32(Index % 64u) + 0.5, f32(Index / 64u) + 0.5) / 64.0;
+        let Pixel = vec2i(Lattice * Frame.ScreenExtent);
+        let Luminance = ResolveLuminance(textureLoad(ResolvedRadiance, Pixel, 0).rgb);
+        var Weight = 1.0;
+        if (Cockpit)
+        {
+            let InWindshield = Lattice.x >= 0.14 && Lattice.x <= 0.86 && Lattice.y >= 0.06 && Lattice.y <= 0.48;
+            if (InWindshield && Luminance > 0.06)
+            {
+                Weight = 8.0;
+            }
+            else if (Luminance > 0.18)
+            {
+                Weight = 5.0;
+            }
+            else
+            {
+                Weight = 0.06;
+            }
+        }
+        Sum += Weight * log2(max(Luminance, 1.0e-5));
+        WeightSum += Weight;
+    }
+    LaneSums[Lane] = Sum;
+    LaneWeights[Lane] = WeightSum;
+    workgroupBarrier();
+    for (var Stride = 128u; Stride > 0u; Stride >>= 1u)
+    {
+        if (Lane < Stride)
+        {
+            LaneSums[Lane] += LaneSums[Lane + Stride];
+            LaneWeights[Lane] += LaneWeights[Lane + Stride];
+        }
+        workgroupBarrier();
+    }
+    if (Lane == 0u)
+    {
+        let Logarithm = LaneSums[0] / max(LaneWeights[0], 1.0);
+        let Average = exp2(Logarithm);
+        // 📐 Middle grey 0.18 at the log-average luminance — below 0.1 the eye adapts only partially so night courses
+        //    stay nocturnal, and in cockpit mode gain is capped so shaded cabin leather stays rich dark charcoal.
+        let Floor = select(log2(0.1), log2(0.22), Cockpit);
+        let Adapted = select(Logarithm, Floor + (Logarithm - Floor) * 0.66, Logarithm < Floor);
+        let MaxGain = select(60.0, 1.05, Cockpit);
+        let Target = clamp(0.18 / exp2(Adapted), 0.02, MaxGain) * exp2(Frame.ExposureCompensation);
+        let Prior = Adaptation[0];
+        var Exposure = Target;
+        if (Prior > 0.0 && Frame.FrameIndex > 2u)
+        {
+            let Speed = select(0.06, 0.14, Cockpit);
+            Exposure = exp2(mix(log2(Prior), log2(Target), Speed));
+        }
+        if (!FeatureEnabled(Frame, FeatureAutoExposure))
+        {
+            Exposure = 0.55 * exp2(Frame.ExposureCompensation);
+        }
+        Adaptation[0] = Exposure;
+        Adaptation[1] = Average;
+    }
+}
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/DisplayPresent.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/DisplayPresent.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ed8d583
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/DisplayPresent.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,119 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                           DISPLAYPRESENT.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 Exposure, ACES tonal projection and the distance-slice inset, written to the swapchain through an sRGB view.
+
+// 📝 The inset is a top-down slice of the ONE scene distance field at SliceHeight, centred on the cascade focus and
+//    spanning cascade 1: blue inside, amber outside with 0.25 m isolines, the cascade-0 window outlined, bricks a
+//    moving occupant rewrote glowing magenta and bricks the scrolling window rewrote flashing teal. Driving the
+//    ControlVehicle shows the union pass chasing it: only the bricks its old and new bounds touch light up.
+
+//! include "FrameDescriptor.wgsl"
+//! include "DistanceTraversal.wgsl"
+
+@group(0) @binding(1) var ResolvedRadiance                : texture_2d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(2) var<storage, read> Adaptation       : array<f32, 4>;
+
+struct PresentVarying
+{
+    @builtin(position) Position : vec4f,
+}
+
+@vertex
+fn PresentVertex(@builtin(vertex_index) Vertex: u32) -> PresentVarying
+{
+    let Corner = vec2f(f32((Vertex << 1u) & 2u), f32(Vertex & 2u));
+    var Varying: PresentVarying;
+    Varying.Position = vec4f(Corner * 2.0 - 1.0, 0.0, 1.0);
+    return Varying;
+}
+
+// 📐 Narkowicz's ACES filmic fit.
+fn ProjectFilmic(Radiance: vec3f) -> vec3f
+{
+    let a = 2.51;
+    let b = 0.03;
+    let c = 2.43;
+    let d = 0.59;
+    let e = 0.14;
+    return clamp((Radiance * (a * Radiance + b)) / (Radiance * (c * Radiance + d) + e), vec3f(0.0), vec3f(1.0));
+}
+
+fn ResolveInsetColour(Coordinates: vec2f) -> vec3f
+{
+    let Window = Distance.Clips[min(1u, Distance.ClipCount - 1u)];
+    let Span = f32(Window.Resolution) * Window.VoxelExtent;
+    let Planar = Frame.FocusPosition.xy + vec2f(Coordinates.x - 0.5, 0.5 - Coordinates.y) * Span;
+    let Position = vec3f(Planar, Frame.SliceHeight);
+    let Level = ResolveFinestClip(Position, 1.0);
+    if (Level >= Distance.ClipCount)
+    {
+        return vec3f(0.05);
+    }
+    let Signed = SampleClipDistance(Level, Position);
+    var Colour = select(vec3f(0.95, 0.62, 0.22), vec3f(0.18, 0.42, 0.95), Signed < 0.0);
+    Colour *= 0.35 + 0.65 * exp(-abs(Signed) * 0.9);
+    let Isoline = abs(fract(Signed / 0.25 + 0.5) - 0.5);
+    Colour = mix(Colour * 0.55, Colour, smoothstep(0.0, 0.06, Isoline));
+    if (abs(Signed) < 0.5 * Distance.Clips[Level].VoxelExtent)
+    {
+        Colour = vec3f(1.0);
+    }
+    let Voxel = vec3i(floor(Position / Distance.Clips[Level].VoxelExtent));
+    let Brick = vec3i(floor(vec3f(Voxel) / f32(BrickEdge)));
+    let Age = ResolveBrickAge(BrickEpochs[ResolveBrickSlot(Level, Brick, Distance.BricksPerAxis)], Frame.FrameIndex);
+    if (Age.y > 0.5 && Age.x < 24.0)
+    {
+        Colour = mix(Colour, vec3f(1.0, 0.1, 0.85), 0.6 * (1.0 - Age.x / 24.0));
+    }
+    else if (Age.x < 6.0)
+    {
+        Colour = mix(Colour, vec3f(0.2, 0.85, 0.9), 0.35 * (1.0 - Age.x / 6.0));
+    }
+    let Finest = Distance.Clips[0];
+    let FinestLow = vec2f(Finest.OriginVoxel.xy) * Finest.VoxelExtent;
+    let FinestHigh = FinestLow + vec2f(f32(Finest.Resolution) * Finest.VoxelExtent);
+    let EdgeLow = abs(Planar - FinestLow);
+    let EdgeHigh = abs(Planar - FinestHigh);
+    let Thickness = Span / 256.0;
+    let InsideX = Planar.x >= FinestLow.x && Planar.x <= FinestHigh.x;
+    let InsideY = Planar.y >= FinestLow.y && Planar.y <= FinestHigh.y;
+    if ((InsideY && (EdgeLow.x < Thickness || EdgeHigh.x < Thickness)) || (InsideX && (EdgeLow.y < Thickness || EdgeHigh.y < Thickness)))
+    {
+        Colour = vec3f(0.3, 1.0, 0.45);
+    }
+    return Colour;
+}
+
+@fragment
+fn PresentFragment(Varying: PresentVarying) -> @location(0) vec4f
+{
+    let Pixel = vec2i(Varying.Position.xy);
+    let Radiance = textureLoad(ResolvedRadiance, Pixel, 0).rgb;
+    var Exposure = Adaptation[0];
+    if (Exposure <= 0.0)
+    {
+        Exposure = 1.0;
+    }
+    var Colour = ProjectFilmic(Radiance * Exposure);
+    if (Frame.InspectionMode == 6u || Frame.InspectionMode == 8u || Frame.InspectionMode == 9u)
+    {
+        Colour = clamp(Radiance, vec3f(0.0), vec3f(1.0));
+    }
+    if (Frame.InsetEnabled != 0u)
+    {
+        let Size = floor(Frame.ScreenExtent.y * 0.34);
+        let Origin = vec2f(Frame.ScreenExtent.x - Size - 16.0, 16.0);
+        let Local = (Varying.Position.xy - Origin) / Size;
+        if (all(Local >= vec2f(0.0)) && all(Local <= vec2f(1.0)))
+        {
+            Colour = ResolveInsetColour(Local);
+            let Border = min(min(Local.x, 1.0 - Local.x), min(Local.y, 1.0 - Local.y)) * Size;
+            if (Border < 1.5)
+            {
+                Colour = vec3f(0.9);
+            }
+        }
+    }
+    return vec4f(Colour, 1.0);
+}
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/DisplayRecombination.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/DisplayRecombination.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2fe976e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/DisplayRecombination.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,180 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                        DISPLAYRECOMBINATION.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 Recombines direct, indirect diffuse, glossy reflection and emission per pixel, or substitutes an inspection signal;
+//    also writes the diffuse exitance that the next frame's screen traces read.
+
+// 📝 The indirect term arrives demodulated (irradiance E) and is modulated here by the diffuse albedo, so texture-free
+//    surfaces keep their edges through the wavelet. Specular indirect uses the split-sum response F0·A + B over the
+//    traced reflection; past the reflection cutoff it falls back to E/π, Lumen's rough-reflection reuse. A clear coat
+//    reflects the same radiance with its own response and attenuates the layer beneath by its Fresnel transmittance.
+
+//! include "FrameDescriptor.wgsl"
+//! include "SurfaceReflectance.wgsl"
+//! include "PackingCodec.wgsl"
+//! include "CabinVolume.wgsl"
+
+@group(0) @binding(1) var<storage, read> Materials : array<MaterialRecord>;
+@group(0) @binding(2) var SurfaceAttributes        : texture_2d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(3) var SurfaceDepth             : texture_depth_2d;
+@group(0) @binding(4) var DirectRadiance           : texture_2d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(5) var IndirectIrradiance       : texture_2d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(6) var ReflectionRadiance       : texture_2d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(7) var ResampledIrradiance      : texture_2d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(8) var InspectionRadiance       : texture_2d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(9) var CardFinal                : texture_2d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(10) var RecombinedTarget         : texture_storage_2d<rgba16float, write>;
+@group(0) @binding(11) var<storage, read> Occupants : array<OccupantRecord>;   // [0]: the car body, for its cabin
+
+@group(0) @binding(12) var TyrePlume : texture_2d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(13) var PlumeSampler : sampler;
+@group(0) @binding(14) var DirectIrradiance : texture_2d<f32>;   // rgb diffuse irradiance of fire and lights, from DirectRadiance
+@group(0) @binding(15) var ExitanceTarget : texture_storage_2d<rgba16float, write>;   // rgb diffuse exitance, read by the next frame's screen traces
+
+fn CompositePlume(Colour: vec3f, Pixel: vec2i) -> vec3f {
+    if (!FeatureEnabled(Frame, FeatureSmokeComposite) || Frame.InspectionMode != 0u) { return Colour; }
+    let Sample = textureSampleLevel(TyrePlume, PlumeSampler, (vec2f(Pixel) + 0.5) * Frame.InverseScreenExtent, 0.0);
+    return Colour * Sample.a + Sample.rgb;
+}
+
+// 📝 Of the traced indirect light the enclosed cabin keeps (CabinVolume.wgsl). Its surfaces lie inside the body's own
+//    distance volume, so their rays "hit" at once and gather the sunlit exterior's cards — several times the open road's
+//    irradiance. A twentieth of that is about what windows let in; the sun through the glass is direct and untouched.
+const CabinIndirectShare : f32 = 0.05;
+
+const InspectionFinal      : u32 = 0u;
+const InspectionDirect     : u32 = 1u;
+const InspectionDiffuse    : u32 = 2u;
+const InspectionIrradiance : u32 = 3u;
+const InspectionResampled  : u32 = 4u;
+const InspectionReflection : u32 = 5u;
+const InspectionDistance   : u32 = 6u;
+const InspectionCards      : u32 = 7u;
+const InspectionNormal     : u32 = 8u;
+const InspectionAlbedo     : u32 = 9u;
+const InspectionFresnel    : u32 = 10u;
+
+// 📝 Diffuse exitance: the Lambert radiance the surface gives off, ρ/π · E, with the sun, the fire and the lights, and the
+//    indirect irradiance the pixel itself shows (enclosure included), plus emission. The cards hold the same quantity, so a
+//    screen-trace hit and a card hit agree. Inspection modes never change it.
+fn ResolveDiffuseExitance(Pixel: vec2i, Depth: f32, Visibility: f32) -> vec3f
+{
+    if (Depth <= 0.0)
+    {
+        return vec3f(0.0);
+    }
+    let Attributes = textureLoad(SurfaceAttributes, Pixel, 0);
+    let Normal = DecodeOctahedral(Attributes.xy);
+    let Surface = ProjectSurfaceSample(Materials[u32(Attributes.z + 0.5)]);
+    let Position = ReconstructWorldPosition(vec2f(Pixel) + 0.5, Depth);
+    let Enclosure = mix(1.0, CabinIndirectShare, ResolveCabinShare((Occupants[0].WorldToLocal * vec4f(Position, 1.0)).xyz));
+    var Irradiance = Frame.SunIlluminance * Visibility * max(dot(Normal, Frame.SunDirection), 0.0);
+    Irradiance += textureLoad(DirectIrradiance, Pixel, 0).rgb;
+    if (FeatureEnabled(Frame, FeatureIndirect))
+    {
+        Irradiance += textureLoad(IndirectIrradiance, Pixel, 0).rgb * Frame.IndirectScale * Enclosure;
+    }
+    let Emission = (Surface.Emission + Surface.Albedo * max(Attributes.w - 1.0, 0.0)) * Frame.EmissionScale;
+    return ResolveDiffuseAlbedo(Surface) * InversePi * Irradiance + Emission;
+}
+
+@compute @workgroup_size(8, 8)
+fn ResolveRecombination(@builtin(global_invocation_id) Invocation: vec3u)
+{
+    let Pixel = vec2i(Invocation.xy);
+    if (any(vec2f(Pixel) >= Frame.ScreenExtent))
+    {
+        return;
+    }
+    let Direct = textureLoad(DirectRadiance, Pixel, 0);
+    let Depth = textureLoad(SurfaceDepth, Pixel, 0);
+    // 📝 Written only while the screen-trace master gate is on; enabling it restarts the temporal tallies for one frame.
+    if (ExtendedEnabled(Frame, ExtendedScreenTraversal))
+    {
+        textureStore(ExitanceTarget, Pixel, vec4f(ResolveDiffuseExitance(Pixel, Depth, Direct.w), 1.0));
+    }
+    if (Frame.InspectionMode == InspectionDistance)
+    {
+        textureStore(RecombinedTarget, Pixel, vec4f(textureLoad(InspectionRadiance, Pixel, 0).rgb, 1.0));
+        return;
+    }
+    if (Frame.InspectionMode == InspectionCards)
+    {
+        let Extent = vec2f(textureDimensions(CardFinal));
+        let Scale = min(Frame.ScreenExtent.x, Frame.ScreenExtent.y) / Extent.x;
+        let Texel = vec2i(vec2f(Pixel) / Scale);
+        var Colour = vec3f(0.04);
+        if (all(Texel < vec2i(Extent)))
+        {
+            Colour = textureLoad(CardFinal, Texel, 0).rgb;
+        }
+        textureStore(RecombinedTarget, Pixel, vec4f(Colour, 1.0));
+        return;
+    }
+    if (Depth <= 0.0)
+    {
+        textureStore(RecombinedTarget, Pixel, vec4f(CompositePlume(Direct.rgb, Pixel), 1.0));
+        return;
+    }
+    let Attributes = textureLoad(SurfaceAttributes, Pixel, 0);
+    let Normal = DecodeOctahedral(Attributes.xy);
+    let Surface = ProjectSurfaceSample(Materials[u32(Attributes.z + 0.5)]);
+    let Position = ReconstructWorldPosition(vec2f(Pixel) + 0.5, Depth);
+    let View = normalize(Frame.CameraPosition - Position);
+    let NdotV = max(dot(Normal, View), 1.0e-3);
+
+    // 📝 Inside the car's cabin: SDF volumes need 0.05 to counter self-hit, whereas the BVH tracer traces through real window openings.
+    let TargetCabinShare = select(CabinIndirectShare, 0.45, FeatureEnabled(Frame, FeatureRayTracing));
+    let Enclosure = mix(1.0, TargetCabinShare, ResolveCabinShare((Occupants[0].WorldToLocal * vec4f(Position, 1.0)).xyz));
+    var Irradiance = vec3f(0.0);
+    if (FeatureEnabled(Frame, FeatureIndirect))
+    {
+        Irradiance = textureLoad(IndirectIrradiance, Pixel, 0).rgb * Frame.IndirectScale * Enclosure;
+    }
+    let Diffuse = ResolveDiffuseAlbedo(Surface) * InversePi * Irradiance;
+
+    let GlossRoughness   = select(Surface.Roughness, Surface.CoatRoughness, Surface.CoatWeight > 0.0);
+    let Reflection       = textureLoad(ReflectionRadiance, Pixel, 0);
+    var Glossy           = Irradiance * InversePi;
+    let UseRtReflections = FeatureEnabled(Frame, FeatureRayTracing) && FeatureEnabled(Frame, FeatureRayTracedReflections);
+    let Cutoff           = select(0.50, ResolveReflectionRoughness(Frame), UseRtReflections);
+    let FadeStart        = max(0.05, Cutoff - 0.18);
+    if (FeatureEnabled(Frame, FeatureReflection))
+    {
+        let ReflScale = select(1.0, Frame.IndirectScale, FeatureEnabled(Frame, FeatureIndirect)) * ResolveReflectionScale(Frame);
+        Glossy = mix(Reflection.rgb * ReflScale * Enclosure, Glossy, smoothstep(FadeStart, Cutoff, GlossRoughness));
+    }
+    let LayerResponse = ResolveEnvironmentResponse(NdotV, Surface.Roughness);
+    let LayerGlossy = select(Glossy, mix(Glossy, Irradiance * InversePi, smoothstep(FadeStart - 0.05, Cutoff, Surface.Roughness)), Surface.CoatWeight > 0.0);
+    var Indirect = Diffuse + LayerGlossy * (ResolveSpecularColour(Surface) * LayerResponse.x + LayerResponse.y);
+    var Specular = LayerGlossy * (ResolveSpecularColour(Surface) * LayerResponse.x + LayerResponse.y);
+    if (Surface.CoatWeight > 0.0)
+    {
+        let CoatResponse = ResolveEnvironmentResponse(NdotV, Surface.CoatRoughness);
+        let CoatReflectance = (0.04 * CoatResponse.x + CoatResponse.y) * Surface.CoatWeight;
+        Indirect = Indirect * (1.0 - CoatReflectance) + Glossy * CoatReflectance;
+        Specular = Specular * (1.0 - CoatReflectance) + Glossy * CoatReflectance;
+    }
+    // 📝 Attributes.w carries 1 + glow: a derezzing car's cells and cubes glow in their own facet's colour.
+    let Emission = (Surface.Emission + Surface.Albedo * max(Attributes.w - 1.0, 0.0)) * Frame.EmissionScale;
+
+    var Colour = Direct.rgb + Indirect + Emission;
+    switch (Frame.InspectionMode)
+    {
+        case 1u: { Colour = Direct.rgb + Emission; }
+        case 2u: { Colour = Diffuse; }
+        case 3u: { Colour = Irradiance * InversePi; }
+        case 4u:
+        {
+            let TracePixel = min(Pixel / i32(Frame.TraceScale), vec2i(Frame.TraceExtent) - vec2i(1));
+            Colour = textureLoad(ResampledIrradiance, TracePixel, 0).rgb * InversePi;
+        }
+        case 5u: { Colour = Specular; }
+        case 8u: { Colour = Normal * 0.5 + 0.5; }
+        case 9u: { Colour = Surface.Albedo; }
+        // 📝 The environment reflectance per pixel: F0·A + B from the split-sum response, so Fresnel's rise toward grazing shows.
+        case 10u: { Colour = ResolveSpecularColour(Surface) * LayerResponse.x + vec3f(LayerResponse.y); }
+        default: { }
+    }
+    textureStore(RecombinedTarget, Pixel, vec4f(CompositePlume(Colour, Pixel), 1.0));
+}
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/DisplayRefraction.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/DisplayRefraction.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..48d9f49
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/DisplayRefraction.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,63 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                           DISPLAYREFRACTION.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 Refraction for transmissive dielectrics: the recombined radiance is copied out, and each refractive pixel adds the
+//    Fresnel-weighted light that lies behind it along Snell's bent direction. A screen-space approximation, not a ray trace.
+
+//! include "FrameDescriptor.wgsl"
+//! include "SurfaceReflectance.wgsl"
+//! include "PackingCodec.wgsl"
+
+@group(0) @binding(1) var<storage, read> Materials : array<MaterialRecord>;
+@group(0) @binding(2) var SurfaceAttributes        : texture_2d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(3) var SurfaceDepth             : texture_depth_2d;
+@group(0) @binding(4) var Backdrop                 : texture_2d<f32>;                  // the recombined radiance, copied before this pass
+@group(0) @binding(5) var RefractedTarget          : texture_storage_2d<rgba16float, write>;
+
+// 📐 Stand-in for the path a bent ray takes through a glass body, in metres: the screen-space offset is the projection of
+//    the point this far along the refracted direction. A ray through a sphere of radius R crosses about 2R; half that
+//    keeps the offset inside the object's own silhouette.
+const RefractionDepth : f32 = 0.5;
+
+fn ProjectRefractionPixel(Position: vec3f) -> vec2f
+{
+    let Clip = Frame.UnjitteredViewProjection * vec4f(Position, 1.0);
+    let Ndc = Clip.xy / max(Clip.w, 1.0e-4);
+    return vec2f(Ndc.x * 0.5 + 0.5, 0.5 - Ndc.y * 0.5) * Frame.ScreenExtent;
+}
+
+// 📝 Transmitted light is what lies behind the surface along Snell's refraction, weighted by the Fresnel transmittance. The
+//    opaque shading, including the Fresnel-weighted reflection, is already in the backdrop at this pixel and is kept. A
+//    body whose path leaves the screen, or that totally reflects, samples its own pixel.
+@compute @workgroup_size(8, 8, 1)
+fn ResolveRefraction(@builtin(global_invocation_id) Invocation: vec3u)
+{
+    let Pixel = vec2i(Invocation.xy);
+    if (any(vec2f(Pixel) >= Frame.ScreenExtent) || Frame.InspectionMode != 0u)
+    {
+        return;
+    }
+    let Depth = textureLoad(SurfaceDepth, Pixel, 0);
+    if (Depth <= 0.0)
+    {
+        return;
+    }
+    let Attributes = textureLoad(SurfaceAttributes, Pixel, 0);
+    let Material = Materials[u32(Attributes.z + 0.5)];
+    if (Material.IndexOfRefraction <= 1.0)
+    {
+        return;
+    }
+    let Normal = DecodeOctahedral(Attributes.xy);
+    let Position = ReconstructWorldPosition(vec2f(Pixel) + 0.5, Depth);
+    let View = normalize(Frame.CameraPosition - Position);
+    let NdotV = max(dot(Normal, View), 1.0e-3);
+    // 📐 Air to body: eta = n_air / n_body. refract() returns zero on total internal reflection; the offset is then zero.
+    let Bent = refract(-View, Normal, 1.0 / Material.IndexOfRefraction);
+    let Offset = ProjectRefractionPixel(Position + Bent * RefractionDepth) - ProjectRefractionPixel(Position);
+    let Sampled = clamp(vec2i(vec2f(Pixel) + Offset), vec2i(0), vec2i(Frame.ScreenExtent) - vec2i(1));
+    let Behind = textureLoad(Backdrop, Sampled, 0).rgb;
+    let Existing = textureLoad(Backdrop, Pixel, 0).rgb;
+    let Transmittance = (vec3f(1.0) - ResolveFresnel(vec3f(Material.SpecularLevel), NdotV)) * Material.Transmission;
+    textureStore(RefractedTarget, Pixel, vec4f(Existing + Transmittance * Behind, 1.0));
+}
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/DistanceRecords.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/DistanceRecords.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..becee03
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/DistanceRecords.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,61 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                           DISTANCERECORDS.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 Cascade records of the scene distance field, shared by the union pass that writes it and every pass that traverses it.
+
+struct ClipRecord
+{
+    OriginVoxel        : vec3i,   // [voxel] world voxel coordinate of the window's minimum corner
+    Resolution         : u32,     // [voxel] lattice edge
+    VoxelExtent        : f32,     // [m]
+    Band               : f32,     // [m]     truncation distance written by the union pass
+    InverseWorldExtent : f32,     // [1/m]   1 / (Resolution · VoxelExtent)
+    InverseVoxelExtent : f32,     // [1/m]   1 / VoxelExtent
+}
+
+struct DistanceRecord
+{
+    Clips                 : array<ClipRecord, 4>,
+    ClipCount             : u32,     // [-]
+    DistanceOccupantCount : u32,     // [-]  occupants [0, count) own distance volumes
+    GroundHeight          : f32,     // [m]  analytic course plane
+    HitFraction           : f32,     // [-]  surface threshold as a fraction of the voxel edge
+    BrickCount            : u32,     // [-]  bricks the union pass rewrites this frame
+    FrameIndex            : u32,     // [-]  stamped into every rewritten brick
+    BricksPerAxis         : u32,     // [-]  Resolution / BrickEdge
+    CeilingHeight         : f32,     // [m]  sky-escape ceiling above all distance occupants
+}
+
+const BrickEdge      : u32 = 8u;
+const SkyIdentity    : u32 = 2045u;
+const GroundIdentity : u32 = 2046u;
+const VacantIdentity : u32 = 2047u;
+
+// 📝 Toroidal brick slot of a world brick in one cascade — the same wrap the voxels use, so an epoch follows its brick.
+fn ResolveBrickSlot(Level: u32, WorldBrick: vec3i, BricksPerAxis: u32) -> u32
+{
+    let Edge = i32(BricksPerAxis);
+    let Wrapped = vec3u(((WorldBrick % Edge) + Edge) % Edge);
+    return Level * BricksPerAxis * BricksPerAxis * BricksPerAxis + (Wrapped.z * BricksPerAxis + Wrapped.y) * BricksPerAxis + Wrapped.x;
+}
+
+// 📝 A brick epoch is the frame of its last rewrite in the low 31 bits; bit 31 records that a moving occupant caused
+//    it, as opposed to the cascade window scrolling over it. The inspection views glow the two causes differently.
+const OccupantEpochBit : u32 = 0x80000000u;
+const VacantEpoch      : u32 = 0xFFFFFFFFu;
+
+fn ConstructBrickEpoch(FrameIndex: u32, OccupantCaused: bool) -> u32
+{
+    return (FrameIndex & 0x7FFFFFFFu) | select(0u, OccupantEpochBit, OccupantCaused);
+}
+
+// 📝 Returns (frames since the rewrite, 1 when a moving occupant caused it); a never-written brick is infinitely old.
+fn ResolveBrickAge(Epoch: u32, FrameIndex: u32) -> vec2f
+{
+    if (Epoch == VacantEpoch)
+    {
+        return vec2f(1.0e9, 0.0);
+    }
+    let Written = Epoch & 0x7FFFFFFFu;
+    return vec2f(f32((FrameIndex & 0x7FFFFFFFu) - Written), select(0.0, 1.0, (Epoch & OccupantEpochBit) != 0u));
+}
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/DistanceTransfer.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/DistanceTransfer.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a7c3ddb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/DistanceTransfer.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,280 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                          DISTANCETRANSFER.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 Transfers one facet set into its signed distance volume — closest-facet distance, sign from back-facing ray hits.
+
+// 📝 The per-occupant volume is the analogue of a mesh distance field: built once, in the facet set's own frame, and
+//    only ever SAMPLED by the union pass that assembles the one scene distance field. No tracer reads it directly.
+//
+//    ① unsigned distance: closest point on any facet, by a pruned traversal of the bounding structure;
+//    ② sign: RayCount rays in a spherical Fibonacci set, randomly rotated per voxel; the voxel is inside when more
+//       than a quarter of all rays first strike a back face. That is the heuristic that survives open and
+//       non-manifold input — the ControlVehicle body has 124 open and 76 non-manifold edges — where parity cannot.
+
+struct TransferRecord
+{
+    VolumeMinimum : vec3f,   // [m]     local corner of texel (0,0,0)
+    VoxelExtent   : f32,     // [m]
+    TexelOrigin   : vec3u,   // [texel] placement inside the volume space
+    NodeCount     : u32,     // [-]
+    TexelExtent   : vec3u,   // [texel] resolution
+    FacetCount    : u32,     // [-]
+    SlabOrigin    : u32,     // [texel] first z slice of this submission
+    SlabExtent    : u32,     // [texel] z slices in this submission
+    RayCount      : u32,     // [-]
+    Pad           : u32,
+}
+
+struct BoundingNode
+{
+    Minimum     : vec3f,
+    LeftOrFirst : u32,
+    Maximum     : vec3f,
+    Count       : u32,
+}
+
+@group(0) @binding(0) var<uniform> Transfer           : TransferRecord;
+@group(0) @binding(1) var<storage, read> Nodes        : array<BoundingNode>;
+@group(0) @binding(2) var<storage, read> FacetCorners : array<vec4f>;
+@group(0) @binding(3) var VolumeSpace                 : texture_storage_3d<rgba16float, write>;
+
+const TraversalDepth : u32 = 40u;
+
+// 📐 Closest point on a triangle by Voronoi-region classification (Ericson, Real-Time Collision Detection §5.1.5).
+fn ProjectClosestOnFacet(Point: vec3f, A: vec3f, B: vec3f, C: vec3f) -> vec3f
+{
+    let AB = B - A;
+    let AC = C - A;
+    let AP = Point - A;
+    let D1 = dot(AB, AP);
+    let D2 = dot(AC, AP);
+    if (D1 <= 0.0 && D2 <= 0.0) { return A; }
+    let BP = Point - B;
+    let D3 = dot(AB, BP);
+    let D4 = dot(AC, BP);
+    if (D3 >= 0.0 && D4 <= D3) { return B; }
+    let VC = D1 * D4 - D3 * D2;
+    if (VC <= 0.0 && D1 >= 0.0 && D3 <= 0.0) { return A + AB * (D1 / (D1 - D3)); }
+    let CP = Point - C;
+    let D5 = dot(AB, CP);
+    let D6 = dot(AC, CP);
+    if (D6 >= 0.0 && D5 <= D6) { return C; }
+    let VB = D5 * D2 - D1 * D6;
+    if (VB <= 0.0 && D2 >= 0.0 && D6 <= 0.0) { return A + AC * (D2 / (D2 - D6)); }
+    let VA = D3 * D6 - D5 * D4;
+    if (VA <= 0.0 && (D4 - D3) >= 0.0 && (D5 - D6) >= 0.0)
+    {
+        return B + (C - B) * ((D4 - D3) / ((D4 - D3) + (D5 - D6)));
+    }
+    let Reciprocal = 1.0 / (VA + VB + VC);
+    return A + AB * (VB * Reciprocal) + AC * (VC * Reciprocal);
+}
+
+fn ResolveBoundsDistanceSquared(Point: vec3f, Minimum: vec3f, Maximum: vec3f) -> f32
+{
+    let Outside = max(max(Minimum - Point, Point - Maximum), vec3f(0.0));
+    return dot(Outside, Outside);
+}
+
+// 📐 Slab test; returns the entry distance or a large value when the ray misses the box before Limit.
+fn IntersectBounds(Origin: vec3f, Reciprocal: vec3f, Minimum: vec3f, Maximum: vec3f, Limit: f32) -> f32
+{
+    let Near = (Minimum - Origin) * Reciprocal;
+    let Far  = (Maximum - Origin) * Reciprocal;
+    let Entry = max(max(min(Near.x, Far.x), min(Near.y, Far.y)), max(min(Near.z, Far.z), 0.0));
+    let Exit  = min(min(max(Near.x, Far.x), max(Near.y, Far.y)), min(max(Near.z, Far.z), Limit));
+    return select(1.0e30, Entry, Entry <= Exit);
+}
+
+//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+//                                                 CLOSEST-FACET QUERY
+//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+fn ResolveClosestDistanceSquared(Point: vec3f) -> f32
+{
+    var Best = 1.0e30;
+    var Stack: array<u32, 40>;
+    var Depth = 1u;
+    Stack[0] = 0u;
+    while (Depth > 0u)
+    {
+        Depth--;
+        let Node = Nodes[Stack[Depth]];
+        if (ResolveBoundsDistanceSquared(Point, Node.Minimum, Node.Maximum) >= Best)
+        {
+            continue;
+        }
+        if (Node.Count > 0u)
+        {
+            for (var Facet = Node.LeftOrFirst; Facet < Node.LeftOrFirst + Node.Count; Facet++)
+            {
+                let A = FacetCorners[Facet * 3u].xyz;
+                let B = FacetCorners[Facet * 3u + 1u].xyz;
+                let C = FacetCorners[Facet * 3u + 2u].xyz;
+                let Offset = Point - ProjectClosestOnFacet(Point, A, B, C);
+                Best = min(Best, dot(Offset, Offset));
+            }
+            continue;
+        }
+        let Left  = Nodes[Node.LeftOrFirst];
+        let Right = Nodes[Node.LeftOrFirst + 1u];
+        let LeftDistance  = ResolveBoundsDistanceSquared(Point, Left.Minimum, Left.Maximum);
+        let RightDistance = ResolveBoundsDistanceSquared(Point, Right.Minimum, Right.Maximum);
+        if (Depth + 2u > TraversalDepth)
+        {
+            continue;
+        }
+        // 📝 The nearer child is pushed last so it is visited first and tightens Best before the farther one.
+        if (LeftDistance < RightDistance)
+        {
+            Stack[Depth] = Node.LeftOrFirst + 1u;
+            Stack[Depth + 1u] = Node.LeftOrFirst;
+        }
+        else
+        {
+            Stack[Depth] = Node.LeftOrFirst;
+            Stack[Depth + 1u] = Node.LeftOrFirst + 1u;
+        }
+        Depth += 2u;
+    }
+    return Best;
+}
+
+//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+//                                                FIRST-HIT FACING QUERY
+//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+// 📝 Returns +1 when the first hit is a front face, −1 for a back face, 0 for a miss.
+fn ResolveFirstHitFacing(Origin: vec3f, Direction: vec3f) -> f32
+{
+    let Reciprocal = 1.0 / select(Direction, vec3f(1.0e-9), abs(Direction) < vec3f(1.0e-9));
+    var Nearest = 1.0e30;
+    var Facing  = 0.0;
+    var Stack: array<u32, 40>;
+    var Depth = 1u;
+    Stack[0] = 0u;
+    while (Depth > 0u)
+    {
+        Depth--;
+        let Node = Nodes[Stack[Depth]];
+        if (IntersectBounds(Origin, Reciprocal, Node.Minimum, Node.Maximum, Nearest) >= Nearest)
+        {
+            continue;
+        }
+        if (Node.Count > 0u)
+        {
+            for (var Facet = Node.LeftOrFirst; Facet < Node.LeftOrFirst + Node.Count; Facet++)
+            {
+                let A  = FacetCorners[Facet * 3u].xyz;
+                let E1 = FacetCorners[Facet * 3u + 1u].xyz - A;
+                let E2 = FacetCorners[Facet * 3u + 2u].xyz - A;
+                // 📐 Möller–Trumbore, two-sided; det = −dot(direction, e₁×e₂), positive for a front-face hit.
+                let P = cross(Direction, E2);
+                let Determinant = dot(E1, P);
+                if (abs(Determinant) < 1.0e-12)
+                {
+                    continue;
+                }
+                let Inverse = 1.0 / Determinant;
+                let T = Origin - A;
+                let U = dot(T, P) * Inverse;
+                if (U < 0.0 || U > 1.0)
+                {
+                    continue;
+                }
+                let Q = cross(T, E1);
+                let V = dot(Direction, Q) * Inverse;
+                if (V < 0.0 || U + V > 1.0)
+                {
+                    continue;
+                }
+                let Travel = dot(E2, Q) * Inverse;
+                if (Travel > 1.0e-5 && Travel < Nearest)
+                {
+                    Nearest = Travel;
+                    Facing  = select(-1.0, 1.0, Determinant > 0.0);
+                }
+            }
+            continue;
+        }
+        if (Depth + 2u > TraversalDepth)
+        {
+            continue;
+        }
+        let LeftEntry  = IntersectBounds(Origin, Reciprocal, Nodes[Node.LeftOrFirst].Minimum, Nodes[Node.LeftOrFirst].Maximum, Nearest);
+        let RightEntry = IntersectBounds(Origin, Reciprocal, Nodes[Node.LeftOrFirst + 1u].Minimum, Nodes[Node.LeftOrFirst + 1u].Maximum, Nearest);
+        if (LeftEntry < RightEntry)
+        {
+            Stack[Depth] = Node.LeftOrFirst + 1u;
+            Stack[Depth + 1u] = Node.LeftOrFirst;
+        }
+        else
+        {
+            Stack[Depth] = Node.LeftOrFirst;
+            Stack[Depth + 1u] = Node.LeftOrFirst + 1u;
+        }
+        Depth += 2u;
+    }
+    return Facing;
+}
+
+//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+//                                                    TRANSFER ENTRY
+//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+fn PermuteTransfer(Input: u32) -> u32
+{
+    let Advanced = Input * 747796405u + 2891336453u;
+    let Word = ((Advanced >> ((Advanced >> 28u) + 4u)) ^ Advanced) * 277803737u;
+    return (Word >> 22u) ^ Word;
+}
+
+// 📐 Spherical Fibonacci point i of n: z = 1 − (2i + 1)/n, φ = 2π·i·(1 − 1/golden), uniform over the sphere.
+fn ProjectSphericalFibonacci(Index: u32, Count: u32) -> vec3f
+{
+    let z = 1.0 - (2.0 * f32(Index) + 1.0) / f32(Count);
+    let Radius = sqrt(max(0.0, 1.0 - z * z));
+    let φ = 2.399963229728653 * f32(Index);
+    return vec3f(Radius * cos(φ), Radius * sin(φ), z);
+}
+
+@compute @workgroup_size(4, 4, 4)
+fn TransferDistance(@builtin(global_invocation_id) Invocation: vec3u)
+{
+    let Voxel = vec3u(Invocation.x, Invocation.y, Invocation.z + Transfer.SlabOrigin);
+    if (Voxel.x >= Transfer.TexelExtent.x || Voxel.y >= Transfer.TexelExtent.y || Voxel.z >= Transfer.TexelExtent.z
+        || Invocation.z >= Transfer.SlabExtent)
+    {
+        return;
+    }
+    let Point = Transfer.VolumeMinimum + (vec3f(Voxel) + 0.5) * Transfer.VoxelExtent;
+    let Unsigned = sqrt(ResolveClosestDistanceSquared(Point));
+
+    // 📝 A random rotation per voxel about a random axis keeps the ray set from imprinting a lattice on the sign.
+    var Seed = PermuteTransfer((Voxel.x * 73856093u) ^ (Voxel.y * 19349663u) ^ (Voxel.z * 83492791u));
+    Seed = PermuteTransfer(Seed);
+    let Angle = f32(Seed >> 8u) * (6.283185307 / 16777216.0);
+    Seed = PermuteTransfer(Seed);
+    let AxisZ = f32(Seed >> 8u) * (2.0 / 16777216.0) - 1.0;
+    Seed = PermuteTransfer(Seed);
+    let AxisAngle = f32(Seed >> 8u) * (6.283185307 / 16777216.0);
+    let AxisRadius = sqrt(max(0.0, 1.0 - AxisZ * AxisZ));
+    let Axis = vec3f(AxisRadius * cos(AxisAngle), AxisRadius * sin(AxisAngle), AxisZ);
+    let Cosine = cos(Angle);
+    let Sine = sin(Angle);
+
+    var BackHits = 0u;
+    for (var Ray = 0u; Ray < Transfer.RayCount; Ray++)
+    {
+        let Fibonacci = ProjectSphericalFibonacci(Ray, Transfer.RayCount);
+        // 📐 Rodrigues rotation of the Fibonacci direction about Axis by Angle.
+        let Direction = Fibonacci * Cosine + cross(Axis, Fibonacci) * Sine + Axis * dot(Axis, Fibonacci) * (1.0 - Cosine);
+        if (ResolveFirstHitFacing(Point, Direction) < 0.0)
+        {
+            BackHits++;
+        }
+    }
+    let Inside = f32(BackHits) > 0.25 * f32(Transfer.RayCount);
+    let Signed = select(Unsigned, -Unsigned, Inside);
+    textureStore(VolumeSpace, vec3i(Transfer.TexelOrigin + Voxel), vec4f(Signed, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0));
+}
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/DistanceTraversal.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/DistanceTraversal.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..660e49b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/DistanceTraversal.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,376 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                          DISTANCETRAVERSAL.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 Sphere traversal of the ONE scene distance field — four nested toroidal cascades, never a walk over occupants.
+
+// 📝 Group 1 is the scene distance field and nothing else. Every ray in the exhibit — indirect candidates, reuse
+//    visibility, card shadows, card radiosity, reflections, the inspection march — is answered by this file.
+//
+//    A cascade is a Resolution³ lattice of rgba16float texels addressed toroidally: world voxel v lives at texel
+//    v mod Resolution, so the window scrolls with the camera by rewriting only the slabs it newly covers. Because the
+//    sampler repeats, uvw = position / (Resolution · VoxelExtent) lands on the right texel with no indirection.
+//    Texel .x is the truncated signed distance [m]; .y is the identity of the occupant nearest the voxel centre.
+
+//! include "DistanceRecords.wgsl"
+
+@group(1) @binding(0) var<uniform> Distance : DistanceRecord;
+@group(1) @binding(1) var SceneClip0        : texture_3d<f32>;
+@group(1) @binding(2) var SceneClip1        : texture_3d<f32>;
+@group(1) @binding(3) var SceneClip2        : texture_3d<f32>;
+@group(1) @binding(4) var SceneClip3        : texture_3d<f32>;
+@group(1) @binding(5) var SceneSampler      : sampler;
+@group(1) @binding(6) var<storage, read> BrickEpochs : array<u32>;
+
+//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+//                                                  CASCADE ADDRESSING
+//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+fn SampleClipTexel(Level: u32, Uvw: vec3f) -> vec4f
+{
+    switch (Level)
+    {
+        case 0u:      { return textureSampleLevel(SceneClip0, SceneSampler, Uvw, 0.0); }
+        case 1u:      { return textureSampleLevel(SceneClip1, SceneSampler, Uvw, 0.0); }
+        case 2u:      { return textureSampleLevel(SceneClip2, SceneSampler, Uvw, 0.0); }
+        default:      { return textureSampleLevel(SceneClip3, SceneSampler, Uvw, 0.0); }
+    }
+}
+
+fn LoadClipTexel(Level: u32, Texel: vec3i) -> vec4f
+{
+    switch (Level)
+    {
+        case 0u:      { return textureLoad(SceneClip0, Texel, 0); }
+        case 1u:      { return textureLoad(SceneClip1, Texel, 0); }
+        case 2u:      { return textureLoad(SceneClip2, Texel, 0); }
+        default:      { return textureLoad(SceneClip3, Texel, 0); }
+    }
+}
+
+fn ClipContains(Level: u32, Position: vec3f, MarginVoxels: f32) -> bool
+{
+    let Clip  = Distance.Clips[Level];
+    let Voxel = Position * Clip.InverseVoxelExtent;
+    let Low   = vec3f(Clip.OriginVoxel) + vec3f(MarginVoxels);
+    let High  = vec3f(Clip.OriginVoxel) + vec3f(f32(Clip.Resolution) - MarginVoxels);
+    return all(Voxel >= Low) && all(Voxel <= High);
+}
+
+// 📝 True once a ray at Position travelling along Direction has crossed the far slab of Clip[Level] and can never
+//    re-enter that convex cascade window at any larger ray parameter.
+fn ClipExitedAlongRay(Level: u32, Position: vec3f, Direction: vec3f, MarginVoxels: f32) -> bool
+{
+    let Clip  = Distance.Clips[Level];
+    let Voxel = Position * Clip.InverseVoxelExtent;
+    let Low   = vec3f(Clip.OriginVoxel) + vec3f(MarginVoxels);
+    let High  = vec3f(Clip.OriginVoxel) + vec3f(f32(Clip.Resolution) - MarginVoxels);
+    return (Voxel.x > High.x && Direction.x >= 0.0) || (Voxel.x < Low.x && Direction.x <= 0.0)
+        || (Voxel.y > High.y && Direction.y >= 0.0) || (Voxel.y < Low.y && Direction.y <= 0.0)
+        || (Voxel.z > High.z && Direction.z >= 0.0) || (Voxel.z < Low.z && Direction.z <= 0.0);
+}
+
+fn ResolveFinestClip(Position: vec3f, MarginVoxels: f32) -> u32
+{
+    for (var Level = 0u; Level < Distance.ClipCount; Level++)
+    {
+        if (ClipContains(Level, Position, MarginVoxels))
+        {
+            return Level;
+        }
+    }
+    return Distance.ClipCount;
+}
+
+fn ResolveRayClip(Position: vec3f, Direction: vec3f, MarginVoxels: f32, StartLevel: ptr<function, u32>) -> u32
+{
+    var Begin = *StartLevel;
+    while (Begin < Distance.ClipCount && ClipExitedAlongRay(Begin, Position, Direction, MarginVoxels))
+    {
+        Begin++;
+    }
+    *StartLevel = Begin;
+    for (var Level = Begin; Level < Distance.ClipCount; Level++)
+    {
+        if (ClipContains(Level, Position, MarginVoxels))
+        {
+            return Level;
+        }
+    }
+    return Distance.ClipCount;
+}
+
+fn SampleClipDistance(Level: u32, Position: vec3f) -> f32
+{
+    return SampleClipTexel(Level, Position * Distance.Clips[Level].InverseWorldExtent).x;
+}
+
+fn ResolveClipIdentity(Level: u32, Position: vec3f) -> u32
+{
+    let Clip       = Distance.Clips[Level];
+    let Voxel      = vec3i(floor(Position * Clip.InverseVoxelExtent));
+    let Resolution = i32(Clip.Resolution);
+    let Texel      = ((Voxel % Resolution) + Resolution) % Resolution;
+    return u32(LoadClipTexel(Level, Texel).y + 0.5);
+}
+
+// 📐 Central-difference gradient over ±¾ voxel; the field is a distance, so its gradient is the surface normal.
+fn ResolveClipNormal(Level: u32, Position: vec3f) -> vec3f
+{
+    let Step = Distance.Clips[Level].VoxelExtent * 0.75;
+    let Gradient = vec3f(SampleClipDistance(Level, Position + vec3f(Step, 0.0, 0.0)) - SampleClipDistance(Level, Position - vec3f(Step, 0.0, 0.0)),
+                         SampleClipDistance(Level, Position + vec3f(0.0, Step, 0.0)) - SampleClipDistance(Level, Position - vec3f(0.0, Step, 0.0)),
+                         SampleClipDistance(Level, Position + vec3f(0.0, 0.0, Step)) - SampleClipDistance(Level, Position - vec3f(0.0, 0.0, Step)));
+    let Length = length(Gradient);
+    return select(vec3f(0.0, 0.0, 1.0), Gradient / Length, Length > 1.0e-6);
+}
+
+// 📝 Distance at a point from the finest cascade holding it; the analytic plane answers outside every cascade.
+fn SampleSceneDistance(Position: vec3f) -> vec2f
+{
+    let Level = ResolveFinestClip(Position, 1.0);
+    if (Level >= Distance.ClipCount)
+    {
+        return vec2f(Position.z - Distance.GroundHeight, f32(Distance.ClipCount));
+    }
+    return vec2f(SampleClipDistance(Level, Position), f32(Level));
+}
+
+// 📝 Normal-and-stride bias that lifts a ray origin off the surface it leaves, scaled by the cascade there.
+fn ResolveSurfaceBias(Position: vec3f) -> f32
+{
+    let Level = min(ResolveFinestClip(Position, 2.0), Distance.ClipCount - 1u);
+    return Distance.Clips[Level].VoxelExtent;
+}
+
+//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+//                                                   SPHERE TRAVERSAL
+//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+struct TraversalHit
+{
+    Position : vec3f,   // [m]
+    Travel   : f32,     // [m]   ray parameter at the surface
+    Normal   : vec3f,   // [-]   distance gradient
+    Identity : u32,     // [-]   occupant, GroundIdentity, or SkyIdentity on a miss
+    Level    : u32,     // [-]   cascade that answered; ClipCount for the far-field plane
+    Steps    : u32,     // [-]
+    Hit      : bool,
+}
+
+// 📝 ① sample the finest cascade holding the point; ② a saturated sample (no surface within that cascade's band)
+//    asks the next coarser cascade, whose band is twice as long, for a longer conservative stride; ③ the surface is
+//    declared within a voxel fraction, widened along the ray by an optional cone; ④ past the outermost cascade the
+//    analytic course plane is the far field. A traversal that exhausts its steps reports a hit rather than leaking.
+fn TraverseSceneDistance(Origin: vec3f, Direction: vec3f, MinimumTravel: f32, MaximumTravel: f32, ConeSlope: f32) -> TraversalHit
+{
+    var Result: TraversalHit;
+    Result.Hit      = false;
+    Result.Identity = SkyIdentity;
+    Result.Level    = Distance.ClipCount;
+    Result.Steps    = 0u;
+    Result.Normal   = -Direction;
+    Result.Travel   = MaximumTravel;
+    Result.Position = Origin + Direction * MaximumTravel;
+
+    var Travel     = MinimumTravel;
+    var StartLevel = 0u;
+    var Escaped    = false;
+    var Exhausted  = true;
+    for (var Step = 0u; Step < MaximumTraversalSteps; Step++)
+    {
+        let Position = Origin + Direction * Travel;
+        if (Position.z > Distance.CeilingHeight && Direction.z >= 0.0)
+        {
+            Escaped = true;
+            Exhausted = false;
+            break;
+        }
+        let Level = ResolveRayClip(Position, Direction, 2.0, &StartLevel);
+        if (Level >= Distance.ClipCount)
+        {
+            Escaped = true;
+            Exhausted = false;
+            break;
+        }
+        let Clip = Distance.Clips[Level];
+        var Sampled = SampleClipDistance(Level, Position);
+        var Saturation = Clip.Band * 0.9;
+        var Coarser = Level + 1u;
+        while (Sampled >= Saturation && Coarser < Distance.ClipCount)
+        {
+            if (!ClipContains(Coarser, Position, 2.0))
+            {
+                break;
+            }
+            let CoarseClip = Distance.Clips[Coarser];
+            Sampled = max(Sampled, SampleClipDistance(Coarser, Position) - 0.5 * CoarseClip.VoxelExtent);
+            Saturation = CoarseClip.Band * 0.9;
+            Coarser++;
+        }
+        Result.Steps = Step + 1u;
+        let Threshold = max(Clip.VoxelExtent * Distance.HitFraction, Travel * ConeSlope);
+        if (Sampled < Threshold)
+        {
+            Result.Hit      = true;
+            Result.Travel   = Travel;
+            Result.Position = Position;
+            Result.Level    = Level;
+            Exhausted = false;
+            break;
+        }
+        Travel += max(Sampled, Clip.VoxelExtent * 0.125);
+        if (Travel > MaximumTravel)
+        {
+            Exhausted = false;
+            break;
+        }
+    }
+
+    if (Result.Hit)
+    {
+        Result.Normal   = ResolveClipNormal(Result.Level, Result.Position);
+        let Inward      = Result.Position - Result.Normal * (0.5 * Distance.Clips[Result.Level].VoxelExtent);
+        Result.Identity = ResolveClipIdentity(Result.Level, Inward);
+        return Result;
+    }
+    if (Exhausted)
+    {
+        let Position = Origin + Direction * Travel;
+        let Level = min(ResolveFinestClip(Position, 2.0), Distance.ClipCount - 1u);
+        Result.Hit      = true;
+        Result.Travel   = Travel;
+        Result.Position = Position;
+        Result.Level    = Level;
+        Result.Normal   = ResolveClipNormal(Level, Position);
+        Result.Identity = ResolveClipIdentity(Level, Position);
+        return Result;
+    }
+    if (Escaped && Direction.z < -1.0e-4)
+    {
+        let GroundTravel = (Distance.GroundHeight - Origin.z) / Direction.z;
+        if (GroundTravel >= MinimumTravel && GroundTravel <= MaximumTravel)
+        {
+            Result.Hit      = true;
+            Result.Travel   = GroundTravel;
+            Result.Position = Origin + Direction * GroundTravel;
+            Result.Normal   = vec3f(0.0, 0.0, 1.0);
+            Result.Identity = GroundIdentity;
+            Result.Level    = Distance.ClipCount;
+        }
+    }
+    return Result;
+}
+
+// 📝 Binary visibility along a segment, for reuse validation: 1 when nothing intervenes before MaximumTravel.
+//    Dedicated march: omits surface-gradient (6× 3D samples) and identity loads, escapes immediately above the scene
+//    ceiling, and tests analytic ground occlusion directly.
+fn TraverseSceneVisibility(Origin: vec3f, Direction: vec3f, MinimumTravel: f32, MaximumTravel: f32) -> f32
+{
+    if (MaximumTravel <= MinimumTravel)
+    {
+        return 1.0;
+    }
+    var SegmentLimit = MaximumTravel;
+    if (Direction.z < -1.0e-4)
+    {
+        let GroundTravel = (Distance.GroundHeight - Origin.z) / Direction.z;
+        if (GroundTravel >= MinimumTravel && GroundTravel < MaximumTravel)
+        {
+            return 0.0;
+        }
+    }
+    var Travel     = MinimumTravel;
+    var StartLevel = 0u;
+    let StepLimit  = min(MaximumTraversalSteps, 56u);
+    for (var Step = 0u; Step < StepLimit; Step++)
+    {
+        let Position = Origin + Direction * Travel;
+        if (Position.z > Distance.CeilingHeight && Direction.z >= 0.0)
+        {
+            return 1.0;
+        }
+        let Level = ResolveRayClip(Position, Direction, 2.0, &StartLevel);
+        if (Level >= Distance.ClipCount)
+        {
+            return 1.0;
+        }
+        let Clip = Distance.Clips[Level];
+        var Sampled = SampleClipDistance(Level, Position);
+        var Saturation = Clip.Band * 0.9;
+        var Coarser = Level + 1u;
+        while (Sampled >= Saturation && Coarser < Distance.ClipCount)
+        {
+            if (!ClipContains(Coarser, Position, 2.0))
+            {
+                break;
+            }
+            let CoarseClip = Distance.Clips[Coarser];
+            Sampled = max(Sampled, SampleClipDistance(Coarser, Position) - 0.5 * CoarseClip.VoxelExtent);
+            Saturation = CoarseClip.Band * 0.9;
+            Coarser++;
+        }
+        let Threshold = max(Clip.VoxelExtent * Distance.HitFraction, Travel * 0.006);
+        if (Sampled < Threshold)
+        {
+            return 0.0;
+        }
+        Travel += max(Sampled, Clip.VoxelExtent * 0.125);
+        if (Travel >= SegmentLimit)
+        {
+            return 1.0;
+        }
+    }
+    return 0.0;
+}
+
+// 📐 Penumbra-estimating visibility toward a distant light: min over the march of k·d/t (Quílez), clamped to [0, 1].
+//    Used for card shadows, where a soft cascade-resolution penumbra is the honest answer.
+fn TraverseSceneShadow(Origin: vec3f, Direction: vec3f, MinimumTravel: f32, MaximumTravel: f32, Hardness: f32) -> f32
+{
+    var Travel     = MinimumTravel;
+    var StartLevel = 0u;
+    var Visibility = 1.0;
+    for (var Step = 0u; Step < MaximumTraversalSteps; Step++)
+    {
+        let Position = Origin + Direction * Travel;
+        if (Position.z > Distance.CeilingHeight && Direction.z >= 0.0)
+        {
+            return clamp(Visibility, 0.0, 1.0);
+        }
+        let Level = ResolveRayClip(Position, Direction, 2.0, &StartLevel);
+        if (Level >= Distance.ClipCount)
+        {
+            if (Direction.z < -1.0e-4)
+            {
+                return 0.0;
+            }
+            return Visibility;
+        }
+        let Clip = Distance.Clips[Level];
+        var Sampled = SampleClipDistance(Level, Position);
+        var Saturation = Clip.Band * 0.9;
+        var Coarser = Level + 1u;
+        while (Sampled >= Saturation && Coarser < Distance.ClipCount)
+        {
+            if (!ClipContains(Coarser, Position, 2.0))
+            {
+                break;
+            }
+            let CoarseClip = Distance.Clips[Coarser];
+            Sampled = max(Sampled, SampleClipDistance(Coarser, Position) - 0.5 * CoarseClip.VoxelExtent);
+            Saturation = CoarseClip.Band * 0.9;
+            Coarser++;
+        }
+        if (Sampled < Clip.VoxelExtent * Distance.HitFraction)
+        {
+            return 0.0;
+        }
+        Visibility = min(Visibility, Hardness * Sampled / max(Travel, 1.0e-3));
+        Travel += max(Sampled, Clip.VoxelExtent * 0.125);
+        if (Travel > MaximumTravel)
+        {
+            break;
+        }
+    }
+    return clamp(Visibility, 0.0, 1.0);
+}
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/DistanceUnion.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/DistanceUnion.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3902a2a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/DistanceUnion.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,146 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                            DISTANCEUNION.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 Rewrites the scene distance field brick by brick: min over the culled occupant volumes and the analytic course plane.
+
+// 📝 This is the ONLY place that walks occupants, and it does so per invalidated 8³ brick, never per ray. A brick is
+//    invalidated when the cascade window scrolls over it or when a moving occupant's old or new bounds, grown by the
+//    cascade band, overlap it. Everything downstream traverses the assembled field alone.
+//
+//    The active list (every enabled distance occupant, rebuilt on the host when activity changes) is walked in pages
+//    of 64: each lane tests one occupant's bounds, the survivors' volume records
+//    are staged in workgroup memory, and every lane then folds the page into the eight voxels it owns. A page can
+//    never overflow, so a brick under any number of occupants (a dense stress field, say) is still exact, and each
+//    surviving record is read from device memory once per brick instead of once per voxel.
+
+//! include "SceneRecords.wgsl"
+//! include "DistanceRecords.wgsl"
+
+@group(0) @binding(0) var<uniform> Distance          : DistanceRecord;
+@group(0) @binding(1) var<storage, read> Bricks      : array<vec4i>;
+@group(0) @binding(2) var<storage, read> Occupants   : array<OccupantRecord>;
+@group(0) @binding(3) var VolumeSpace                : texture_3d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(4) var VolumeSampler              : sampler;
+@group(0) @binding(5) var TargetClip0                : texture_storage_3d<rgba16float, write>;
+@group(0) @binding(6) var TargetClip1                : texture_storage_3d<rgba16float, write>;
+@group(0) @binding(7) var TargetClip2                : texture_storage_3d<rgba16float, write>;
+@group(0) @binding(8) var TargetClip3                : texture_storage_3d<rgba16float, write>;
+@group(0) @binding(9) var<storage, read_write> BrickEpochs : array<u32>;
+@group(0) @binding(10) var<storage, read> DistanceList : array<u32>;   // occupant indices; Distance.DistanceOccupantCount long
+
+const PageSize : u32 = 64u;   // [-] - occupants tested per page, one per lane
+
+var<workgroup> PageCount    : atomic<u32>;
+var<workgroup> PageIdentity : array<u32, 64>;
+var<workgroup> PageInverse  : array<mat4x4f, 64>;   // WorldToLocal
+var<workgroup> PageVolume   : array<vec4f, 64>;     // xyz VolumeMinimum [m], w VoxelExtent [m]
+var<workgroup> PageTexel    : array<vec4f, 64>;     // xyz VolumeTexelOrigin [texel]
+var<workgroup> PageExtent   : array<vec4f, 64>;     // xyz VolumeTexelExtent [texel]
+
+fn WriteClipTexel(Level: u32, Texel: vec3i, Texel4: vec4f)
+{
+    switch (Level)
+    {
+        case 0u:      { textureStore(TargetClip0, Texel, Texel4); }
+        case 1u:      { textureStore(TargetClip1, Texel, Texel4); }
+        case 2u:      { textureStore(TargetClip2, Texel, Texel4); }
+        default:      { textureStore(TargetClip3, Texel, Texel4); }
+    }
+}
+
+// 📐 Inside its volume an occupant answers with its transferred distance; outside, with the distance to the volume
+//    plus the distance stored at the nearest volume point — the extension the union needs for its band.
+fn SamplePageDistance(Slot: u32, Position: vec3f, InverseSpace: vec3f) -> f32
+{
+    let Local   = (PageInverse[Slot] * vec4f(Position, 1.0)).xyz;
+    let Volume  = PageVolume[Slot];
+    let Lowest  = Volume.xyz + vec3f(0.5 * Volume.w);
+    let Highest = Volume.xyz + (PageExtent[Slot].xyz - vec3f(0.5)) * Volume.w;
+    let Clamped = clamp(Local, Lowest, Highest);
+    let Outside = length(Local - Clamped);
+    let Texel   = PageTexel[Slot].xyz + (Clamped - Volume.xyz) / Volume.w;
+    return textureSampleLevel(VolumeSpace, VolumeSampler, Texel * InverseSpace, 0.0).x + Outside;
+}
+
+@compute @workgroup_size(64)
+fn UniteDistance(@builtin(workgroup_id) Group: vec3u, @builtin(local_invocation_index) Lane: u32)
+{
+    let BrickIndex = Group.x + Group.y * 65535u;
+    if (BrickIndex >= Distance.BrickCount)
+    {
+        return;
+    }
+
+    let Brick = Bricks[BrickIndex];
+    let Level = u32(Brick.w) & 0xFFu;
+    let OccupantCaused = ((u32(Brick.w) >> 8u) & 2u) != 0u;
+    let Clip  = Distance.Clips[Level];
+    let BrickMinimum = vec3f(Brick.xyz * i32(BrickEdge)) * Clip.VoxelExtent;
+    let BrickMaximum = BrickMinimum + vec3f(f32(BrickEdge) * Clip.VoxelExtent);
+    let InverseSpace = 1.0 / vec3f(textureDimensions(VolumeSpace));
+
+    // ① each lane owns a 2×2×2 sub-cube of the brick, seeded with the analytic course plane
+    let LaneVoxel = vec3u(Lane & 3u, (Lane >> 2u) & 3u, Lane >> 4u) * 2u;
+    var Nearest  : array<f32, 8>;
+    var Identity : array<u32, 8>;
+    for (var Sub = 0u; Sub < 8u; Sub++)
+    {
+        let WorldVoxel = Brick.xyz * i32(BrickEdge) + vec3i(LaneVoxel + vec3u(Sub & 1u, (Sub >> 1u) & 1u, Sub >> 2u));
+        Nearest[Sub]  = (f32(WorldVoxel.z) + 0.5) * Clip.VoxelExtent - Distance.GroundHeight;
+        Identity[Sub] = GroundIdentity;
+    }
+
+    // ② pages: cull 64 occupants against the brick grown by the band, stage the survivors, fold them in
+    for (var Page = 0u; Page < Distance.DistanceOccupantCount; Page += PageSize)
+    {
+        if (Lane == 0u)
+        {
+            atomicStore(&PageCount, 0u);
+        }
+        workgroupBarrier();
+        if (Page + Lane < Distance.DistanceOccupantCount)
+        {
+            let Index = DistanceList[Page + Lane];
+            let Minimum = Occupants[Index].WorldMinimum;
+            let Maximum = Occupants[Index].WorldMaximum;
+            if (all(Maximum + vec3f(Clip.Band) >= BrickMinimum) && all(Minimum - vec3f(Clip.Band) <= BrickMaximum))
+            {
+                let Slot = atomicAdd(&PageCount, 1u);
+                PageIdentity[Slot] = Index;
+                PageInverse[Slot]  = Occupants[Index].WorldToLocal;
+                PageVolume[Slot]   = vec4f(Occupants[Index].VolumeMinimum, Occupants[Index].VoxelExtent);
+                PageTexel[Slot]    = vec4f(Occupants[Index].VolumeTexelOrigin, 0.0);
+                PageExtent[Slot]   = vec4f(Occupants[Index].VolumeTexelExtent, 0.0);
+            }
+        }
+        workgroupBarrier();
+        let Count = atomicLoad(&PageCount);
+        for (var Slot = 0u; Slot < Count; Slot++)
+        {
+            for (var Sub = 0u; Sub < 8u; Sub++)
+            {
+                let WorldVoxel = Brick.xyz * i32(BrickEdge) + vec3i(LaneVoxel + vec3u(Sub & 1u, (Sub >> 1u) & 1u, Sub >> 2u));
+                let Sampled = SamplePageDistance(Slot, (vec3f(WorldVoxel) + 0.5) * Clip.VoxelExtent, InverseSpace);
+                if (Sampled < Nearest[Sub])
+                {
+                    Nearest[Sub]  = Sampled;
+                    Identity[Sub] = PageIdentity[Slot];
+                }
+            }
+        }
+        workgroupBarrier();
+    }
+
+    // ③ write the brick into its toroidal texels and stamp its epoch
+    let Resolution = i32(Clip.Resolution);
+    for (var Sub = 0u; Sub < 8u; Sub++)
+    {
+        let WorldVoxel = Brick.xyz * i32(BrickEdge) + vec3i(LaneVoxel + vec3u(Sub & 1u, (Sub >> 1u) & 1u, Sub >> 2u));
+        let Texel = ((WorldVoxel % vec3i(Resolution)) + vec3i(Resolution)) % vec3i(Resolution);
+        WriteClipTexel(Level, Texel, vec4f(clamp(Nearest[Sub], -Clip.Band, Clip.Band), f32(Identity[Sub]), 0.0, 1.0));
+    }
+    if (Lane == 0u)
+    {
+        BrickEpochs[ResolveBrickSlot(Level, Brick.xyz, Distance.BricksPerAxis)] = ConstructBrickEpoch(Distance.FrameIndex, OccupantCaused);
+    }
+}
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/EffectRaster.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/EffectRaster.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0b0dcee
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/EffectRaster.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,382 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                             EFFECTRASTER.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 Derez and rez cubes, drawn into the surface projection like any surface — so they are lit, glow and reflect in the GI.
+
+// 📝 No particle state lives anywhere. Each cube's whole life is a closed-form function of its emitter, its anchor
+//    and the clock: it waits on the surface until its cell's release, launches with the emitter's velocity plus a
+//    burst along the surface normal and a hashed scatter, flies under gravity and linear drag (v' = g − k·v, solved
+//    exactly), and when it meets the floor it shatters into eight children that tumble out and shrink away. A rez
+//    cube flies the other way, from a shell around the emitter onto its anchor, eased and arcing. The vertex program
+//    evaluates that function for the frame's clock (and for the clock a frame ago, for motion vectors); nothing is
+//    simulated, nothing is read back, and an emitter costs one instanced draw while it lasts.
+//
+//    Instance = particle (EmitterIndex · 4096 + index), vertex = 36 corners × (parent + eight children).
+
+//! include "FrameDescriptor.wgsl"
+//! include "PackingCodec.wgsl"
+//! include "EffectRecords.wgsl"
+
+@group(0) @binding(1) var<uniform> Effect             : EffectRecord;
+@group(0) @binding(2) var<storage, read> VehicleCells : array<vec4f>;   // per cell: local anchor (w its facet's family), local normal
+@group(0) @binding(3) var<storage, read> Poses        : array<EffectPose>;
+
+const Gravity      : f32 = 9.81;
+const ChildLife    : f32 = 1.2;    // [s]
+const Shell        : f32 = 2.6;    // [m] rez cubes start this far out
+
+struct EffectVarying
+{
+    @builtin(position) Position             : vec4f,
+    @location(0) Normal                     : vec3f,
+    @location(1) @interpolate(flat) Family  : u32,
+    @location(2) CurrentClip                : vec4f,
+    @location(3) PreviousClip               : vec4f,
+    @location(4) WorldPosition              : vec3f,
+    @location(5) @interpolate(flat) Glow    : f32,
+}
+
+struct CubeState
+{
+    Centre  : vec3f,
+    Size    : f32,     // [m] edge; 0 hides the cube
+    Spin    : vec4f,   // xyz axis, w angle
+    Family  : u32,
+    Glow    : f32,     // [-] emission as a multiple of the family's albedo (face colours)
+}
+
+// 📝 The car's pose at Clock, interpolated between the 60 Hz samples (EffectPose); clamped to the recorded span.
+fn SamplePose(Clock: f32) -> EffectPose
+{
+    let Count = u32(Effect.Colour.z);
+    let Cursor = clamp((Clock - Effect.Colour.w) / EffectPoseSpacing, 0.0, f32(Count - 1u));
+    let Index = min(u32(floor(Cursor)), Count - 2u);
+    let Fraction = clamp(Cursor - f32(Index), 0.0, 1.0);
+    let A = Poses[Index];
+    let B = Poses[Index + 1u];
+    var Pose: EffectPose;
+    Pose.Position = mix(A.Position, B.Position, Fraction);
+    let Aligned = select(B.Rotation, -B.Rotation, dot(A.Rotation, B.Rotation) < 0.0);
+    Pose.Rotation = normalize(mix(A.Rotation, Aligned, Fraction));
+    Pose.Velocity = mix(A.Velocity, B.Velocity, Fraction);
+    Pose.Angular = mix(A.Angular, B.Angular, Fraction);
+    return Pose;
+}
+
+// 📝 The family a cube wears: the facet it was spread on (the car), the cone's band by height (a cone), else the
+//    emitter's own (BodyToWorld[0].w, which the affine transform leaves free).
+fn ResolveFaceFamily(Emitter: EffectEmitter, Kind: u32, Particle: u32, Unit: vec3f) -> u32
+{
+    if (Kind == EffectKindVehicleDerez || Kind == EffectKindVehicleRez)
+    {
+        return u32(VehicleCells[Particle * 2u].w + 0.5);
+    }
+    let Family = u32(Emitter.BodyToWorld[0].w + 0.5);
+    if (Family == ConeOrangeFamily)
+    {
+        if (Unit.z < 0.12) { return ConeBaseFamily; }
+        if (Unit.z > 0.45 && Unit.z < 0.66) { return ConeBandFamily; }
+    }
+    return Family;
+}
+
+fn RotateAxisAngle(Vector: vec3f, Axis: vec3f, Angle: f32) -> vec3f
+{
+    let C = cos(Angle);
+    let S = sin(Angle);
+    return Vector * C + cross(Axis, Vector) * S + Axis * dot(Axis, Vector) * (1.0 - C);
+}
+
+fn HashDirection(Seed: u32) -> vec3f
+{
+    let U = HashEffect(Seed);
+    let V = HashEffect(Seed ^ 0x68E31DA4u);
+    let Z = 2.0 * U - 1.0;
+    let R = sqrt(max(0.0, 1.0 - Z * Z));
+    let Phi = 6.2831853 * V;
+    return vec3f(R * cos(Phi), R * sin(Phi), Z);
+}
+
+// 📐 Linear drag k under gravity: v(τ) = g/k + (v₀ − g/k)·e^(−kτ),  x(τ) = x₀ + (g/k)·τ + (v₀ − g/k)·(1 − e^(−kτ))/k.
+fn Ballistic(Origin: vec3f, Velocity: vec3f, Drag: f32, Time: f32) -> vec3f
+{
+    let Terminal = vec3f(0.0, 0.0, -Gravity) / Drag;
+    return Origin + Terminal * Time + (Velocity - Terminal) * (1.0 - exp(-Drag * Time)) / Drag;
+}
+
+fn BallisticVelocity(Velocity: vec3f, Drag: f32, Time: f32) -> vec3f
+{
+    let Terminal = vec3f(0.0, 0.0, -Gravity) / Drag;
+    return Terminal + (Velocity - Terminal) * exp(-Drag * Time);
+}
+
+// 📝 First time the cube's bottom meets the floor (z = Floor), by bisection on the ballistic height; Limit if never.
+fn ResolveImpact(Origin: vec3f, Velocity: vec3f, Drag: f32, Floor: f32, Limit: f32) -> f32
+{
+    if (Ballistic(Origin, Velocity, Drag, Limit).z > Floor)
+    {
+        return Limit;
+    }
+    // 📝 Height rises then falls, so step to the first sample below the floor, then bisect that bracket.
+    var Low = 0.0;
+    var High = Limit;
+    for (var Step = 1; Step <= 8; Step++)
+    {
+        let Time = Limit * f32(Step) / 8.0;
+        if (Ballistic(Origin, Velocity, Drag, Time).z <= Floor)
+        {
+            High = Time;
+            break;
+        }
+        Low = Time;
+    }
+    for (var Iteration = 0; Iteration < 10; Iteration++)
+    {
+        let Middle = 0.5 * (Low + High);
+        if (Ballistic(Origin, Velocity, Drag, Middle).z <= Floor) { High = Middle; } else { Low = Middle; }
+    }
+    return High;
+}
+
+fn ResolveAnchor(Emitter: EffectEmitter, Kind: u32, Particle: u32, Normal: ptr<function, vec3f>) -> vec3f
+{
+    if (Kind == EffectKindVehicleDerez || Kind == EffectKindVehicleRez)
+    {
+        *Normal = VehicleCells[Particle * 2u + 1u].xyz;
+        return VehicleCells[Particle * 2u].xyz;
+    }
+    // 📝 A box emitter: a 6 × 6 grid on each of its six faces.
+    let Face = min(Particle / 36u, 5u);
+    let Cell = Particle % 36u;
+    let Grid = (vec2f(f32(Cell % 6u), f32(Cell / 6u)) + 0.5) / 6.0 * 2.0 - 1.0;
+    let Axis = Face >> 1u;
+    let Sign = select(-1.0, 1.0, (Face & 1u) == 1u);
+    var Local = vec3f(0.0);
+    var Facing = vec3f(0.0);
+    if (Axis == 0u)      { Local = vec3f(Sign, Grid.x, Grid.y); Facing = vec3f(Sign, 0.0, 0.0); }
+    else if (Axis == 1u) { Local = vec3f(Grid.x, Sign, Grid.y); Facing = vec3f(0.0, Sign, 0.0); }
+    else                 { Local = vec3f(Grid.x, Grid.y, Sign); Facing = vec3f(0.0, 0.0, Sign); }
+    *Normal = Facing;
+    return Emitter.Centre.xyz + Local * Emitter.Extent.xyz;
+}
+
+fn ResolveCube(Emitter: EffectEmitter, Particle: u32, Child: u32, Clock: f32) -> CubeState
+{
+    var Cube: CubeState;
+    Cube.Size = 0.0;
+    Cube.Family = DerezGlowFamily;
+    Cube.Spin = vec4f(0.0, 0.0, 1.0, 0.0);
+    Cube.Glow = 0.0;
+    let Kind = u32(Emitter.Angular.w);
+    let Count = u32(Emitter.Extent.w);
+    if (Particle >= Count)
+    {
+        return Cube;
+    }
+    let Seed = u32(Emitter.Centre.w) ^ (Particle * 9781u);
+    var LocalNormal = vec3f(0.0, 0.0, 1.0);
+    let Anchor = ResolveAnchor(Emitter, Kind, Particle, &LocalNormal);
+    let Vehicle = Kind == EffectKindVehicleDerez || Kind == EffectKindVehicleRez;
+    let Minimum = select(Emitter.Centre.xyz - Emitter.Extent.xyz, Effect.BodyMinimum.xyz, Vehicle);
+    let Maximum = select(Emitter.Centre.xyz + Emitter.Extent.xyz, Effect.BodyMaximum.xyz, Vehicle);
+    let Unit = (Anchor - Minimum) / max(Maximum - Minimum, vec3f(1.0e-3));
+    let Scale = select(0.45, 1.0, Vehicle);
+    var World = (Emitter.BodyToWorld * vec4f(Anchor, 1.0)).xyz;
+    var Normal = normalize((Emitter.BodyToWorld * vec4f(LocalNormal, 0.0)).xyz);
+    let Elapsed = Clock - Emitter.Velocity.w;
+    let Faces = Effect.Colour.x > 0.5;
+    let FaceFamily = ResolveFaceFamily(Emitter, Kind, Particle, Unit);
+    let Debris = Kind == EffectKindDebris;
+    let Size = Effect.Timing.y * select(select(0.75, 0.6, Debris), 1.0, Vehicle) * (0.75 + 0.5 * HashEffect(Seed ^ 0x51u));
+    let SpinAxis = HashDirection(Seed ^ 0x3Au);
+    let SpinRate = 4.0 + 10.0 * HashEffect(Seed ^ 0x7Bu);
+
+    if (Kind == EffectKindVehicleRez || Kind == EffectKindBoxRez)
+    {
+        // 📝 Rez: from the shell onto the anchor, arriving when the cell completes; only the parent flies.
+        if (Child != 0u)
+        {
+            return Cube;
+        }
+        let Arrival = ResolveRezArrival(Unit, u32(Emitter.Centre.w), Effect.Style, Scale);
+        if (Elapsed < 0.0 || Elapsed >= Arrival)
+        {
+            return Cube;
+        }
+        let Centre = (Emitter.BodyToWorld * vec4f(Emitter.Centre.xyz, 1.0)).xyz;
+        let Outward = normalize(normalize(World - Centre) + 0.6 * HashDirection(Seed ^ 0x2Cu) + vec3f(0.0, 0.0, 0.35));
+        let Start = World + Outward * Shell * Scale * (0.7 + 0.6 * HashEffect(Seed ^ 0x1Du));
+        let Progress = clamp(Elapsed / Arrival, 0.0, 1.0);
+        let Eased = 1.0 - pow(1.0 - Progress, 3.0);
+        Cube.Centre = mix(Start, World, Eased) + vec3f(0.0, 0.0, 0.5 * Scale * sin(3.14159265 * Progress));
+        Cube.Size = Size * (0.6 + 0.4 * Progress);
+        Cube.Spin = vec4f(SpinAxis, SpinRate * (Arrival - Elapsed));
+        Cube.Family = select(DerezGlowFamily, DerezHotFamily, Progress > 0.82);
+        if (Effect.Style == 1u)
+        {
+            Cube.Family = select(DerezGlitchFamily, DerezHotFamily, Progress > 0.82);
+            Cube.Centre += 0.06 * (vec3f(HashEffect(Seed ^ u32(Clock * 12.0)), HashEffect(Seed ^ u32(Clock * 12.0) ^ 7u), 0.5) - 0.5);
+        }
+        if (Faces)
+        {
+            // 📝 Assembling: each cube already wears its facet's colour, glowing brighter as it closes on its place.
+            Cube.Family = FaceFamily;
+            Cube.Glow = Effect.Colour.y * (0.35 + 2.0 * smoothstep(0.7, 1.0, Progress));
+        }
+        return Cube;
+    }
+
+    // 📝 Derez: wait for the release, launch, fall, shatter.
+    let Release = select(ResolveDerezRelease(Unit, u32(Emitter.Centre.w), Effect.Style, Scale), 0.04 * HashEffect(Seed ^ 0x13u), Debris);
+    let Flight = Elapsed - Release;
+    let Life = select(Effect.Timing.x * (0.85 + 0.3 * HashEffect(Seed ^ 0x4Eu)), 2.2 + 0.6 * HashEffect(Seed ^ 0x4Eu), Debris);
+    if (Flight < 0.0 || Flight > Life)
+    {
+        return Cube;
+    }
+    let Drag = select(max(Effect.Motion.w, 0.05), 0.5, Debris);
+    let Launch = select(mix(Effect.Motion.y, Effect.Motion.z, HashEffect(Seed ^ 0x65u)), 2.0 + 5.0 * HashEffect(Seed ^ 0x65u), Debris);
+    var Inherited = Emitter.Velocity.xyz + cross(Emitter.Angular.xyz, World - Emitter.BodyToWorld[3].xyz);
+    if (Kind == EffectKindVehicleDerez && Effect.Colour.z >= 2.0)
+    {
+        // 📝 The car kept moving: leave from where it was at this cell's release, at its velocity there.
+        let Pose = SamplePose(Emitter.Velocity.w + Release);
+        World = Pose.Position.xyz + RotateByQuaternion(Pose.Rotation, Anchor);
+        Normal = normalize(RotateByQuaternion(Pose.Rotation, LocalNormal));
+        Inherited = Pose.Velocity.xyz + cross(Pose.Angular.xyz, World - Pose.Position.xyz);
+    }
+    let Velocity = Inherited + Normal * select(Effect.Motion.x, 3.0, Debris) + HashDirection(Seed ^ 0x99u) * Launch + vec3f(0.0, 0.0, 0.6 * Launch);
+    let Floor = 0.5 * Size;
+    let Impact = ResolveImpact(World, Velocity, Drag, Floor, Life);
+    if (Child == 0u)
+    {
+        if (Flight >= Impact)
+        {
+            return Cube;
+        }
+        Cube.Centre = Ballistic(World, Velocity, Drag, Flight);
+        Cube.Size = Size;
+        Cube.Spin = vec4f(SpinAxis, SpinRate * Flight);
+        Cube.Family = select(DerezGlowFamily, DerezHotFamily, Flight < EffectHotSeconds);
+        if (Effect.Style == 1u)
+        {
+            Cube.Family = select(DerezGlitchFamily, DerezGlowFamily, (u32(Clock * 12.0) + Particle) % 3u == 0u);
+            Cube.Centre += 0.06 * (vec3f(HashEffect(Seed ^ u32(Clock * 12.0)), HashEffect(Seed ^ u32(Clock * 12.0) ^ 7u), 0.5) - 0.5);
+        }
+        if (Faces || Debris)
+        {
+            Cube.Family = FaceFamily;
+            Cube.Glow = select(ResolveFaceGlow(Flight, Effect.Colour.y), 0.0, Debris);
+        }
+        return Cube;
+    }
+    // 📝 Children: born at the impact point with the parent's bounce and a corner's direction, ground-clamped.
+    let ChildTime = Flight - Impact;
+    if (Impact >= Life || ChildTime < 0.0 || ChildTime > ChildLife)
+    {
+        return Cube;
+    }
+    let Hit = Ballistic(World, Velocity, Drag, Impact);
+    let Incoming = BallisticVelocity(Velocity, Drag, Impact);
+    let Corner = vec3f(select(-1.0, 1.0, ((Child - 1u) & 1u) != 0u), select(-1.0, 1.0, ((Child - 1u) & 2u) != 0u),
+                       select(-1.0, 1.0, ((Child - 1u) & 4u) != 0u));
+    let Scatter = normalize(Corner + 0.6 * HashDirection(Seed ^ (Child * 131u)));
+    let Bounce = vec3f(Incoming.xy * 0.35, abs(Incoming.z) * 0.25);
+    let ChildVelocity = Bounce + Scatter * (0.8 + 1.0 * HashEffect(Seed ^ (Child * 17u))) + vec3f(0.0, 0.0, 0.9);
+    var Position = Ballistic(Hit + Corner * 0.25 * Size, ChildVelocity, 1.2, ChildTime);
+    let ChildSize = 0.45 * Size * (1.0 - smoothstep(0.65 * ChildLife, ChildLife, ChildTime));
+    Position.z = max(Position.z, 0.5 * ChildSize);
+    Cube.Centre = Position;
+    Cube.Size = ChildSize;
+    Cube.Spin = vec4f(HashDirection(Seed ^ (Child * 29u)), 9.0 * ChildTime);
+    Cube.Family = select(DerezGlowFamily, DerezGlitchFamily, Effect.Style == 1u && (Child & 1u) == 0u);
+    if (Faces || Debris)
+    {
+        // 📝 The shards keep the colour of what they broke from, a last ember of the glow fading as they shrink.
+        Cube.Family = FaceFamily;
+        Cube.Glow = select(0.4 * Effect.Colour.y * exp(-ChildTime / 0.4), 0.0, Debris);
+    }
+    return Cube;
+}
+
+// 📝 The 36 corners of a unit cube (six faces of two triangles, counter-clockwise from outside) and their normals.
+fn ResolveCubeCorner(Corner: u32, Normal: ptr<function, vec3f>) -> vec3f
+{
+    let Face = Corner / 6u;
+    let Index = Corner % 6u;
+    var Square = array<vec2f, 6>(vec2f(-1.0, -1.0), vec2f(1.0, -1.0), vec2f(1.0, 1.0), vec2f(-1.0, -1.0), vec2f(1.0, 1.0), vec2f(-1.0, 1.0));
+    let Q = Square[Index];
+    let Sign = select(-1.0, 1.0, (Face & 1u) == 1u);
+    let Axis = Face >> 1u;
+    var Point = vec3f(0.0);
+    if (Axis == 0u)      { Point = vec3f(Sign, Q.x * Sign, Q.y); *Normal = vec3f(Sign, 0.0, 0.0); }
+    else if (Axis == 1u) { Point = vec3f(-Q.x * Sign, Sign, Q.y); *Normal = vec3f(0.0, Sign, 0.0); }
+    else                 { Point = vec3f(Q.x, Q.y * Sign, Sign); *Normal = vec3f(0.0, 0.0, Sign); }
+    return 0.5 * Point;
+}
+
+fn PlaceCorner(Cube: CubeState, Local: vec3f) -> vec3f
+{
+    return Cube.Centre + RotateAxisAngle(Local * Cube.Size, Cube.Spin.xyz, Cube.Spin.w);
+}
+
+@vertex
+fn EffectVertex(@builtin(vertex_index) VertexIndex: u32, @builtin(instance_index) InstanceIndex: u32) -> EffectVarying
+{
+    let EmitterIndex = min(InstanceIndex / 4096u, 7u);
+    let Particle = InstanceIndex % 4096u;
+    let Emitter = Effect.Emitters[EmitterIndex];
+    let Child = VertexIndex / 36u;
+    var LocalNormal = vec3f(0.0, 0.0, 1.0);
+    let Local = ResolveCubeCorner(VertexIndex % 36u, &LocalNormal);
+    let Now = ResolveCube(Emitter, Particle, Child, Effect.Clock);
+    let Before = ResolveCube(Emitter, Particle, Child, Effect.Clock - Effect.BodyMaximum.w);
+    var Varying: EffectVarying;
+    if (Now.Size <= 0.0)
+    {
+        Varying.Position = vec4f(0.0, 0.0, -2.0, 1.0);   // outside the clip volume: culled
+        return Varying;
+    }
+    let World = PlaceCorner(Now, Local);
+    let Previous = select(World, PlaceCorner(Before, Local), Before.Size > 0.0);
+    Varying.Position      = Frame.ViewProjection * vec4f(World, 1.0);
+    Varying.CurrentClip   = Frame.UnjitteredViewProjection * vec4f(World, 1.0);
+    Varying.PreviousClip  = Frame.PreviousUnjitteredViewProjection * vec4f(Previous, 1.0);
+    Varying.Normal        = RotateAxisAngle(LocalNormal, Now.Spin.xyz, Now.Spin.w);
+    Varying.Family        = Now.Family;
+    Varying.WorldPosition = World;
+    Varying.Glow          = Now.Glow;
+    return Varying;
+}
+
+fn ProjectEffectPixel(Clip: vec4f) -> vec2f
+{
+    let Ndc = Clip.xy / Clip.w;
+    return vec2f(Ndc.x * 0.5 + 0.5, 0.5 - Ndc.y * 0.5) * Frame.ScreenExtent;
+}
+
+// 📝 The cubes are not occupants, so their identity is SkyIdentity (DistanceRecords.wgsl): past the occupant array, where a screen
+//    trace reads no card for them. Declared here because this shader does not include the distance records.
+const EffectIdentity : f32 = 2045.0;
+
+struct EffectTargets
+{
+    @location(0) Attributes : vec4f,
+    @location(1) Motion     : vec2f,
+    @location(2) Identity   : f32,
+}
+
+@fragment
+fn EffectFragment(Varying: EffectVarying) -> EffectTargets
+{
+    var Normal = normalize(Varying.Normal);
+    if (dot(Normal, Frame.CameraPosition - Varying.WorldPosition) < 0.0)
+    {
+        Normal = -Normal;
+    }
+    var Targets: EffectTargets;
+    Targets.Attributes = vec4f(EncodeOctahedral(Normal), f32(Varying.Family), 1.0 + max(Varying.Glow, 0.0));
+    Targets.Motion     = ProjectEffectPixel(Varying.CurrentClip) - ProjectEffectPixel(Varying.PreviousClip);
+    Targets.Identity   = EffectIdentity;
+    return Targets;
+}
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/EffectRecords.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/EffectRecords.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..87d7ee6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/EffectRecords.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,119 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                            EFFECTRECORDS.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 The derez / rez effect as both the surface raster and the effect raster read it: emitters, the vehicle mask, the release clock.
+
+// 📝 One clock decides everything. A point of the car (or of a cone's box) belongs to a cell of a 16³ lattice over its
+//    bounds; the cell's release time is a wave across the bounds plus a hashed jitter. The surface raster discards a
+//    car pixel once its cell is released (glowing white-hot, then cyan, just before), and the effect raster launches
+//    a cube from every anchor of that cell at the same instant — so the car comes apart exactly where the cubes leave
+//    it, with no state shared between the two but this function. Rez runs it backwards: cubes fly in and each cell
+//    of the car appears as its cubes arrive.
+//
+//    Colour: with Colour.x set, every cube is the car — each anchor carries the material family of the facet it was
+//    spread on, so the lime coat comes away as lime cubes, the glass as glass, the tyres as rubber — and glows in
+//    that colour (G-buffer Attributes.w = 1 + glow: the recombination adds albedo × glow as emission). Otherwise the
+//    Particle Editor's palette families (cyan glow, white-hot core, glitch pink) stand in.
+//
+//    Momentum: the car keeps moving while it comes apart, so a cell must leave from where the car is when that cell
+//    lets go. EffectSequence samples the car's pose and velocity at 60 Hz from the derez on (Colour.z samples from
+//    clock Colour.w); a cube launches from the pose at its release time with the car's velocity there (plus the spin
+//    about the centre of mass) — the falling blocks carry on with the car.
+
+struct EffectEmitter
+{
+    BodyToWorld : mat4x4f,   // the emitter's pose when it started (local → world)
+    Velocity    : vec4f,     // xyz [m/s] velocity the cubes inherit, w [s] start on the effect clock
+    Angular     : vec4f,     // xyz [rad/s] spin they inherit, w kind (EffectKind*)
+    Extent      : vec4f,     // xyz [m] half extent of the local bounds, w particle count
+    Centre      : vec4f,     // xyz [m] centre of the local bounds, w seed
+}
+
+struct EffectRecord
+{
+    Clock       : f32,       // [s]  effect clock now
+    MaskMode    : u32,       // [-]  vehicle mask: 0 off, 1 derez, 2 rez, 3 hidden
+    MaskStart   : f32,       // [s]  clock the mask started at
+    Style       : u32,       // [-]  0 cubes, 1 glitch
+    BodyMinimum : vec4f,     // xyz [m] the car's local bounds, w hold offset [s]
+    BodyMaximum : vec4f,     // xyz [m], w frame seconds (motion vectors)
+    Motion      : vec4f,     // x burst [m/s], y slowest launch [m/s], z fastest launch [m/s], w drag [1/s]
+    Timing      : vec4f,     // x cube life [s], y cube size [m], z wave spread [s], w rez flight [s]
+    Colour      : vec4f,     // x face colours (1) or palette (0), y glow strength [-], z pose samples, w first sample's clock [s]
+    Emitters    : array<EffectEmitter, 8>,
+}
+
+// 📝 One sample of the car's motion during a derez (EffectSequence.RecordPose), 60 Hz on the effect clock.
+struct EffectPose
+{
+    Position : vec4f,        // xyz [m] centre of mass, w [s] clock
+    Rotation : vec4f,        // body → world quaternion (x, y, z, w)
+    Velocity : vec4f,        // xyz [m/s]
+    Angular  : vec4f,        // xyz [rad/s]
+}
+
+const EffectPoseSpacing : f32 = 1.0 / 60.0;   // [s]
+
+fn RotateByQuaternion(Rotation: vec4f, Vector: vec3f) -> vec3f
+{
+    let T = 2.0 * cross(Rotation.xyz, Vector);
+    return Vector + Rotation.w * T + cross(Rotation.xyz, T);
+}
+
+fn ResolveFaceGlow(Seconds: f32, Strength: f32) -> f32
+{
+    // 📝 A flash at release, then an afterglow a third of a second long.
+    return Strength * (select(0.0, 2.5, Seconds < EffectHotSeconds) + exp(-max(Seconds, 0.0) / 0.35));
+}
+
+const EffectKindVehicleDerez : u32 = 0u;
+const EffectKindVehicleRez   : u32 = 1u;
+const EffectKindBoxDerez     : u32 = 2u;
+const EffectKindBoxRez       : u32 = 3u;
+const EffectKindDebris       : u32 = 4u;   // a burst tyre's rubber: released at once, thrown hard, never glowing
+const EffectCellsPerAxis     : f32 = 16.0;
+const EffectHotSeconds       : f32 = 0.07;   // [s] white-hot just before release / after arrival
+const EffectGlowSeconds      : f32 = 0.22;   // [s] cyan glow before that
+
+fn HashEffect(Value: u32) -> f32
+{
+    var State = Value * 747796405u + 2891336453u;
+    State = ((State >> ((State >> 28u) + 4u)) ^ State) * 277803737u;
+    State = (State >> 22u) ^ State;
+    return f32(State) / 4294967296.0;
+}
+
+fn HashEffectCell(Cell: vec3u, Seed: u32) -> f32
+{
+    return HashEffect((Cell.x * 73856093u) ^ (Cell.y * 19349663u) ^ (Cell.z * 83492791u) ^ (Seed * 2654435761u));
+}
+
+// 📝 Unit: the point within the emitter's bounds, [0, 1]³. Glitch style uses coarser, uneven 7 × 5 × 7 cells and
+//    rises from the floor; cubes style sweeps the diagonal of 16³ cells.
+fn ResolveEffectCell(Unit: vec3f, Style: u32) -> vec3u
+{
+    let Divisions = select(vec3f(EffectCellsPerAxis), vec3f(7.0, 5.0, 7.0), Style == 1u);
+    return vec3u(clamp(Unit, vec3f(0.0), vec3f(0.9999)) * Divisions);
+}
+
+fn ResolveEffectWave(Unit: vec3f, Style: u32) -> f32
+{
+    let Divisions = select(vec3f(EffectCellsPerAxis), vec3f(7.0, 5.0, 7.0), Style == 1u);
+    let Centre = (vec3f(ResolveEffectCell(Unit, Style)) + 0.5) / Divisions;
+    return select((Centre.x + Centre.y + Centre.z) / 3.0, 0.4 * Centre.z, Style == 1u);
+}
+
+// 📝 Seconds after the derez starts at which this cell lets go. Scale shortens it for small emitters (cones).
+fn ResolveDerezRelease(Unit: vec3f, Seed: u32, Style: u32, Scale: f32) -> f32
+{
+    let Jitter = HashEffectCell(ResolveEffectCell(Unit, Style), Seed);
+    let Spread = select(0.15 * Jitter, 1.0 * Jitter, Style == 1u);
+    return Scale * (Effect.BodyMinimum.w + Effect.Timing.z * (ResolveEffectWave(Unit, Style) + Spread));
+}
+
+// 📝 Seconds after the rez starts at which this cell is complete again.
+fn ResolveRezArrival(Unit: vec3f, Seed: u32, Style: u32, Scale: f32) -> f32
+{
+    let Jitter = HashEffectCell(ResolveEffectCell(Unit, Style), Seed ^ 0x9E3779B9u);
+    return Scale * (0.3 + Effect.Timing.w * (ResolveEffectWave(Unit, Style) + 0.15 * Jitter));
+}
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/FireIllumination.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/FireIllumination.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a3d8527
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/FireIllumination.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                          FIREILLUMINATION.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 A burning tyre as a point light on the scene: inverse-square, windowed to its reach, shadowed through the scene distance field.
+
+// 📝 Read by the direct pass (screen) and the card direct pass (the surface cache), so a tyre fire lights the course
+//    and the car directly and, through the cards the final gather reads, bounces into the indirect term as well.
+//    The shadow ray stops short of the light: the light sits inside the burning wheel, which must not shadow itself.
+
+//! include "FrameDescriptor.wgsl"
+//! include "DistanceTraversal.wgsl"
+
+struct FireArrival
+{
+    Direction   : vec3f,   // [-]  toward the fire
+    Illuminance : vec3f,   // [-]  arriving at normal incidence, shadowed and windowed
+}
+
+fn ResolveFireArrival(Position: vec3f, Normal: vec3f) -> FireArrival
+{
+    var Arrival: FireArrival;
+    Arrival.Direction = vec3f(0.0, 0.0, 1.0);
+    Arrival.Illuminance = vec3f(0.0);
+    if (Frame.FireLightIntensity <= 0.0)
+    {
+        return Arrival;
+    }
+    let Toward = Frame.FireLightPosition - Position;
+    let Squared = dot(Toward, Toward);
+    let Reach = Frame.FireLightReach;
+    if (Squared >= Reach * Reach)
+    {
+        return Arrival;
+    }
+    let Range = sqrt(Squared);
+    Arrival.Direction = Toward / max(Range, 1.0e-4);
+    if (dot(Normal, Arrival.Direction) <= 0.0)
+    {
+        return Arrival;
+    }
+    let Ratio = Squared / (Reach * Reach);
+    let Window = (1.0 - Ratio * Ratio) * (1.0 - Ratio * Ratio);
+    var Visibility = 1.0;
+    if (FeatureEnabled(Frame, FeatureDirectShadow))
+    {
+        let Bias = ResolveSurfaceBias(Position);
+        Visibility = TraverseSceneShadow(Position + Normal * Bias, Arrival.Direction, 0.5 * Bias, max(Range - 0.6, 0.0), 4.0);
+    }
+    Arrival.Illuminance = Frame.FireLightColour * Frame.FireLightIntensity * Window * Visibility / max(Squared, 0.25);
+    return Arrival;
+}
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/ForwardRaster.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/ForwardRaster.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..afd5786
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/ForwardRaster.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,243 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                            FORWARDRASTER.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 A small lit forward pass over the scene's facets: the mirrors' reflected views and the HMI Garage's studio portrait of the car.
+
+// 📝 The main view is deferred and globally illuminated — far too much for three side views and a 640 × 400 preview.
+//    This pass draws the same vertex records (the same instanced runs, the same rigid wheel damage state, steering wheel and
+//    derez mask) with direct light only:
+//
+//    | Mode   | Light                                                                                              |
+//    |--------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
+//    | scene  | the sun through the cascaded shadow depth, the sky view averaged over the normal's hemisphere, a    |
+//    |        | sun-lit ground bounce from below, authored emission — what a mirror shows of the grounds           |
+//    | studio | a key, a fill and a rim light fixed to the camera, a dim ambient, a soft floor glow — the car as a  |
+//    |        | configurator shows it, its own camera and lighting (Docs/CarHmiReport.md)                           |
+//
+//    A mirror's view is the driver's eye reflected in the mirror's plane, through an off-axis frustum fitted to the
+//    glass; its near plane is the mirror itself, so nothing behind the glass leaks into it.
+
+//! include "FrameDescriptor.wgsl"
+//! include "SurfaceReflectance.wgsl"
+//! include "SkyProjection.wgsl"
+//! include "EffectRecords.wgsl"
+//! include "VehicleVisual.wgsl"
+//! include "CabinVolume.wgsl"
+
+struct ForwardView
+{
+    ViewProjection : mat4x4f,
+    Camera         : vec4f,   // xyz [m] eye, w mode: 0 scene, 1 studio
+    Key            : vec4f,   // xyz studio key light direction (toward the light), w its intensity
+    Fill           : vec4f,   // xyz studio fill direction, w intensity
+    Rim            : vec4f,   // xyz studio rim direction, w intensity; scene: x hides the car (derezzed)
+    RippleCentre   : vec4f,   // xyz [m] paint ripple centre (body frame), w [m] current sphere radius
+    RippleNext     : vec4f,   // rgb next finish albedo, w ripple active
+    RippleFinish   : vec4f,   // x roughness, y metalness, z coat weight the sphere carries
+}
+
+struct CascadeReceiver
+{
+    LightViewProjection : array<mat4x4f, 3>,
+    Splits              : vec4f,
+    TexelWorld          : vec4f,
+}
+
+@group(0) @binding(1) var<uniform> View                 : ForwardView;
+@group(0) @binding(2) var<storage, read> Occupants      : array<OccupantRecord>;
+@group(0) @binding(3) var<storage, read> Materials      : array<MaterialRecord>;
+@group(0) @binding(4) var<storage, read> VehicleState   : VehicleRecord;
+@group(0) @binding(5) var<uniform> Effect               : EffectRecord;
+@group(0) @binding(6) var ShadowDepth                   : texture_depth_2d_array;
+@group(0) @binding(7) var ShadowSampler                 : sampler_comparison;
+@group(0) @binding(8) var<uniform> Receiver             : CascadeReceiver;
+@group(0) @binding(9) var SkyView                       : texture_2d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(10) var SkySampler                   : sampler;
+
+struct ForwardVarying
+{
+    @builtin(position) Position             : vec4f,
+    @location(0) Normal                     : vec3f,
+    @location(1) @interpolate(flat) Family  : u32,
+    @location(2) WorldPosition              : vec3f,
+    @location(3) @interpolate(flat) Vehicle : u32,
+    @location(4) BodyLocal                  : vec3f,
+    @location(5) Barycentric : vec3f,
+}
+
+@vertex
+fn ForwardVertex(@location(0) Position: vec3f, @location(1) Family: u32, @location(2) Normal: vec3f,
+                 @location(3) OccupantOffset: u32, @builtin(instance_index) OccupantIndex: u32, @builtin(vertex_index) VertexIndex: u32) -> ForwardVarying
+{
+    let Index = OccupantIndex + OccupantOffset;
+    let Occupant = Occupants[Index];
+    var Moved: DeformedVertex;
+    Moved.Position = Position;
+    Moved.Normal = Normal;
+    if (Index >= 1u && Index < 5u)
+    {
+        Moved = ResolveWheelVertex(Index - 1u, Family, Position, Normal);
+    }
+    else if (Index == 0u)
+    {
+        Moved = DeformBodyVertex(Family, Position, Normal);
+    }
+    let World = Occupant.LocalToWorld * vec4f(Moved.Position, 1.0);
+    var Varying: ForwardVarying;
+    Varying.Position = View.ViewProjection * World;
+    Varying.Normal = (Occupant.LocalToWorld * vec4f(Moved.Normal, 0.0)).xyz;
+    Varying.Family = select(Family, Occupant.MaterialOverride, Occupant.MaterialOverride != NoMaterialOverride);
+    Varying.WorldPosition = World.xyz;
+    Varying.Vehicle = select(0u, 1u, Index < 5u);
+    Varying.Barycentric = vec3f(select(0.0, 1.0, VertexIndex % 3u == 0u), select(0.0, 1.0, VertexIndex % 3u == 1u), select(0.0, 1.0, VertexIndex % 3u == 2u));
+    Varying.BodyLocal = (Occupants[0].WorldToLocal * World).xyz;
+    return Varying;
+}
+
+fn ResolveSunVisibility(Position: vec3f, Normal: vec3f) -> f32
+{
+    let ViewDistance = ResolveViewDepth(Position);
+    let Count = u32(Receiver.Splits.w);
+    if (Count == 0u || ViewDistance < 0.0 || ViewDistance > Receiver.Splits[Count - 1u])
+    {
+        return 1.0;
+    }
+    var Cascade = 0u;
+    while (Cascade + 1u < Count && ViewDistance > Receiver.Splits[Cascade])
+    {
+        Cascade++;
+    }
+    let Offset = Position + Normal * (1.5 * Receiver.TexelWorld[Cascade]);
+    let Clip = Receiver.LightViewProjection[Cascade] * vec4f(Offset, 1.0);
+    let Ndc = Clip.xyz / Clip.w;
+    let Coordinates = vec2f(Ndc.x * 0.5 + 0.5, 0.5 - Ndc.y * 0.5);
+    if (any(Coordinates < vec2f(0.0)) || any(Coordinates > vec2f(1.0)) || Ndc.z > 1.0)
+    {
+        return 1.0;
+    }
+    return textureSampleCompareLevel(ShadowDepth, ShadowSampler, Coordinates, Cascade, Ndc.z);
+}
+
+// 📝 The derez mask as the surface raster applies it: released cells are gone, hidden is all gone.
+fn ClassifyMasked(BodyLocal: vec3f) -> bool
+{
+    if (Effect.MaskMode == 0u)
+    {
+        return false;
+    }
+    if (Effect.MaskMode == 3u)
+    {
+        return true;
+    }
+    let Unit = (BodyLocal - Effect.BodyMinimum.xyz) / max(Effect.BodyMaximum.xyz - Effect.BodyMinimum.xyz, vec3f(1.0e-3));
+    let Elapsed = Effect.Clock - Effect.MaskStart;
+    let Seed = u32(Effect.Emitters[0].Centre.w);
+    if (Effect.MaskMode == 1u)
+    {
+        return Elapsed >= ResolveDerezRelease(Unit, Seed, Effect.Style, 1.0);
+    }
+    return Elapsed < ResolveRezArrival(Unit, Seed, Effect.Style, 1.0);
+}
+
+@fragment
+fn ForwardFragment(Varying: ForwardVarying) -> @location(0) vec4f
+{
+    // Derivatives evaluated uniformly; triangle-list barycentrics give pixel-width edges.
+    let Width = max(fwidth(Varying.Barycentric), vec3f(0.00001));
+    let EdgeDistance = Varying.Barycentric / Width;
+    let Edge = 1.0 - smoothstep(0.6, 1.6, min(min(EdgeDistance.x, EdgeDistance.y), EdgeDistance.z));
+    let Scanning = View.Camera.w > 3.5;
+    let ScanPlane = mix(3.2, -3.2, fract(Frame.ElapsedSeconds * 0.2));
+    if (Scanning && abs(Varying.BodyLocal.x - ScanPlane) < 0.035) { return vec4f(0.5, 0.95, 1.0, 1.0); }
+    if (View.Camera.w > 1.5 && (!Scanning || Varying.BodyLocal.x > ScanPlane)) {
+        if (!Scanning && View.Camera.w > 2.5 && Edge < 0.15) { discard; }
+        // Screen-door transparency avoids sorting and leaves the world materials untouched.
+        if ((Scanning || View.Camera.w < 2.5) && Edge < 0.15 && (u32(Varying.Position.x) + u32(Varying.Position.y)) % 4u != 0u) { discard; }
+        return vec4f(mix(vec3f(0.035, 0.16, 0.2), vec3f(0.35, 0.85, 1.0), Edge), 1.0);
+    }
+    if (Varying.Vehicle == 1u)
+    {
+        // 📝 A mirror never sees mirror glass (each mirror's own lies on its near plane); see-through glazing is gone.
+        if ((Varying.Family == VehicleGlassFamily && VehicleState.Cabin.y > 0.5) || Varying.Family == MirrorGlassFamily)
+        {
+            discard;
+        }
+        if (ClassifyMasked(Varying.BodyLocal))
+        {
+            discard;
+        }
+    }
+    var Surface = ProjectSurfaceSample(Materials[Varying.Family]);
+    // 📝 Paint application, the reference configurator's ripple (Truck.tsx): the next finish takes
+    //    every body point the expanding sphere from the touch point has covered, trailing 0.55 m edge.
+    if (View.RippleNext.w > 0.5 && Varying.Family == PaintCoatFamily)
+    {
+        let Coverage = 1.0 - smoothstep(View.RippleCentre.w - 0.55, View.RippleCentre.w,
+                                        distance(Varying.BodyLocal, View.RippleCentre.xyz));
+        Surface.Albedo    = mix(Surface.Albedo, View.RippleNext.rgb, Coverage);
+        Surface.Roughness = mix(Surface.Roughness, View.RippleFinish.x, Coverage);
+        Surface.Metalness = mix(Surface.Metalness, View.RippleFinish.y, Coverage);
+        Surface.CoatWeight = mix(Surface.CoatWeight, View.RippleFinish.z, Coverage);
+    }
+    let ViewDirection = normalize(View.Camera.xyz - Varying.WorldPosition);
+    var Normal = normalize(Varying.Normal);
+    if (dot(Normal, ViewDirection) < 0.0)
+    {
+        Normal = -Normal;
+    }
+    let TextureKind = u32(round(View.RippleFinish.w));
+    if (Varying.Family == PaintCoatFamily && TextureKind > 0u)
+    {
+        let P = Varying.BodyLocal;
+        if (TextureKind == 1u)
+        {
+            // Carbon twill weave
+            let U = sin((P.x + P.y) * 95.0) * cos((P.x - P.y + P.z) * 95.0);
+            Normal = normalize(Normal + vec3f(U * 0.09, -U * 0.09, U * 0.04));
+            Surface.Roughness = clamp(Surface.Roughness + 0.09 + 0.05 * U, 0.04, 0.95);
+            Surface.Albedo *= 0.86 + 0.14 * abs(U);
+        }
+        else if (TextureKind == 2u)
+        {
+            // Brushed longitudinal alloy grain
+            let Grain = sin(P.y * 220.0 + P.z * 140.0) * 0.5 + sin(P.y * 430.0) * 0.5;
+            Normal = normalize(Normal + vec3f(0.0, Grain * 0.11, Grain * 0.06));
+            Surface.Roughness = clamp(Surface.Roughness + 0.14, 0.06, 0.95);
+            Surface.Metalness = max(Surface.Metalness, 0.85);
+        }
+        else if (TextureKind == 3u)
+        {
+            // Hex ceramic tactile micro-pattern
+            let Hx = sin(P.x * 58.0) * sin((0.5 * P.x + 0.866 * (P.y + P.z)) * 58.0);
+            Normal = normalize(Normal + vec3f(Hx * 0.08, Hx * 0.08, -Hx * 0.05));
+            Surface.Roughness = clamp(Surface.Roughness + 0.20, 0.08, 0.95);
+            Surface.CoatWeight = 0.25;
+        }
+    }
+    let Albedo = ResolveDiffuseAlbedo(Surface);
+    var Radiance = Surface.Emission * Frame.EmissionScale;
+    if (View.Camera.w > 0.5)
+    {
+        // 📝 Studio: three lights fixed to the camera, a dim cool ambient, a warm glow from the floor.
+        Radiance += ResolveDirectReflectance(Surface, Normal, ViewDirection, normalize(View.Key.xyz)) * View.Key.w;
+        Radiance += ResolveDirectReflectance(Surface, Normal, ViewDirection, normalize(View.Fill.xyz)) * View.Fill.w;
+        Radiance += ResolveDirectReflectance(Surface, Normal, ViewDirection, normalize(View.Rim.xyz)) * View.Rim.w;
+        Radiance += Albedo * (vec3f(0.10, 0.12, 0.14) * (0.6 + 0.4 * Normal.z) + vec3f(0.05, 0.045, 0.04) * max(-Normal.z, 0.0));
+        let Reflected = reflect(-ViewDirection, Normal);
+        Radiance += ResolveSpecularColour(Surface) * 0.08 * smoothstep(-0.2, 0.6, Reflected.z) * (1.0 - Surface.Roughness);
+        // 📝 The preview is a picture on a screen (display-referred, 8-bit): a soft shoulder keeps the coat's highlights.
+        return vec4f(Radiance * 1.5 / (vec3f(1.0) + Radiance * 1.5), 1.0);
+    }
+    // 📝 Scene: the sun with its cascaded shadow, the sky over the normal's hemisphere, the ground's bounce.
+    let Visibility = ResolveSunVisibility(Varying.WorldPosition, Normal);
+    Radiance += Frame.SunIlluminance * Visibility * ResolveDirectReflectance(Surface, Normal, ViewDirection, Frame.SunDirection);
+    let SkyDirection = normalize(vec3f(Normal.xy, max(Normal.z, 0.0) + 0.35));
+    let Sky = textureSampleLevel(SkyView, SkySampler, ProjectSkyCoordinates(SkyDirection), 0.0).rgb * Frame.SkyScale + Frame.NightSkyRadiance;
+    let Bounce = Frame.SunIlluminance * (max(Frame.SunDirection.z, 0.0) * 0.18 * InversePi);
+    let Enclosure = select(1.0, mix(1.0, 0.2, ResolveCabinShare(Varying.BodyLocal)), Varying.Vehicle == 1u);
+    Radiance += Albedo * (Sky * (0.55 + 0.45 * Normal.z) + Bounce * (0.5 - 0.5 * Normal.z)) * Enclosure;
+    let Reflected = reflect(-ViewDirection, Normal);
+    let Glossy = textureSampleLevel(SkyView, SkySampler, ProjectSkyCoordinates(normalize(vec3f(Reflected.xy, max(Reflected.z, 0.02)))), 0.0).rgb * Frame.SkyScale;
+    Radiance += ResolveSpecularColour(Surface) * Glossy * (1.0 - Surface.Roughness) * 0.6;
+    return vec4f(Radiance, 1.0);
+}
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/FragmentDistance.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/FragmentDistance.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..fab28fd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/FragmentDistance.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,114 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                          FRAGMENTDISTANCE.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 A fragment's signed distance volume, computed on the device the frame it is born — one workgroup per fragment.
+
+// 📝 A fragment is a closed convex solid, so its distance has a closed form on both sides: inside, the largest face
+//    plane distance (exact for a convex solid); outside, the nearest of its triangles (exact). A 12³ volume
+//    is 1728 voxels against at most 48 triangles — about eighty thousand point-triangle tests, a few microseconds,
+//    so a break that throws forty pieces puts all forty into the scene distance field the same frame.
+
+struct FragmentJob
+{
+    TexelOrigin : vec3u,   // [texel] the pool slot in the occupant distance space
+    Counts      : u32,     // [-]     triangles | planes << 16
+    Minimum     : vec3f,   // [m]     local corner of texel (0, 0, 0)
+    VoxelExtent : f32,     // [m]
+}
+
+@group(0) @binding(0) var<storage, read> Jobs     : array<FragmentJob>;
+@group(0) @binding(1) var<storage, read> Geometry : array<vec4f>;   // per job: MaxTriangles·3 corners, then MaxPlanes planes
+@group(0) @binding(2) var Target                  : texture_storage_3d<rgba16float, write>;
+
+const Edge         : u32 = 12u;
+const MaxTriangles : u32 = 48u;
+const MaxPlanes    : u32 = 40u;
+const Stride       : u32 = MaxTriangles * 3u + MaxPlanes;
+
+var<workgroup> Corners : array<vec3f, 144>;
+var<workgroup> Planes  : array<vec4f, 40>;
+
+// 📐 Ericson, Real-Time Collision Detection §5.1.5: the closest point of triangle ABC to P, by Voronoi region.
+fn MeasureTriangleDistanceSquared(P: vec3f, A: vec3f, B: vec3f, C: vec3f) -> f32
+{
+    let AB = B - A;
+    let AC = C - A;
+    let AP = P - A;
+    let D1 = dot(AB, AP);
+    let D2 = dot(AC, AP);
+    if (D1 <= 0.0 && D2 <= 0.0) { return dot(AP, AP); }
+    let BP = P - B;
+    let D3 = dot(AB, BP);
+    let D4 = dot(AC, BP);
+    if (D3 >= 0.0 && D4 <= D3) { return dot(BP, BP); }
+    let VC = D1 * D4 - D3 * D2;
+    if (VC <= 0.0 && D1 >= 0.0 && D3 <= 0.0)
+    {
+        let V = D1 / (D1 - D3);
+        let Q = P - (A + V * AB);
+        return dot(Q, Q);
+    }
+    let CP = P - C;
+    let D5 = dot(AB, CP);
+    let D6 = dot(AC, CP);
+    if (D6 >= 0.0 && D5 <= D6) { return dot(CP, CP); }
+    let VB = D5 * D2 - D1 * D6;
+    if (VB <= 0.0 && D2 >= 0.0 && D6 <= 0.0)
+    {
+        let W = D2 / (D2 - D6);
+        let Q = P - (A + W * AC);
+        return dot(Q, Q);
+    }
+    let VA = D3 * D6 - D5 * D4;
+    if (VA <= 0.0 && (D4 - D3) >= 0.0 && (D5 - D6) >= 0.0)
+    {
+        let W = (D4 - D3) / ((D4 - D3) + (D5 - D6));
+        let Q = P - (B + W * (C - B));
+        return dot(Q, Q);
+    }
+    let Denominator = 1.0 / (VA + VB + VC);
+    let V = VB * Denominator;
+    let W = VC * Denominator;
+    let Q = P - (A + AB * V + AC * W);
+    return dot(Q, Q);
+}
+
+@compute @workgroup_size(64)
+fn ComputeFragmentDistance(@builtin(workgroup_id) Group: vec3u, @builtin(local_invocation_index) Lane: u32)
+{
+    let Job = Jobs[Group.x];
+    let TriangleCount = min(Job.Counts & 0xFFFFu, MaxTriangles);
+    let PlaneCount = min(Job.Counts >> 16u, MaxPlanes);
+    let Base = Group.x * Stride;
+    for (var Index = Lane; Index < TriangleCount * 3u; Index += 64u)
+    {
+        Corners[Index] = Geometry[Base + Index].xyz;
+    }
+    for (var Index = Lane; Index < PlaneCount; Index += 64u)
+    {
+        Planes[Index] = Geometry[Base + MaxTriangles * 3u + Index];
+    }
+    workgroupBarrier();
+
+    for (var Voxel = Lane; Voxel < Edge * Edge * Edge; Voxel += 64u)
+    {
+        let Cell = vec3u(Voxel % Edge, (Voxel / Edge) % Edge, Voxel / (Edge * Edge));
+        let Point = Job.Minimum + (vec3f(Cell) + 0.5) * Job.VoxelExtent;
+        var Inside = -1.0e9;
+        for (var Index = 0u; Index < PlaneCount; Index++)
+        {
+            Inside = max(Inside, dot(Planes[Index].xyz, Point) - Planes[Index].w);
+        }
+        var Signed = Inside;
+        if (Inside > 0.0)
+        {
+            var Nearest = 1.0e18;
+            for (var Triangle = 0u; Triangle < TriangleCount; Triangle++)
+            {
+                Nearest = min(Nearest, MeasureTriangleDistanceSquared(Point, Corners[Triangle * 3u], Corners[Triangle * 3u + 1u], Corners[Triangle * 3u + 2u]));
+            }
+            Signed = sqrt(Nearest);
+        }
+        textureStore(Target, vec3i(Job.TexelOrigin + Cell), vec4f(Signed, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0));
+    }
+}
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/FrameDescriptor.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/FrameDescriptor.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..55433e8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/FrameDescriptor.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                           FRAMEDESCRIPTOR.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 The frame record at group 0, slot 0 — every program that reads the camera, the light or the toggles includes this.
+
+//! include "SceneRecords.wgsl"
+
+@group(0) @binding(0) var<uniform> Frame : FrameRecord;
+
+// 📝 Reconstructs the world position of a screen pixel centre from reversed depth through the jittered inverse.
+fn ReconstructWorldPosition(Pixel: vec2f, Depth: f32) -> vec3f
+{
+    let Ndc = vec2f(Pixel.x * Frame.InverseScreenExtent.x * 2.0 - 1.0, 1.0 - Pixel.y * Frame.InverseScreenExtent.y * 2.0);
+    let Clip = Frame.InverseViewProjection * vec4f(Ndc, Depth, 1.0);
+    return Clip.xyz / Clip.w;
+}
+
+// 📝 Linear view distance along −Z of a world position; used by the similarity tests of every reprojection.
+fn ResolveViewDepth(Position: vec3f) -> f32
+{
+    return -(Frame.View * vec4f(Position, 1.0)).z;
+}
+
+// 📝 View distance the same world point had in the previous frame: w of its previous unjittered clip position.
+fn ResolvePriorViewDepth(Position: vec3f) -> f32
+{
+    return (Frame.PreviousUnjitteredViewProjection * vec4f(Position, 1.0)).w;
+}
+
+// 📝 A prior guide depth agrees when it matches either where this point was last frame (a static surface under a
+//    moving camera) or where it is now (a surface riding with the camera, such as the chased vehicle).
+fn ClassifyPriorDepth(PriorDepth: f32, ExpectedDepth: f32, ViewDepth: f32) -> bool
+{
+    return abs(PriorDepth - ExpectedDepth) < 0.08 * ExpectedDepth + 0.03 || abs(PriorDepth - ViewDepth) < 0.08 * ViewDepth + 0.03;
+}
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/InspectionMarch.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/InspectionMarch.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5d84a18
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/InspectionMarch.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,139 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                           INSPECTIONMARCH.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 Primary rays through the scene distance field alone — the field, its stride cost, and the cards as the tracers see them.
+
+// 📝 DistanceInspection selects what each camera ray reports:
+//    1  surface normal of the field, tinted by the cascade that answered, with bricks rewritten in the last
+//       half-second glowing — the field updating around the moving vehicle is visible here directly;
+//    2  traversal steps as a heat ramp;
+//    3  card radiance at the hit (Lumen's "surface cache" view): the scene exactly as every indirect ray sees it.
+
+//! include "CardSampling.wgsl"
+//! include "RayTraversal.wgsl"
+
+@group(0) @binding(1) var InspectionTarget : texture_storage_2d<rgba16float, write>;
+
+const CascadeTints : array<vec3f, 5> = array<vec3f, 5>(vec3f(1.0, 0.92, 0.80), vec3f(0.70, 0.90, 1.0),
+                                                      vec3f(0.78, 1.0, 0.72), vec3f(1.0, 0.75, 0.95), vec3f(0.6, 0.6, 0.6));
+
+fn ProjectHeat(Fraction: f32) -> vec3f
+{
+    let t = clamp(Fraction, 0.0, 1.0);
+    return clamp(vec3f(1.5 * t, 1.5 * t - 0.4, 0.6 - 1.2 * t) + vec3f(0.0, 0.0, 0.3 * (1.0 - t)), vec3f(0.0), vec3f(1.0));
+}
+
+fn ResolveHitBrickAge(Hit: TraversalHit) -> vec2f
+{
+    if (Hit.Level >= Distance.ClipCount)
+    {
+        return vec2f(1.0e9, 0.0);
+    }
+    let Voxel = vec3i(floor(Hit.Position / Distance.Clips[Hit.Level].VoxelExtent));
+    let Brick = vec3i(floor(vec3f(Voxel) / f32(BrickEdge)));
+    return ResolveBrickAge(BrickEpochs[ResolveBrickSlot(Hit.Level, Brick, Distance.BricksPerAxis)], Frame.FrameIndex);
+}
+
+@compute @workgroup_size(8, 8)
+fn MarchInspection(@builtin(global_invocation_id) Invocation: vec3u)
+{
+    let Pixel = Invocation.xy;
+    if (any(vec2f(Pixel) >= Frame.ScreenExtent))
+    {
+        return;
+    }
+    let Far = ReconstructWorldPosition(vec2f(Pixel) + 0.5, 1.0e-6);
+    let Direction = normalize(Far - Frame.CameraPosition);
+    var Colour = vec3f(0.0);
+
+    if (FeatureEnabled(Frame, FeatureRayTracing))
+    {
+        let RtHit = TraceSceneRay(Frame.CameraPosition, Direction, 0.01, 600.0);
+        switch (ResolveDistanceInspectionMode(Frame))
+        {
+            case 2u:
+            {
+                Colour = ProjectHeat(f32(RtHit.Steps) / 96.0);
+            }
+            case 3u:
+            {
+                if (RtHit.Hit)
+                {
+                    var Seed = ConstructPixelSeed(Pixel, Frame.FrameIndex, 53u);
+                    let Surf = ProjectSurfaceSample(RayMaterials[RtHit.Family]);
+                    Colour   = Surf.Emission * Frame.EmissionScale
+                             + EvaluateDirectNextEvent(RtHit.Position, RtHit.Normal, -Direction, Surf, &Seed, true, false);
+                }
+                else
+                {
+                    Colour = SampleSkyRadiance(Direction);
+                }
+            }
+            default:
+            {
+                if (RtHit.Hit)
+                {
+                    let Surf  = ProjectSurfaceSample(RayMaterials[RtHit.Family]);
+                    let Shade = 0.35 + 0.65 * max(dot(RtHit.Normal, normalize(vec3f(0.4, 0.3, 0.85))), 0.0);
+                    Colour = mix(Surf.Albedo, RtHit.Normal * 0.5 + 0.5, 0.55) * Shade;
+                    if (RtHit.Identity < arrayLength(&Occupants))
+                    {
+                        let Occ = Occupants[RtHit.Identity];
+                        if ((Occ.Roles & RoleDynamic) != 0u)
+                        {
+                            Colour = mix(Colour, vec3f(0.25, 0.90, 0.70), 0.30);
+                        }
+                    }
+                    let Lattice = fract(RtHit.Position * 2.0);
+                    let Edge = min(min(min(Lattice.x, 1.0 - Lattice.x), min(Lattice.y, 1.0 - Lattice.y)), min(Lattice.z, 1.0 - Lattice.z));
+                    Colour *= mix(0.84, 1.0, smoothstep(0.0, 0.05, Edge));
+                }
+                else
+                {
+                    Colour = mix(vec3f(0.10, 0.11, 0.14), vec3f(0.22, 0.26, 0.34), clamp(Direction.z * 2.0 + 0.5, 0.0, 1.0));
+                }
+            }
+        }
+        textureStore(InspectionTarget, vec2i(Pixel), vec4f(Colour, 1.0));
+        return;
+    }
+
+    let Hit = TraverseSceneDistance(Frame.CameraPosition, Direction, 0.0, 600.0, 0.0);
+    switch (ResolveDistanceInspectionMode(Frame))
+    {
+        case 2u:
+        {
+            Colour = ProjectHeat(f32(Hit.Steps) / f32(MaximumTraversalSteps));
+        }
+        case 3u:
+        {
+            Colour = ResolveTraversalRadiance(Hit, Direction);
+        }
+        default:
+        {
+            if (Hit.Hit)
+            {
+                let Shade = 0.35 + 0.65 * max(dot(Hit.Normal, normalize(vec3f(0.4, 0.3, 0.85))), 0.0);
+                Colour = (Hit.Normal * 0.5 + 0.5) * CascadeTints[min(Hit.Level, 4u)] * Shade;
+                let Age = ResolveHitBrickAge(Hit);
+                if (Age.y > 0.5 && Age.x < 24.0)
+                {
+                    Colour = mix(Colour, vec3f(1.0, 0.15, 0.85), 0.7 * (1.0 - Age.x / 24.0));
+                }
+                else if (Age.x < 6.0)
+                {
+                    Colour = mix(Colour, vec3f(0.2, 0.85, 0.9), 0.3 * (1.0 - Age.x / 6.0));
+                }
+                // 📝 Voxel lattice lines of the answering cascade, so its resolution reads at a glance.
+                let Lattice = fract(Hit.Position / Distance.Clips[min(Hit.Level, Distance.ClipCount - 1u)].VoxelExtent);
+                let Edge = min(min(min(Lattice.x, 1.0 - Lattice.x), min(Lattice.y, 1.0 - Lattice.y)), min(Lattice.z, 1.0 - Lattice.z));
+                Colour *= mix(0.82, 1.0, smoothstep(0.0, 0.06, Edge));
+            }
+            else
+            {
+                Colour = mix(vec3f(0.10, 0.11, 0.14), vec3f(0.22, 0.26, 0.34), clamp(Direction.z * 2.0 + 0.5, 0.0, 1.0));
+            }
+        }
+    }
+    textureStore(InspectionTarget, vec2i(Pixel), vec4f(Colour, 1.0));
+}
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/LightClusterSpace.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/LightClusterSpace.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8f05f5d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/LightClusterSpace.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,240 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                          LIGHTCLUSTERSPACE.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 Light records binned into a world-space grid: each cell's 32-bit mask names the lights whose reach touches it, and each
+//    light's arrival is its beam profile with inverse-square falloff.
+
+// 📝 Includer declares SceneLights as the LightClusterRecords storage buffer (LightClusterSpace.js lays it out).
+
+struct LightRecord
+{
+    PositionType    : vec4f, // xyz = world position, w = light type (0: omni, 1: street lamp, 2: low beam, 3: high beam, 4: fog, 5: flood)
+    DirectionReach  : vec4f, // xyz = forward direction, w = reach radius [m]
+    ColourIntensity : vec4f, // rgb = linear colour, w = intensity
+    Params          : vec4f, // x = inner angle cos, y = outer angle cos, z = profile variant, w = active
+}
+
+// 📝 The photometric atlas: 7 Type C profiles (IES LM-63, Photometry.js) of PhotometryAzimuthBins × PhotometryPolarBins bytes each, peak = 255, four to a u32.
+const PhotometryAzimuthBins      : u32 = 37u;    // 10° steps of C-plane around the optical axis
+const PhotometryPolarBins        : u32 = 91u;    // 2° steps from the axis
+const PhotometryTexelsPerProfile : u32 = 3367u;
+
+// 📝 The emissive region (EmissiveLightSpace.js): emissive triangles per facet set in local space, one record per cluster instance, and per grid cell eight cluster ids.
+struct EmissiveTriangleRecord
+{
+    A  : vec4f,   // xyz local corner A
+    E1 : vec4f,   // xyz edge B − A, w the local area
+    E2 : vec4f,   // xyz edge C − A, w the material family (bitcast u32)
+}
+
+struct EmissiveClusterRecord
+{
+    CentreReach : vec4f,   // xyz world centre, w radius
+    Meta        : vec4u,   // x occupant, y first triangle, z triangle count, w power (bitcast f32; area × luminance, world)
+}
+
+struct LightClusterRecords
+{
+    Minimum   : vec4f,            // xyz world minimum corner of the grid, w = 1 once the photometric atlas is uploaded
+    Extent    : vec4f,            // xyz world size of the grid, w unused
+    Lights    : array<LightRecord, 32>,
+    CellMasks : array<vec4u, 256>, // 16 × 16 × 4 cells, x fastest: bit i of cell c is bit (c & 3) of lane CellMasks[c >> 2]; vec4u keeps the
+                                   // record legal as a UNIFORM too (array strides there are multiples of 16), with the memory of array<u32, 1024>
+    Atlas     : array<vec4u, 1474>, // 7 photometric profiles, one byte per texel (23 569 texels, padded to a vec4u)
+    EmissiveTriangles : array<EmissiveTriangleRecord, 160>,
+    EmissiveClusters  : array<EmissiveClusterRecord, 224>,
+    EmissiveCells     : array<vec4u, 1024>,   // per cell eight u16 cluster ids, the strongest first (0x7FFF empty)
+}
+
+// 📝 Extent.w holds the number of cluster instances in the table, 0 when the emissive structure is off.
+
+const LightClusterResolution : vec3u = vec3u(16u, 16u, 4u);
+
+// 📝 Points outside the grid take every light: the mask is then all ones, so no light is skipped.
+fn ResolveLightCandidates(Position: vec3f) -> u32
+{
+    // 📝 ExtendedLightGrid off: the reference mode, in which every receiver tests every light (inactive lights contribute nothing).
+    if (!ExtendedEnabled(Frame, ExtendedLightGrid))
+    {
+        return 0xFFFFFFFFu;
+    }
+    let Local = (Position - SceneLights.Minimum.xyz) / SceneLights.Extent.xyz;
+    if (any(Local < vec3f(0.0)) || any(Local >= vec3f(1.0)))
+    {
+        return 0xFFFFFFFFu;
+    }
+    let Cell = min(vec3u(Local * vec3f(LightClusterResolution)), LightClusterResolution - vec3u(1u));
+    let Index = Cell.x + LightClusterResolution.x * (Cell.y + LightClusterResolution.y * Cell.z);
+    return SceneLights.CellMasks[Index >> 2u][Index & 3u];
+}
+
+// 📝 Which photometric profile a light follows: its type picks the luminaire (roadway, low beam, high beam, fog beam), the flood type's variant picks flood or spot pods.
+//    0 means none (an omnidirectional point, or a type without a file).
+fn ResolvePhotometricProfile(Light: LightRecord) -> u32
+{
+    let Type = u32(Light.PositionType.w + 0.5);
+    if (Type == 1u) { return 1u; }
+    if (Type == 2u) { return 3u; }
+    if (Type == 3u) { return 4u; }
+    if (Type == 4u) { return 5u; }
+    if (Type == 5u) { return select(6u, 7u, Light.Params.z > 0.5); }
+    return 0u;
+}
+
+fn LoadPhotometricTexel(Profile: u32, Azimuth: u32, Polar: u32) -> f32
+{
+    let Texel = (Profile - 1u) * PhotometryTexelsPerProfile + Azimuth * PhotometryPolarBins + Polar;
+    let Word  = SceneLights.Atlas[Texel >> 4u][(Texel >> 2u) & 3u];
+    return f32((Word >> ((Texel & 3u) * 8u)) & 255u) * (1.0 / 255.0);
+}
+
+// 📝 The profile's relative intensity towards FromFixture (unit, from the light to the point). Type C: the polar angle is measured from the optical axis; C0 is up around it
+//    (world +Z; +X for a fixture that looks straight up or down), C90 to its right. Bilinear reconstruction removes banding at a beam's cutoff.
+fn SamplePhotometry(Light: LightRecord, Profile: u32, FromFixture: vec3f) -> f32
+{
+    let Axis      = normalize(Light.DirectionReach.xyz);
+    let Reference = select(vec3f(0.0, 0.0, 1.0), vec3f(1.0, 0.0, 0.0), abs(Axis.z) > 0.99);
+    let Right     = normalize(cross(Axis, Reference));
+    let Up        = cross(Right, Axis);
+    let Polar     = acos(clamp(dot(FromFixture, Axis), -1.0, 1.0)) * (f32(PhotometryPolarBins - 1u) / 3.141592653589793);
+    var Angle     = atan2(dot(FromFixture, Right), dot(FromFixture, Up));
+    if (Angle < 0.0) { Angle += 6.283185307179586; }
+    let Azimuth = Angle * (f32(PhotometryAzimuthBins - 1u) / 6.283185307179586);
+    let H0 = min(u32(floor(Azimuth)), PhotometryAzimuthBins - 2u);
+    let V0 = min(u32(floor(Polar)), PhotometryPolarBins - 2u);
+    let H  = clamp(Azimuth - f32(H0), 0.0, 1.0);
+    let V  = clamp(Polar - f32(V0), 0.0, 1.0);
+    let A  = mix(LoadPhotometricTexel(Profile, H0, V0), LoadPhotometricTexel(Profile, H0, V0 + 1u), V);
+    let B  = mix(LoadPhotometricTexel(Profile, H0 + 1u, V0), LoadPhotometricTexel(Profile, H0 + 1u, V0 + 1u), V);
+    return mix(A, B, H);
+}
+
+fn EvaluateBeamProfile(Light: LightRecord, TowardPoint: vec3f, Distance: f32) -> f32
+{
+    let Type = u32(Light.PositionType.w + 0.5);
+    if (Type == 0u)
+    {
+        return 1.0; // Omnidirectional point
+    }
+
+    // 📝 Measured (or authored) photometry where the atlas is loaded and the switch is on: the file's shape, bounded by the same cone the analytic beams respect.
+    let Profile = ResolvePhotometricProfile(Light);
+    if (Profile != 0u && SceneLights.Minimum.w > 0.5 && ExtendedEnabled(Frame, ExtendedIesProfiles))
+    {
+        let FromFixture = TowardPoint / max(Distance, 1.0e-4);
+        let Shape = SamplePhotometry(Light, Profile, FromFixture);
+        if (Type == 5u)
+        {
+            return Shape * smoothstep(Light.Params.y, Light.Params.x, dot(FromFixture, normalize(Light.DirectionReach.xyz)));
+        }
+        return Shape;
+    }
+
+    let LDir = TowardPoint / max(Distance, 1.0e-4);
+    let Forward = normalize(Light.DirectionReach.xyz);
+    let CosTheta = dot(LDir, Forward);
+
+    // Type 1: Street Lamp / Roadway Batwing (roadway luminaire, Type II / III spread)
+    if (Type == 1u)
+    {
+        let CosDown = -LDir.z;
+        if (CosDown <= 0.05) { return 0.0; }
+        let Theta = acos(clamp(CosDown, 0.0, 1.0));
+        // Smooth batwing distribution without sharp ring discontinuities
+        let Batwing = sin(Theta * 1.8) * CosDown * 2.2;
+        return max(0.0, Batwing);
+    }
+
+    // Type 2: Automotive Low Beam (Asymmetric sharp cutoff, right-side kick, wide horizontal spread)
+    if (Type == 2u)
+    {
+        if (CosTheta <= 0.08) { return 0.0; }
+        let Right = normalize(cross(Forward, vec3f(0.0, 0.0, 1.0)));
+        let Up = cross(Right, Forward);
+        let LocalY = dot(LDir, Right);
+        let LocalZ = dot(LDir, Up);
+
+        // Asymmetric beam cutoff (ECE / DOT standard: lower on oncoming lane, kicks up towards shoulder)
+        let CutoffZ = -0.02 - 0.04 * max(0.0, LocalY);
+        let TopFade = clamp((CutoffZ + 0.035 - LocalZ) / 0.035, 0.0, 1.0);
+        let HorizAngle = atan2(LocalY, CosTheta);
+        let HorizFade = max(0.0, cos(clamp(HorizAngle * 1.6, -1.57, 1.57)));
+        return TopFade * HorizFade * (CosTheta * CosTheta);
+    }
+
+    // Type 3: Automotive High Beam (Collimated pencil spotlight with soft halo)
+    if (Type == 3u)
+    {
+        if (CosTheta <= 0.15) { return 0.0; }
+        return pow(max(0.0, CosTheta), 14.0);
+    }
+
+    // Type 4: Automotive Fog Light (Wide fan, razor-sharp top cutoff to prevent glare in fog/smoke)
+    if (Type == 4u)
+    {
+        if (CosTheta <= 0.08) { return 0.0; }
+        let Right = normalize(cross(Forward, vec3f(0.0, 0.0, 1.0)));
+        let Up = cross(Right, Forward);
+        let LocalY = dot(LDir, Right);
+        let LocalZ = dot(LDir, Up);
+        if (LocalZ > -0.005) { return 0.0; }
+        let HorizAngle = atan2(LocalY, CosTheta);
+        return max(0.0, cos(clamp(HorizAngle * 1.3, -1.57, 1.57))) * pow(CosTheta, 4.0);
+    }
+
+    // Type 5: Roof Floodlight (Multi-lens LED bar or dual rally pods)
+    if (Type == 5u)
+    {
+        let InnerCos = Light.Params.x;
+        let OuterCos = Light.Params.y;
+        return smoothstep(OuterCos, InnerCos, CosTheta);
+    }
+
+    return 1.0;
+}
+
+// 📐 Inverse-square illuminance with a smooth window at the reach; the cosine of the surface is inside the result.
+fn EvaluateLightArrival(Light: LightRecord, Position: vec3f, Normal: vec3f) -> vec3f
+{
+    if (Light.Params.w < 0.5)
+    {
+        return vec3f(0.0);
+    }
+
+    let LightPos = Light.PositionType.xyz;
+    let Reach = Light.DirectionReach.w;
+    let Toward = LightPos - Position;
+    let D2 = dot(Toward, Toward);
+
+    if (D2 >= Reach * Reach || Reach <= 0.0)
+    {
+        return vec3f(0.0);
+    }
+
+    let Distance = sqrt(D2);
+    let LightDir = Toward / max(Distance, 1.0e-4);
+    let NdotL = max(dot(Normal, LightDir), 0.0);
+
+    if (NdotL <= 0.0)
+    {
+        return vec3f(0.0);
+    }
+
+    // Window function: C2 continuous polynomial smoothly dropping to 0 at Reach
+    let Ratio = D2 / (Reach * Reach);
+    let Window = (1.0 - Ratio * Ratio) * (1.0 - Ratio * Ratio);
+
+    // Beam profile evaluation along the light direction
+    let Profile = EvaluateBeamProfile(Light, -Toward, Distance);
+    if (Profile <= 0.0)
+    {
+        return vec3f(0.0);
+    }
+
+    let Intensity = Light.ColourIntensity.w;
+    let Colour = Light.ColourIntensity.rgb;
+
+    // Standard physical inverse-square falloff with radius margin to avoid singularity
+    let Falloff = Window / max(D2, 0.36);
+    return Colour * (Intensity * Falloff * Profile * NdotL);
+}
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/NearestDepthReduction.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/NearestDepthReduction.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8f2b78f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/NearestDepthReduction.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                        NEARESTDEPTHREDUCTION.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 One level of the nearest-depth pyramid the screen traces walk: each texel keeps the nearest depth of its source tile.
+
+// 📝 Reversed depth stores larger values nearer the eye, so "nearest" is a maximum, and the clear value 0 (nothing
+//    rastered) never wins over a surface. A level-L texel therefore bounds every pixel of its 2^L × 2^L tile from in
+//    front: a ray in front of that value is in front of the whole tile and may cross it in a single step.
+//
+//    Level extents follow max(1, ⌊extent / 2⌋). Where the source extent is odd its last row or column has no partner,
+//    so the final target texel takes three source texels on that axis instead of two — no pixel is ever left unbounded.
+
+@group(0) @binding(0) var LevelSource : texture_2d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(1) var LevelTarget : texture_storage_2d<r32float, write>;
+
+@compute @workgroup_size(8, 8)
+fn ReduceNearestDepth(@builtin(global_invocation_id) Invocation: vec3u)
+{
+    let TargetExtent = vec2i(textureDimensions(LevelTarget));
+    let Pixel = vec2i(Invocation.xy);
+    if (any(Pixel >= TargetExtent))
+    {
+        return;
+    }
+    let SourceExtent = vec2i(textureDimensions(LevelSource));
+    let Unpartnered = ((SourceExtent & vec2i(1)) == vec2i(1)) & (Pixel == TargetExtent - vec2i(1));
+    let Span = vec2i(2) + select(vec2i(0), vec2i(1), Unpartnered);
+    var Nearest = 0.0;
+    for (var Row = 0; Row < Span.y; Row++)
+    {
+        for (var Column = 0; Column < Span.x; Column++)
+        {
+            let Texel = min(Pixel * 2 + vec2i(Column, Row), SourceExtent - vec2i(1));
+            Nearest = max(Nearest, textureLoad(LevelSource, Texel, 0).r);
+        }
+    }
+    textureStore(LevelTarget, Pixel, vec4f(Nearest, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0));
+}
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/NearestDepthTransfer.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/NearestDepthTransfer.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..43f1e78
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/NearestDepthTransfer.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                         NEARESTDEPTHTRANSFER.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 Level 0 of the nearest-depth pyramid: the reversed depth attachment copied into a storable single-channel lattice.
+
+// 📝 A depth attachment can be neither copied into a colour texture nor written as storage, so level 0 is transferred
+//    texel for texel here; NearestDepthReduction.wgsl then builds every coarser level from the one beneath it.
+
+@group(0) @binding(0) var SurfaceDepth : texture_depth_2d;
+@group(0) @binding(1) var LevelTarget  : texture_storage_2d<r32float, write>;
+
+@compute @workgroup_size(8, 8)
+fn TransferNearestDepth(@builtin(global_invocation_id) Invocation: vec3u)
+{
+    let Pixel = vec2i(Invocation.xy);
+    if (any(Pixel >= vec2i(textureDimensions(LevelTarget))))
+    {
+        return;
+    }
+    textureStore(LevelTarget, Pixel, vec4f(textureLoad(SurfaceDepth, Pixel, 0), 0.0, 0.0, 1.0));
+}
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/PackingCodec.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/PackingCodec.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d8f6d42
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/PackingCodec.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                            PACKINGCODEC.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 Octahedral unit-vector encoding and half-precision packing for reservoirs and surface attributes.
+
+// 📐 Octahedral projection (Cigolle et al. 2014): the unit sphere folded onto the [−1, 1]² square.
+fn EncodeOctahedral(Normal: vec3f) -> vec2f
+{
+    let Projected = Normal.xy / (abs(Normal.x) + abs(Normal.y) + abs(Normal.z));
+    if (Normal.z >= 0.0)
+    {
+        return Projected;
+    }
+    let Folded = (1.0 - abs(Projected.yx)) * select(vec2f(-1.0), vec2f(1.0), Projected >= vec2f(0.0));
+    return Folded;
+}
+
+fn DecodeOctahedral(Encoded: vec2f) -> vec3f
+{
+    var Normal = vec3f(Encoded.x, Encoded.y, 1.0 - abs(Encoded.x) - abs(Encoded.y));
+    let Fold = max(-Normal.z, 0.0);
+    Normal.x += select(Fold, -Fold, Normal.x >= 0.0);
+    Normal.y += select(Fold, -Fold, Normal.y >= 0.0);
+    return normalize(Normal);
+}
+
+fn PackOctahedral(Normal: vec3f) -> u32
+{
+    return pack2x16snorm(EncodeOctahedral(Normal));
+}
+
+fn UnpackOctahedral(Packed: u32) -> vec3f
+{
+    return DecodeOctahedral(unpack2x16snorm(Packed));
+}
+
+fn PackHalfTriple(Triple: vec3f, Fourth: f32) -> vec2u
+{
+    return vec2u(pack2x16float(Triple.xy), pack2x16float(vec2f(Triple.z, Fourth)));
+}
+
+fn UnpackHalfTriple(Packed: vec2u) -> vec4f
+{
+    return vec4f(unpack2x16float(Packed.x), unpack2x16float(Packed.y));
+}
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/PlumeAdvection.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/PlumeAdvection.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4c0b128
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/PlumeAdvection.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,277 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                           PLUMEADVECTION.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 Semi-Lagrangian transport of both plume lattices, obstruction by the scene distance field, combustion, sources, decay and coverage.
+
+// 📝 AdvectVelocity (coarse), AdvectThermo (fine) and ResolveSunTransmittance (coarse) share one layout; the host
+//    binds, per step parity,
+//      AdvectVelocity:           1 = velocity state,  2 = thermo state,  4 = next velocity
+//      AdvectThermo:             1 = final velocity,  2 = thermo state,  4 = next thermo
+//      ResolveSunTransmittance:  1 = final velocity,  2 = next thermo,   4 = light
+//    A cell the ONE scene distance field calls solid — the ground plane, a wall, a container, the moving ControlVehicle
+//    — holds no gas, and a velocity cell inside a moving occupant takes that occupant's point velocity, so the car's
+//    body drags and parts the plume. Frontier gathers the same obstruction through a separate intake
+//    (GasSceneDistanceIntake.h); here it is one sample of the field the GI already traces.
+
+//! include "PlumeRecords.wgsl"
+//! include "SceneRecords.wgsl"
+//! include "DistanceTraversal.wgsl"
+
+@group(0) @binding(0) var<uniform> Plume                    : PlumeRecord;
+@group(0) @binding(1) var VelocityState                     : texture_3d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(2) var ThermoState                       : texture_3d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(3) var LatticeSampler                    : sampler;
+@group(0) @binding(4) var LatticeTarget                     : texture_storage_3d<rgba16float, write>;
+@group(0) @binding(5) var<storage, read> Sources            : array<PlumeSource>;
+@group(0) @binding(6) var<storage, read_write> Coverage     : array<atomic<i32>, 8>;
+@group(0) @binding(7) var<storage, read> Occupants          : array<OccupantRecord>;
+
+var<workgroup> CoverageLow  : array<atomic<i32>, 3>;
+var<workgroup> CoverageHigh : array<atomic<i32>, 3>;
+
+//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+//                                                     OBSTRUCTION
+//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+// 📝 Returns (velocity, 1) inside geometry and (0, 0) in open air. A velocity cell is solid once its centre lies inside
+//    a surface, a thermo cell once its centre is a quarter cell inside, so the first layer of gas above the road and
+//    around a tyre survives and a wall still holds no smoke. The velocity reach was a quarter cell outside until the
+//    flame seats moved beside the tyres: at 0.5 m cells the cell beside a sidewall counted as solid, its velocity was
+//    zero, and a fire pooled under the arch instead of rising. The point velocity of a moving occupant is the
+//    displacement of the material point now at Position since the previous frame's transform, over that frame.
+const VelocitySolidReach : f32 = 0.0;     // [cells]
+const ThermoSolidReach   : f32 = -0.25;   // [cells]
+
+// 📝 Sub-grid buoyant rise: a hot thread of gas or a flame tongue rises faster than the coarse lattice resolves, so the
+//    thermo backtrace adds a slip toward +Z that saturates with the cell's heat and flame.
+const SubgridHeatRise  : f32 = 1.4;    // [m/s] at 40 K and above
+const SubgridFlameRise : f32 = 1.1;    // [m/s] at unit flame and above
+
+fn ResolveSolid(Position: vec3f, Edge: f32) -> vec4f
+{
+    let Sampled = SampleSceneDistance(Position);
+    if (Sampled.x >= VelocitySolidReach * Edge)
+    {
+        return vec4f(0.0);
+    }
+    var Velocity = vec3f(0.0);
+    let Level = u32(Sampled.y);
+    if (Level < Distance.ClipCount && Plume.SourceMinimum.w > 0.0)
+    {
+        let Identity = ResolveClipIdentity(Level, Position);
+        if (Identity < arrayLength(&Occupants))
+        {
+            let Occupant = Occupants[Identity];
+            if ((Occupant.Roles & RoleDynamic) != 0u)
+            {
+                let Prior = (Occupant.PreviousLocalToWorld * (Occupant.WorldToLocal * vec4f(Position, 1.0))).xyz;
+                Velocity = (Position - Prior) / Plume.SourceMinimum.w;
+                let Speed = length(Velocity);
+                Velocity = select(Velocity, Velocity * (PlumeSpeedCeiling / Speed), Speed > PlumeSpeedCeiling);
+            }
+        }
+    }
+    return vec4f(Velocity, 1.0);
+}
+
+//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+//                                                  VELOCITY ADVECTION
+//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+@compute @workgroup_size(4, 4, 4)
+fn AdvectVelocity(@builtin(global_invocation_id) Invocation: vec3u)
+{
+    if (any(Invocation >= Plume.VelocityExtent.xyz))
+    {
+        return;
+    }
+    let Edge     = Plume.Lattice.y;
+    let Seconds  = Plume.Lattice.w;
+    let Position = ProjectVelocityWorld(Plume, Invocation);
+    let Texel    = ResolveVelocityTexel(Plume, vec3i(Invocation));
+    let Solid    = ResolveSolid(Position, Edge);
+    if (Solid.w > 0.5)
+    {
+        textureStore(LatticeTarget, Texel, Solid);
+        return;
+    }
+
+    // ① self-advection; a departure point outside the previous window brings the ambient wind
+    let Wind = Plume.Wind.xyz;
+    var Velocity = Wind;
+    if (ClassifyPriorVelocity(Plume, Position))
+    {
+        let Own = textureSampleLevel(VelocityState, LatticeSampler, ProjectVelocityCoordinates(Plume, Position), 0.0).xyz;
+        let Departure = Position - Own * Seconds;
+        if (ClassifyPriorVelocity(Plume, Departure))
+        {
+            Velocity = textureSampleLevel(VelocityState, LatticeSampler, ProjectVelocityCoordinates(Plume, Departure), 0.0).xyz;
+        }
+    }
+
+    // ② viscous relaxation toward the ambient flow, then buoyancy: hot gas rises, particulate sinks. The lift saturates
+    //    with temperature — Frontier's heat scale puts a burning tyre near 75 K, which at 2.4 m/s²/K would fire the
+    //    flame out of its cells at 180 m/s²; flames rise at metres per second, so the lift tends to 8× the coefficient.
+    Velocity = Wind + (Velocity - Wind) * Plume.Retention.w;
+    if (ClassifyPriorThermo(Plume, Position))
+    {
+        let Thermo = textureSampleLevel(ThermoState, LatticeSampler, ProjectThermoCoordinates(Plume, Position), 0.0);
+        let Lift = Plume.Forces.x * Thermo.g / (1.0 + 0.125 * Thermo.g);
+        Velocity.z += (Lift - Plume.Forces.y * (Thermo.r + Thermo.a)) * Seconds;
+    }
+
+    // ③ sources impart their momentum as a relaxation toward the source velocity, so a strong source cannot overshoot
+    if (ClassifySourceBounds(Plume, Position))
+    {
+        for (var Index = 0u; Index < u32(Plume.PriorVelocityOrigin.w); Index++)
+        {
+            let Source = Sources[Index];
+            let Weight = ResolveSourceWeight(Source, Position, Edge);
+            let Push   = 1.0 - exp(-Weight * Seconds * (4.0 + 0.15 * (Source.Rates.x + Source.Rates.w) + 0.05 * Source.Rates.z));
+            Velocity = mix(Velocity, Source.Velocity.xyz, Push);
+        }
+    }
+    let Speed = length(Velocity);
+    Velocity = select(Velocity, Velocity * (PlumeSpeedCeiling / Speed), Speed > PlumeSpeedCeiling);
+    textureStore(LatticeTarget, Texel, vec4f(Velocity, 0.0));
+}
+
+//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+//                                                   THERMO ADVECTION
+//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+// 📝 The coarse velocity plus divergence-free detail below the lattice: the curl of a world-anchored trigonometric
+//    potential, each component omitting its own coordinate (Frontier's SmokeTransport.slang FineVelocity), now in two
+//    octaves and scaled by how much is happening at the point — clean air stays still, a boiling plume churns.
+fn SampleLatticeVelocity(Position: vec3f, Activity: f32) -> vec3f
+{
+    var Velocity = textureSampleLevel(VelocityState, LatticeSampler, ProjectVelocityCoordinates(Plume, Position), 0.0).xyz;
+    let Time = Plume.Wind.w;
+    let Frequency = Plume.Detail.z;
+    let First = Position * Frequency + vec3f(0.43, -0.31, 0.27) * Time;
+    let Second = Position * (Frequency * 2.37) + vec3f(-0.61, 0.53, -0.89) * Time + vec3f(1.7, 4.1, 2.9);
+    let Swirl = vec3f(sin(First.y) - sin(First.z), sin(First.z) - sin(First.x), sin(First.x) - sin(First.y))
+              + 0.45 * vec3f(sin(Second.y) - sin(Second.z), sin(Second.z) - sin(Second.x), sin(Second.x) - sin(Second.y));
+    return Velocity + Plume.Forces.w * (0.3 + 0.7 * Activity) * Swirl;
+}
+
+@compute @workgroup_size(4, 4, 4)
+fn AdvectThermo(@builtin(global_invocation_id) Invocation: vec3u, @builtin(local_invocation_index) Lane: u32)
+{
+    if (Lane < 3u)
+    {
+        atomicStore(&CoverageLow[Lane], 2147483647);
+        atomicStore(&CoverageHigh[Lane], -2147483647);
+    }
+    workgroupBarrier();
+
+    if (all(Invocation < Plume.ThermoExtent.xyz))
+    {
+        let Edge     = Plume.Lattice.x;
+        let Seconds  = Plume.Lattice.w;
+        let Position = ProjectThermoWorld(Plume, Invocation);
+        var Thermo   = vec4f(0.0);
+        if (SampleSceneDistance(Position).x >= ThermoSolidReach * Edge)
+        {
+            // ① second-order (midpoint) backtrace through the final velocity of this step
+            var Activity = 0.0;
+            var Rise = vec2f(0.0);
+            if (ClassifyPriorThermo(Plume, Position))
+            {
+                let Here = textureSampleLevel(ThermoState, LatticeSampler, ProjectThermoCoordinates(Plume, Position), 0.0);
+                Activity = clamp(0.6 * (Here.r + Here.a) + 0.02 * Here.g + Here.b, 0.0, 1.0);
+                Rise = clamp(vec2f(Here.g / 40.0, Here.b), vec2f(0.0), vec2f(1.0));
+            }
+            let Slip      = vec3f(0.0, 0.0, SubgridHeatRise * Rise.x + SubgridFlameRise * Rise.y);
+            let Midpoint  = Position - (SampleLatticeVelocity(Position, Activity) + Slip) * (0.5 * Seconds);
+            let Departure = Position - (SampleLatticeVelocity(Midpoint, Activity) + Slip) * Seconds;
+            if (ClassifyPriorThermo(Plume, Departure))
+            {
+                Thermo = textureSampleLevel(ThermoState, LatticeSampler, ProjectThermoCoordinates(Plume, Departure), 0.0);
+            }
+
+            // ② combustion: a flame cell keeps heating its gas and sheds soot as it burns — a tyre fire's black column
+            let Burning = max(Thermo.b, 0.0) * Seconds;
+            Thermo.g += Burning * Plume.Combustion.y;
+            Thermo.a += Burning * Plume.Combustion.x;
+
+            // ③ per-second losses, converted for this step by the host
+            Thermo = vec4f(Thermo.r * Plume.Retention.x, Thermo.g * Plume.Retention.y, Thermo.b * Plume.Retention.z, Thermo.a * Plume.Combustion.z);
+
+            // ④ sources: smoke, heat, flame and soot per second at each Gaussian centre
+            if (ClassifySourceBounds(Plume, Position))
+            {
+                for (var Index = 0u; Index < u32(Plume.PriorVelocityOrigin.w); Index++)
+                {
+                    let Source = Sources[Index];
+                    Thermo += Source.Rates * (ResolveSourceWeight(Source, Position, Edge) * Seconds);
+                }
+            }
+            Thermo = clamp(Thermo, vec4f(0.0), vec4f(64.0, 4096.0, 16.0, 64.0));
+        }
+        textureStore(LatticeTarget, ResolveThermoTexel(Plume, vec3i(Invocation)), Thermo);
+
+        // ⑤ coverage: the march only enters the box of cells that hold anything visible
+        if (Thermo.r > 0.002 || Thermo.a > 0.002 || Thermo.b > 0.01)
+        {
+            let Local = vec3i(Invocation);
+            for (var Axis = 0u; Axis < 3u; Axis++)
+            {
+                atomicMin(&CoverageLow[Axis], Local[Axis]);
+                atomicMax(&CoverageHigh[Axis], Local[Axis]);
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
+    workgroupBarrier();
+    if (Lane < 3u)
+    {
+        let Low  = atomicLoad(&CoverageLow[Lane]);
+        let High = atomicLoad(&CoverageHigh[Lane]);
+        if (Low <= High)
+        {
+            atomicMin(&Coverage[Lane], Low);
+            atomicMax(&Coverage[4u + Lane], High);
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+//                                                  SUN TRANSMITTANCE
+//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+// 📝 Transmittance through the plume once per coarse cell per step, toward the sun (r) and toward the zenith (g):
+//    eight steps each that lengthen with distance through the new thermo lattice. The march then reads both with one
+//    filtered sample per point — sunlight self-shadowing, and the sky occluded by the smoke above, which is what
+//    darkens the belly of a thick column.
+fn ResolveOpticalDepth(Position: vec3f, Toward: vec3f) -> f32
+{
+    var Depth = 0.0;
+    var Travel = 0.25 * Plume.Lattice.y;
+    for (var Step = 0u; Step < 8u; Step++)
+    {
+        let Length = Plume.Lattice.x * (1.0 + 0.6 * f32(Step));
+        let Sample = Position + Toward * (Travel + 0.5 * Length);
+        if (!ClassifyWindowInterior(Sample, vec3i(2 * Plume.VelocityOrigin.xy, 0), Plume.ThermoExtent.xyz, Plume.Lattice.x, Plume.Lattice.z))
+        {
+            break;
+        }
+        let Thermo = max(textureSampleLevel(ThermoState, LatticeSampler, ProjectThermoCoordinates(Plume, Sample), 0.0), vec4f(0.0));
+        Depth += (Thermo.r * Plume.Optical.x + Thermo.a * Plume.Optical.z) * Length;
+        Travel += Length;
+    }
+    return Depth;
+}
+
+@compute @workgroup_size(4, 4, 4)
+fn ResolveSunTransmittance(@builtin(global_invocation_id) Invocation: vec3u)
+{
+    if (any(Invocation >= Plume.VelocityExtent.xyz))
+    {
+        return;
+    }
+    let Position = ProjectVelocityWorld(Plume, Invocation);
+    let Sun = exp(-ResolveOpticalDepth(Position, Plume.Sun.xyz) * 0.65);
+    let Zenith = exp(-ResolveOpticalDepth(Position, vec3f(0.0, 0.0, 1.0)) * 0.5);
+    textureStore(LatticeTarget, ResolveVelocityTexel(Plume, vec3i(Invocation)), vec4f(Sun, Zenith, 0.0, 1.0));
+}
diff --git a/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/PlumeMarch.wgsl b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/PlumeMarch.wgsl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..26d673d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Experimental/FrontierEngine/Shader/PlumeMarch.wgsl
@@ -0,0 +1,267 @@
+//============================================================================================================================================
+//                                                             PLUMEMARCH.WGSL
+//============================================================================================================================================
+// 🧩 Scattering quadrature of the smoke-and-fire lattice at trace resolution: sun, sky, fire light, flame emission and transmittance.
+
+// 📝 Per resampling pixel, the camera ray is clipped to the coverage box the transport wrote and to the opaque depth,
+//    then marched at about one sample per cell from a per-pixel offset that rotates every frame, so the temporal
+//    antialiasing integrates the quadrature noise away. What each sample receives:
+//
+//    | Term             | How                                                                                       |
+//    |------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
+//    | sun              | cascaded shadow depth × the light lattice's transmittance, in three scattering octaves     |
+//    |                  | (Wrenninge): each octave sees a thinner medium and a rounder phase, so dense smoke glows   |
+//    |                  | through instead of turning grey                                                           |
+//    | sky              | the sky view averaged, occluded by the zenith transmittance — a thick column has a dark   |
+//    |                  | belly — plus a sun-lit ground bounce from below                                           |
+//    | fire light       | the burning tyres and exhaust pops as point lights inside the volume: smoke above a fire  |
+//    |                  | is lit orange from beneath                                                                |
+//    | flame            | blackbody emission at a temperature between tip and core set by the cell's heat,          |
+//    |                  | flickering with the detail noise                                                          |
+//
+//    Optics mix per sample: rubber smoke scatters (albedo ≈ 0.9), soot absorbs (≈ 0.1). Sub-cell detail erodes the
+//    trilinear blobs of the lattice with a tiling noise volume drifting with the wind and the rise of the plume.
+//    The result is premultiplied radiance and transmittance, composited before antialiasing by the recombination.
+
+//! include "FrameDescriptor.wgsl"
+//! include "PlumeRecords.wgsl"
+//! include "SkyProjection.wgsl"
+
+struct CascadeReceiver
+{
+    LightViewProjection : array<mat4x4f, 3>,
+    Splits              : vec4f,   // [m] xyz far distance of each cascade, w cascade count
+    TexelWorld          : vec4f,   // [m] world size of one shadow texel per cascade
+}
+
+@group(0) @binding(1) var<uniform> Plume                : PlumeRecord;
+@group(0) @binding(2) var ThermoState                   : texture_3d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(3) var LatticeSampler                : sampler;
+@group(0) @binding(4) var SurfaceDepth                  : texture_depth_2d;
+@group(0) @binding(5) var<storage, read> Coverage       : array<i32, 8>;
+@group(0) @binding(6) var ShadowDepth                   : texture_depth_2d_array;
+@group(0) @binding(7) var ShadowSampler                 : sampler_comparison;
+@group(0) @binding(8) var<uniform> Receiver             : CascadeReceiver;
+@group(0) @binding(9) var SkyView                       : texture_2d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(10) var SkySampler                   : sampler;
+@group(0) @binding(11) var PlumeTarget                  : texture_storage_2d<rgba16float, write>;
+@group(0) @binding(12) var LightState                   : texture_3d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(13) var<uniform> FireLights          : FireLightRecord;
+@group(0) @binding(14) var DetailState                  : texture_3d<f32>;
+@group(0) @binding(15) var DetailSampler                : sampler;
+
+fn SampleThermo(Position: vec3f) -> vec4f
+{
+    return max(textureSampleLevel(ThermoState, LatticeSampler, ProjectThermoCoordinates(Plume, Position), 0.0), vec4f(0.0));
+}
+
+// 📐 Henyey–Greenstein, normalised over the sphere.
+fn ResolveHenyeyGreenstein(Cosine: f32, Anisotropy: f32) -> f32
+{
+    let Squared = Anisotropy * Anisotropy;
+    return (1.0 - Squared) / (12.56637061436 * pow(max(1.0 + Squared - 2.0 * Anisotropy * Cosine, 1.0e-4), 1.5));
+}
+
+// 📐 Frontier's smoke phase generalised: a forward lobe (g) mixed 72 % with a backward one (−0.65 g), which is what
+//    gives a back-lit plume its silver lining. Frontier's own pair is g = 0.38, backward −0.25.
+fn ResolvePhase(Cosine: f32, Anisotropy: f32) -> f32
+{
+    return mix(ResolveHenyeyGreenstein(Cosine, -0.65 * Anisotropy), ResolveHenyeyGreenstein(Cosine, Anisotropy), 0.72);
+}
+
+// 📝 One hardware-filtered comparison in the cascade that holds the sample; beyond the last cascade the sun is seen.
+fn ResolveSunVisibility(Position: vec3f) -> f32
+{
+    let ViewDistance = ResolveViewDepth(Position);
+    let Count = u32(Receiver.Splits.w);
+    if (Count == 0u || ViewDistance > Receiver.Splits[Count - 1u])
+    {
+        return 1.0;
+    }
+    var Cascade = 0u;
+    while (Cascade + 1u < Count && ViewDistance > Receiver.Splits[Cascade])
+    {
+        Cascade++;
+    }
+    let Clip = Receiver.LightViewProjection[Cascade] * vec4f(Position, 1.0);
+    let Ndc = Clip.xyz / Clip.w;
+    let Coordinates = vec2f(Ndc.x * 0.5 + 0.5, 0.5 - Ndc.y * 0.5);
+    if (any(Coordinates < vec2f(0.0)) || any(Coordinates > vec2f(1.0)) || Ndc.z > 1.0)
+    {
+        return 1.0;
+    }
+    return textureSampleCompareLevel(ShadowDepth, ShadowSampler, Coordinates, Cascade, Ndc.z);
+}
+
+// 📝 Transmittance toward the sun (x) and the zenith (y) through the plume, resolved once per coarse cell by the
+//    transport (PlumeAdvection.wgsl ResolveSunTransmittance) and read here with one filtered sample.
+fn ResolveSelfShadow(Position: vec3f) -> vec2f
+{
+    return clamp(textureSampleLevel(LightState, LatticeSampler, ProjectVelocityCoordinates(Plume, Position), 0.0).xy, vec2f(0.0), vec2f(1.0));
+}
+
+// 📝 Isotropic sky term: the zenith and four horizon directions of the sky view.
+fn ResolveSkyAmbient() -> vec3f
+{
+    var Sky = textureSampleLevel(SkyView, SkySampler, ProjectSkyCoordinates(vec3f(0.0, 0.0, 1.0)), 0.0).rgb * 2.0;
+    for (var Side = 0u; Side < 4u; Side++)
+    {
+        let θ = f32(Side) * 1.5707963;
+        Sky += textureSampleLevel(SkyView, SkySampler, ProjectSkyCoordinates(normalize(vec3f(cos(θ), sin(θ), 0.15))), 0.0).rgb;
+    }
+    return (Sky / 6.0) * Frame.SkyScale + Frame.NightSkyRadiance;
+}
+
+// 📝 The burning tyres and exhaust pops as softened point lights: irradiance over 4π, the phase taken as isotropic.
+fn ResolveFireLight(Position: vec3f) -> vec3f
+{
+    var Light = vec3f(0.0);
+    for (var Index = 0u; Index < min(FireLights.Count.x, 4u); Index++)
+    {
+        let Offset = FireLights.PositionRadius[Index].xyz - Position;
+        let Radius = FireLights.PositionRadius[Index].w;
+        Light += FireLights.Radiance[Index].rgb / (dot(Offset, Offset) + Radius * Radius);
+    }
+    return Light * (0.0795774715 * Plume.Scattering.w);
+}
+
+// 📐 Sub-cell detail: three noise octaves (one per channel) folded into a value around 0.5, drifting downwind and
+//    upward with the plume so the detail reads as motion below the lattice. Erosion takes density away where the
+//    noise is low, more of it where the cell is thin — edges turn to wisps while a dense core keeps its mass.
+fn ResolveDetail(Position: vec3f) -> vec4f
+{
+    let Time = Plume.Wind.w;
+    let Drift = vec3f(-Plume.Wind.x * 0.35, -Plume.Wind.y * 0.35, -0.55) * Time;
+    let Coordinates = (Position + Drift) * Plume.Detail.y;
+    return textureSampleLevel(DetailState, DetailSampler, Coordinates, 0.0);
+}
+
+fn ErodeDensity(Density: f32, Noise: f32) -> f32
+{
+    let Strength = Plume.Detail.x;
+    let Thin = 1.0 - clamp(Density * 0.8, 0.0, 1.0);
+    return max(0.0, Density * (1.0 + Strength * (Noise - 0.5) * 1.6) - Strength * Thin * (1.0 - Noise) * 0.35 * min(Density, 1.0));
+}
+
+@compute @workgroup_size(8, 8)
+fn MarchPlume(@builtin(global_invocation_id) Invocation: vec3u)
+{
+    let TracePixel = vec2i(Invocation.xy);
+    if (any(vec2f(TracePixel) >= Frame.TraceExtent))
+    {
+        return;
+    }
+    let Low  = vec3i(Coverage[0], Coverage[1], Coverage[2]);
+    let High = vec3i(Coverage[4], Coverage[5], Coverage[6]);
+    if (any(Low > High))
+    {
+        textureStore(PlumeTarget, TracePixel, vec4f(0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0));
+        return;
+    }
+
+    // ① the ray, clipped to the coverage box (grown by a cell) and to the opaque surface
+    let Edge = Plume.Lattice.x;
+    let Origin = vec3f(vec2f(2 * Plume.VelocityOrigin.xy) * Edge, Plume.Lattice.z);
+    let BoxMinimum = Origin + (vec3f(Low) - 1.0) * Edge;
+    let BoxMaximum = Origin + (vec3f(High) + 2.0) * Edge;
+    let ScreenPixel = min(TracePixel * i32(Frame.TraceScale), vec2i(Frame.ScreenExtent) - vec2i(1));
+    let Depth = textureLoad(SurfaceDepth, ScreenPixel, 0);
+    let Far = ReconstructWorldPosition(vec2f(ScreenPixel) + 0.5, max(Depth, 1.0e-6));
+    let Toward = Far - Frame.CameraPosition;
+    let Reach = length(Toward);
+    let Direction = Toward / Reach;
+    let Opaque = select(Reach, 1.0e5, Depth <= 0.0);
+    let Inverse = 1.0 / select(Direction, vec3f(1.0e-9), abs(Direction) < vec3f(1.0e-9));
+    let Near = (BoxMinimum - Frame.CameraPosition) * Inverse;
+    let Distant = (BoxMaximum - Frame.CameraPosition) * Inverse;
+    let Enter = max(max(min(Near.x, Distant.x), min(Near.y, Distant.y)), max(min(Near.z, Distant.z), 0.0));
+    let Exit  = min(min(max(Near.x, Distant.x), max(Near.y, Distant.y)), min(max(Near.z, Distant.z), Opaque));
+    if (Exit <= Enter)
+    {
+        textureStore(PlumeTarget, TracePixel, vec4f(0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0));
+        return;
+    }
+
+    // ② about one sample per cell, from an interleaved-gradient offset rotated by the golden ratio each frame
+    let Count = u32(clamp(ceil((Exit - Enter) / (0.9 * Edge)), 4.0, max(Plume.Optical.w, 4.0)));
+    let Step = (Exit - Enter) / f32(Count);
+    let Offset = fract(52.9829189 * fract(0.06711056 * f32(TracePixel.x) + 0.00583715 * f32(TracePixel.y))
+                       + 0.61803398875 * f32(Frame.FrameIndex % 256u));
+    let Cosine = dot(Direction, Frame.SunDirection);
+    let Anisotropy = Plume.Scattering.y;
+    let PhaseOctaves = vec3f(ResolvePhase(Cosine, Anisotropy), ResolvePhase(Cosine, 0.5 * Anisotropy), ResolvePhase(Cosine, 0.25 * Anisotropy));
+    let SkyAmbient = ResolveSkyAmbient() * Plume.Scattering.z;
+    let GroundBounce = Frame.SunIlluminance * (max(Frame.SunDirection.z, 0.0) * 0.12 * InversePi * Plume.Scattering.z);
+    let Cells = Plume.ThermoExtent.w == 1u;
+    let Strength = Plume.Scattering.x;
+    let Flicker = 0.5 + 0.5 * sin(Plume.Wind.w * 23.0);
+
+    var Radiance = vec3f(0.0);
+    var Transmittance = 1.0;
+    for (var Index = 0u; Index < Count; Index++)
+    {
+        if (Transmittance < 0.01)
+        {
+            break;
+        }
+        let Position = Frame.CameraPosition + Direction * (Enter + (f32(Index) + Offset) * Step);
+        var Thermo = SampleThermo(Position);
+        if (Thermo.r < 1.0e-3 && Thermo.a < 1.0e-3 && Thermo.b < 1.0e-3)
+        {
+            continue;
+        }
+        if (Cells)
+        {
+            // 🔍 the lattice itself: smoke cyan, soot violet, heat red, flame yellow, unlit
+            let Absorbed = 1.0 - exp(-(Thermo.r * 1.5 + Thermo.a * 1.5 + Thermo.b) * Step);
+            let Colour = vec3f(0.35, 0.75, 1.0) * min(Thermo.r, 2.0) + vec3f(0.55, 0.3, 0.9) * min(Thermo.a, 2.0)
+                       + vec3f(1.0, 0.25, 0.05) * min(Thermo.g * 0.02, 2.0) + vec3f(1.0, 0.85, 0.2) * min(Thermo.b, 2.0);
+            Radiance += Transmittance * Colour * Absorbed * 4.0;
+            Transmittance *= 1.0 - Absorbed;
+            continue;
+        }
+
+        // ③ sub-cell detail on both particulates; the flame flickers with the noise's fourth channel
+        if (Plume.Detail.x > 0.0)
+        {
+            let Noise = ResolveDetail(Position);
+            let Folded = dot(Noise.rgb, vec3f(0.5, 0.3, 0.2));
+            Thermo.r = ErodeDensity(Thermo.r, Folded);
+            Thermo.a = ErodeDensity(Thermo.a, Folded);
+            Thermo.b *= mix(1.0, 0.45 + 1.1 * mix(Noise.a, Flicker, 0.25), min(Plume.Detail.x, 1.0));
+        }
+
+        // ④ optics of the mixture
+        let SmokeExtinction = Thermo.r * Plume.Optical.x;
+        let SootExtinction = Thermo.a * Plume.Optical.z;
+        let Particulate = SmokeExtinction + SootExtinction;
+        let Extinction = Particulate + Thermo.b * 0.8;
+        if (Extinction < 1.0e-4)
+        {
+            continue;
+        }
+        let Absorbed = 1.0 - exp(-Extinction * Step);
+        let Albedo = (SmokeExtinction * Plume.Optical.y + SootExtinction * Plume.Sun.w) / max(Particulate, 1.0e-5);
+        let Share = Particulate / Extinction;
+
+        // ⑤ sun in three octaves, sky occluded from above, fire light from within
+        let Shadow = ResolveSelfShadow(Position);
+        let Visibility = ResolveSunVisibility(Position);
+        // 📝 Each further octave is light that scattered again inside the medium, so it is weighted by the albedo once
+        //    more: white rubber smoke glows through, soot — which absorbs at every event — keeps only its single bounce.
+        let Octaves = PhaseOctaves.x * Shadow.x + Strength * Albedo * (0.6 * PhaseOctaves.y * pow(Shadow.x, 0.25)
+                                                                       + 0.36 * PhaseOctaves.z * pow(Shadow.x, 0.0625));
+        let Sunlight = Frame.SunIlluminance * (Visibility * Octaves);
+        let Sky = SkyAmbient * (0.18 + 0.82 * pow(Shadow.y, 0.6)) + GroundBounce;
+        let Scattered = (Sunlight + Sky + ResolveFireLight(Position)) * (Albedo * Share * Absorbed);
+
+        // ⑥ flame: blackbody between tip and core, brighter where the gas is hotter
+        let Heat = Thermo.g / (Thermo.g + Plume.Flame.z);
+        let Temperature = mix(Plume.Flame.y, Plume.Flame.x, Heat);
+        let Emission = ResolveBlackbodyRadiance(Temperature) * (Plume.SourceMaximum.w * min(Thermo.b, 1.5) * Step);
+
+        Radiance += Transmittance * (Scattered + Emission);
+        Transmittance *= 1.0 - Absorbed;
+    }
+    textureStore(PlumeTarget, TracePixel, vec4f(Radiance, Transmittance));
+}
